INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00001', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 0, 'What were the key federal features that India''s Constitution borrowed from the Government of India Act, 1935?', 'The **Government of India Act, 1935** is the single largest source of borrowing for the Indian Constitution, contributing roughly half of its provisions in substance.

Key elements borrowed include the **federal scheme** with division of powers between the Centre and provinces, the **office of Governor**, the **judiciary** structure, **public service commissions**, and the system of **emergency powers**.

The Act had itself proposed an all-India federation that never came into force, but its administrative framework was retained almost intact after independence.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00002', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 1, 'What was "dyarchy" and which Act introduced it in the provinces?', '**Dyarchy** (dual government) was introduced in the provinces by the **Government of India Act, 1919** (Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms).

It divided provincial subjects into **"reserved"** subjects (controlled by the Governor and executive council, e.g. police, finance) and **"transferred"** subjects (administered by ministers responsible to the legislature, e.g. education, health).

The scheme was criticised for giving ministers responsibility without real power, and it was replaced by **provincial autonomy** under the Government of India Act, 1935.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00003', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 2, 'Which plan led to the formation of the Constituent Assembly of India, and when did it first meet?', 'The **Constituent Assembly** was formed under the **Cabinet Mission Plan of 1946**.

Members were indirectly elected by the **provincial legislative assemblies**, with each province allotted seats roughly in proportion to its population.

The Assembly held its **first meeting on 9 December 1946**, with **Dr. Sachchidananda Sinha** as the temporary chairman; **Dr. Rajendra Prasad** was later elected as its permanent President.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00004', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 3, 'What was the significance of the "Objectives Resolution" moved by Jawaharlal Nehru in the Constituent Assembly?', 'The **Objectives Resolution**, moved by **Jawaharlal Nehru on 13 December 1946**, laid down the fundamental philosophy and underlying values of the Constitution.

It declared India to be an **independent sovereign republic**, guaranteed **justice, equality, and freedom** to all citizens, and promised adequate safeguards for minorities and backward communities.

This resolution, adopted on 22 January 1947, eventually formed the basis of the **Preamble** to the Constitution.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00005', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 4, 'Who chaired the Drafting Committee of the Constituent Assembly?', 'The **Drafting Committee** was chaired by **Dr. B.R. Ambedkar**, who is widely regarded as the chief architect of the Indian Constitution.

The committee was constituted on **29 August 1947** and had seven members tasked with preparing a draft constitution based on decisions already taken by the Constituent Assembly.

The final draft was submitted and the Constitution was **adopted on 26 November 1949**, coming into force on **26 January 1950**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00006', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 5, 'Which words were added to the Preamble by the 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976?', 'The **42nd Amendment Act, 1976** inserted three words into the Preamble: **"Socialist," "Secular,"** and **"Integrity"** (the last added to "unity of the Nation" to make it "unity and integrity of the Nation").

This amendment, passed during the **Emergency**, is also known for several other sweeping changes and is sometimes called a **"Mini-Constitution."**

The Preamble itself has been amended only once, through this Act.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00007', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 6, 'Is the Preamble a part of the Constitution of India, and is it amendable?', 'In the **Kesavananda Bharati case (1973)**, the Supreme Court held that the **Preamble is part of the Constitution**, reversing its earlier view in the Berubari Union case (1960).

The Court also held that the Preamble can be **amended under Article 368**, but only to the extent that the amendment does not alter the **"basic structure"** of the Constitution.

This was demonstrated when the 42nd Amendment itself modified the Preamble''s wording in 1976.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00008', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 7, 'What does Article 14 of the Constitution guarantee?', '**Article 14** guarantees **"equality before law"** and **"equal protection of the laws"** to all persons within the territory of India.

"Equality before law" is a negative concept borrowed from Britain, implying the absence of special privileges, while "equal protection of laws" is a positive concept borrowed from the USA, implying equal treatment under equal circumstances.

The Article permits **reasonable classification** based on intelligible differentia having a rational nexus with the object sought to be achieved.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00009', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 8, 'What does Article 15 of the Constitution prohibit, and what exceptions does it carry?', '**Article 15** prohibits the State from discriminating against any citizen on grounds only of **religion, race, caste, sex, or place of birth**.

It carries important exceptions that allow the State to make **special provisions for women and children**, and for the advancement of **socially and educationally backward classes**, Scheduled Castes, and Scheduled Tribes.

The **103rd Amendment Act, 2019** added Article 15(6), enabling **reservation for the Economically Weaker Sections (EWS)** up to 10%.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00010', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 9, 'What does Article 16 of the Constitution deal with?', '**Article 16** guarantees **equality of opportunity** in matters of public employment under the State.

It permits the State to reserve posts in public employment for **backward classes** that are not adequately represented, and allows reservation in **promotions for SCs/STs** under certain conditions (Article 16(4A)).

It also allowed EWS reservation of up to 10% in public employment, inserted by the **103rd Amendment Act, 2019**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00011', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 10, 'Name the fundamental freedoms originally guaranteed under Article 19 of the Constitution.', 'Article 19(1) originally guaranteed seven freedoms, now reduced to six after the deletion of the right to property by the 44th Amendment.

- Freedom of **speech and expression**
- Freedom to **assemble peaceably and without arms**
- Freedom to **form associations or unions**
- Freedom to **move freely** throughout India
- Freedom to **reside and settle** in any part of India
- Freedom to **practise any profession, or to carry on any occupation, trade or business**

All these freedoms are subject to **reasonable restrictions** that the State may impose on grounds such as sovereignty, public order, decency, or morality.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00012', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 11, 'How did the Maneka Gandhi vs Union of India (1978) case expand the scope of Article 21?', 'In **Maneka Gandhi vs Union of India (1978)**, the Supreme Court held that the **"procedure established by law"** under Article 21 must be **fair, just, and reasonable**, not arbitrary.

This overturned the narrow interpretation given earlier in **A.K. Gopalan''s case (1950)**, which had treated Article 21 and Article 19 as mutually exclusive.

The judgment effectively read elements of **due process** into Article 21 and established that Articles 14, 19, and 21 are interlinked, vastly widening the scope of the **right to life and personal liberty**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00013', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 12, 'Which amendment inserted Article 21A, and what does it guarantee?', 'The **86th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2002** inserted **Article 21A**, making the **right to free and compulsory education** a Fundamental Right for children aged **six to fourteen years**.

This right is operationalised through the **Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education (RTE) Act, 2009**.

Article 21A converted what was earlier a Directive Principle (Article 45) into an enforceable Fundamental Right.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00014', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 13, 'What do Articles 23 and 24 protect under the Right against Exploitation?', '**Article 23** prohibits **traffic in human beings, begar (forced labour), and other similar forms of forced labour**, making violation a punishable offence.

**Article 24** prohibits the employment of children below the age of **14 years** in any factory, mine, or other hazardous employment.

These rights are available against both the State and private individuals, unlike most other Fundamental Rights, which operate mainly against the State.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00015', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 14, 'What is covered under the Right to Freedom of Religion (Articles 25-28)?', '**Article 25** guarantees freedom of **conscience and the right to freely profess, practise, and propagate religion**, subject to public order, morality, and health.

**Article 26** gives every religious denomination the right to **manage its own affairs** in matters of religion and to own and administer property.

**Articles 27 and 28** deal respectively with freedom from **paying taxes for promotion of a religion** and freedom from **religious instruction in wholly State-funded educational institutions**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00016', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 15, 'What cultural and educational rights do Articles 29 and 30 provide to minorities?', '**Article 29** protects the right of any section of citizens with a distinct **language, script, or culture** to conserve the same.

**Article 30** grants all **minorities (religious or linguistic)** the right to **establish and administer educational institutions** of their choice.

These provisions aim to protect the interests of minorities while ensuring they are not discriminated against in admission to State-aided educational institutions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00017', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 16, 'Why did Dr. B.R. Ambedkar call Article 32 the "heart and soul" of the Constitution?', '**Article 32** guarantees the **right to constitutional remedies**, empowering citizens to move the **Supreme Court directly** for the enforcement of their Fundamental Rights.

Dr. Ambedkar called it the **"heart and soul"** of the Constitution because without an effective remedy, Fundamental Rights would be meaningless.

The Article empowers the Supreme Court to issue **writs** for this purpose; a parallel power is given to High Courts under **Article 226**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00018', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 17, 'Explain the five types of writs that courts in India can issue.', 'The Constitution empowers the Supreme Court (Article 32) and High Courts (Article 226) to issue five types of writs.

- **Habeas Corpus** ("to have the body") — to produce a detained person before the court and check the legality of detention
- **Mandamus** ("we command") — directing a public authority to perform a duty it has failed to perform
- **Prohibition** — issued by a higher court to a lower court or tribunal to stop it from exceeding its jurisdiction
- **Certiorari** — to quash an order already passed by a lower court or tribunal that exceeded its jurisdiction
- **Quo Warranto** — questioning the legality of a person''s claim to a public office', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00019', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 18, 'What is the nature of the Directive Principles of State Policy, and where are they located?', 'The **Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP)** are contained in **Part IV (Articles 36-51)** of the Constitution, inspired by the Irish Constitution.

They are **non-justiciable**, meaning courts cannot enforce them, but **Article 37** declares them **"fundamental in the governance of the country,"** obliging the State to apply them in making laws.

The **42nd Amendment** inserted Article 31C, giving certain DPSPs (Articles 39(b) and (c)) precedence over Articles 14 and 19 in case of conflict, subject to the basic structure doctrine.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00020', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 19, 'What are the three broad categories into which the Directive Principles are classified?', 'Scholars broadly classify the Directive Principles into three categories.

- **Gandhian principles** — reflecting Gandhian ideology, such as organisation of village panchayats (Art. 40) and promotion of cottage industries (Art. 43)
- **Socialist principles** — reflecting the ideology of socialism, such as securing a living wage for workers (Art. 43) and equal pay for equal work (Art. 39(d))
- **Liberal-intellectual principles** — reflecting liberalism, such as a Uniform Civil Code (Art. 44) and separation of judiciary from executive (Art. 50)', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00021', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 20, 'What does Article 44 of the Constitution deal with?', '**Article 44**, a Directive Principle, directs the State to **"endeavour to secure for the citizens a Uniform Civil Code"** throughout the territory of India.

The aim is to replace personal laws based on religion with a **common set of laws** governing marriage, divorce, inheritance, and adoption for all citizens.

**Goa** is often cited as the only Indian state with a form of uniform civil code (the Portuguese Civil Code, 1867), and **Uttarakhand** became the first state after independence to enact a UCC, in 2024.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00022', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 21, 'Which amendment added the Fundamental Duties, and on whose recommendation?', 'The **42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976** added **Part IV-A (Article 51A)**, listing the **Fundamental Duties** of citizens, based on the recommendations of the **Swaran Singh Committee**.

Originally **ten** duties were listed; the **86th Amendment Act, 2002** added an eleventh duty — requiring parents or guardians to provide **educational opportunities to children aged six to fourteen years**.

Unlike Fundamental Rights, the Fundamental Duties are **non-justiciable** and have no direct legal sanction for their enforcement.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00023', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 22, 'What are the qualifications required to become the President of India?', 'To be eligible for election as **President**, a person must be a **citizen of India**, at least **35 years of age**, and qualified for election as a member of the **Lok Sabha**.

The person must not hold any **office of profit** under the Government of India, a State Government, or any local authority.

The President''s election is conducted in accordance with **Article 58** and the Presidential and Vice-Presidential Elections Act, 1952.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00024', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 23, 'Describe the system used to elect the President of India.', 'The President is elected by an **Electoral College** consisting of the **elected members of both Houses of Parliament** and the **elected members of the Legislative Assemblies** of States and the UTs of Delhi and Puducherry.

The election follows the system of **proportional representation by means of the single transferable vote**, with voting by **secret ballot**.

The value of votes of MLAs and MPs is calculated so as to give **parity between the states as a whole and the Union**, ensuring uniformity in the scale of representation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00025', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 24, 'What is the pardoning power of the President under Article 72?', '**Article 72** empowers the President to grant **pardons, reprieves, respites, or remissions of punishment**, or to suspend, remit, or commute a sentence.

This power extends to cases involving punishment by a **court martial**, offences against **Union laws**, and sentences of **death**.

A similar but narrower power is available to the **Governor** under Article 161, which does not extend to death sentences in the same unconditional manner nor to court-martial cases.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00026', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 25, 'What is the ex officio role of the Vice President of India?', 'The **Vice President** of India serves as the **ex officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha** under Article 64.

The Vice President is elected by members of an **Electoral College** consisting of members of **both Houses of Parliament**, through proportional representation by single transferable vote.

The Vice President also acts as **President** when a vacancy arises due to the President''s death, resignation, removal, or inability to act, until a new President is elected.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00027', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 26, 'What does Article 75 say about the collective responsibility of the Council of Ministers?', '**Article 75(3)** states that the **Council of Ministers shall be collectively responsible to the House of the People (Lok Sabha)**.

This means the Council of Ministers acts as a team, and if the Lok Sabha passes a **no-confidence motion** against the government, all ministers (including those from the Rajya Sabha) must resign.

The principle of collective responsibility is the bedrock of India''s **parliamentary form of government**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00028', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 27, 'What is the maximum strength prescribed for the Lok Sabha, and what is its present composition?', 'The Constitution originally fixed the **maximum strength of the Lok Sabha at 552** — up to 530 members from states, up to 20 from Union Territories, and (until the 104th Amendment) 2 nominated Anglo-Indian members.

The **104th Amendment Act, 2019** ended the provision for nominating Anglo-Indian members with effect from January 2020.

The current strength of the Lok Sabha is **543 elected seats**, with the total number of seats **frozen at the pre-2001 level until the first census after 2026**, as per the 42nd and 84th Amendments, pending a fresh delimitation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00029', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 28, 'How is the Rajya Sabha composed, and what is unique about its 12 nominated members?', 'The **Rajya Sabha** (Council of States) has a maximum strength of **250 members** — up to 238 representatives of States and UTs, and **12 members nominated by the President**.

Nominated members are persons having **special knowledge or practical experience in literature, science, art, and social service**, as provided under Article 80.

Unlike the Lok Sabha, the Rajya Sabha is a **permanent body** not subject to dissolution, with one-third of its members retiring every two years.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00030', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 29, 'How is a Money Bill certified, and what role does the Speaker play?', 'A **Money Bill**, as defined under **Article 110**, deals exclusively with matters such as taxation, borrowing by government, or the Consolidated Fund of India.

A Money Bill can **only be introduced in the Lok Sabha**, and crucially, the **Speaker of the Lok Sabha''s decision on whether a bill is a Money Bill is final** and cannot be questioned in any court or in either House of Parliament.

The Rajya Sabha can only make **recommendations** on a Money Bill, which the Lok Sabha may accept or reject, and must return the bill within **14 days**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00031', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 30, 'How does a Financial Bill differ from a Money Bill?', 'A **Financial Bill** is broader than a Money Bill — it contains some matters listed in Article 110 along with other general legislative provisions, whereas a Money Bill deals **exclusively** with those matters.

A Financial Bill (Category I, Article 117(1)) can only be introduced in the **Lok Sabha** on the President''s recommendation, but unlike a Money Bill, it can be **amended or rejected by the Rajya Sabha** like an ordinary bill.

A Financial Bill (Category II, Article 117(3)) involves expenditure from the Consolidated Fund but has no other special feature and can be introduced in **either House**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00032', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 31, 'What are the functions of the Public Accounts Committee (PAC)?', 'The **Public Accounts Committee (PAC)** examines the **annual audit reports of the Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG)**, which point out irregularities and losses in government spending.

It scrutinises whether money granted by Parliament was spent **"within the scope of the demand"** and for the purposes for which it was sanctioned.

The PAC has **22 members** (15 from Lok Sabha, 7 from Rajya Sabha); since 1967, by convention, its Chairman is a member of the **principal opposition party**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00033', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 32, 'What is the Anti-Defection Law, and which Schedule contains it?', 'The **Anti-Defection Law** was introduced by the **52nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1985**, which inserted the **Tenth Schedule** to the Constitution.

It provides for the **disqualification of members** of Parliament or State Legislatures on grounds of defection — if a member voluntarily gives up party membership or votes/abstains contrary to a party whip without prior permission.

The **91st Amendment Act, 2003** removed the earlier exception that protected a group of defectors constituting one-third of a party, retaining only the exception for a genuine **merger** involving two-thirds of party members.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00034', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 33, 'Distinguish between "Zero Hour" and "Question Hour" in Indian parliamentary practice.', '**Question Hour**, usually the first hour of a sitting, is devoted to questions that members ask of ministers regarding the working of their departments; it is mentioned in the **Rules of Procedure**.

**Zero Hour**, by contrast, is an **Indian innovation** and is not mentioned in the Rules of Procedure — it starts immediately after Question Hour, around noon, and allows members to raise urgent matters without prior notice.

Zero Hour has no fixed duration and depends entirely on how long the House allows such discussions to continue before moving to the listed agenda.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00035', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 34, 'Distinguish between a "No-Confidence Motion" and a "Censure Motion" in the Lok Sabha.', 'A **No-Confidence Motion** can be moved only against the **Council of Ministers as a whole**, and if passed, the entire government must resign.

A **Censure Motion** may be moved against the **Council of Ministers or an individual minister**, and must state specific reasons; if passed, the government is not bound to resign, though a Prime Minister may choose to seek a confidence vote.

Both motions can be moved only in the **Lok Sabha**, requiring the support of at least **50 members** to be admitted for discussion.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00036', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 35, 'On what constitutional basis does the Supreme Court of India exercise judicial review?', '**Judicial review** is the power of courts to examine the **constitutionality of legislative and executive actions** and strike them down if they violate the Constitution.

Though not explicitly named, judicial review is implied by several Articles — notably **Article 13** (laws inconsistent with Fundamental Rights are void), **Article 32**, **Article 226**, and **Article 136**.

The Supreme Court has held judicial review to be a part of the **basic structure** of the Constitution, which cannot be taken away even by a constitutional amendment.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00037', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 36, 'What did the Supreme Court hold in Kesavananda Bharati vs State of Kerala (1973)?', 'In **Kesavananda Bharati vs State of Kerala (1973)**, a 13-judge bench of the Supreme Court propounded the **"Basic Structure Doctrine."**

The Court held that Parliament''s power to amend the Constitution under **Article 368** is wide but **not unlimited** — it cannot alter the basic structure or essential features of the Constitution, such as the supremacy of the Constitution, the rule of law, and judicial review.

This landmark ruling, delivered by a narrow 7:6 majority, remains one of the most significant judgments in Indian constitutional history.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00038', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 37, 'What was held in the Golaknath vs State of Punjab (1967) case?', 'In **I.C. Golaknath vs State of Punjab (1967)**, the Supreme Court held that **Parliament has no power to amend Part III (Fundamental Rights)** of the Constitution.

The Court ruled that a constitutional amendment under Article 368 is **"law"** within the meaning of Article 13(2), and therefore cannot violate Fundamental Rights.

This ruling was effectively overturned by the **24th Amendment Act, 1971**, and later superseded by the more nuanced **Basic Structure Doctrine** laid down in Kesavananda Bharati.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00039', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 38, 'What marked the origin of Public Interest Litigation (PIL) in India?', '**Public Interest Litigation (PIL)** emerged in India in the late 1970s and early 1980s, pioneered by judges like **Justice P.N. Bhagwati and Justice V.R. Krishna Iyer**.

It relaxed the traditional rule of **locus standi** (only an aggrieved party can approach the court), allowing any public-spirited citizen or organisation to approach the courts on behalf of those who cannot do so themselves.

The **S.P. Gupta case (1981)**, also known as the "Judges'' Transfer case," is often cited as a landmark in formally recognising PIL in India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00040', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 39, 'What is the Collegium System for the appointment of judges in India?', 'The **Collegium System** is the mechanism by which judges of the **Supreme Court and High Courts** are appointed and transferred, evolved through a series of Supreme Court judgments known as the **"Three Judges Cases"** (1982, 1993, and 1998).

The Supreme Court Collegium is headed by the **Chief Justice of India** and comprises the **four senior-most judges** of the Supreme Court; recommendations are sent to the government, which can return them once but must accept them if reiterated.

The system is not mentioned in the Constitution but was devised through **judicial interpretation** of the word "consultation" with the CJI in Articles 124 and 217.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00041', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 40, 'Why was the National Judicial Appointments Commission (NJAC) struck down by the Supreme Court?', 'The **99th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2014**, along with the **NJAC Act, 2014**, sought to replace the Collegium system with a **National Judicial Appointments Commission** for appointing judges.

In **2015**, a 5-judge Constitution Bench of the Supreme Court struck down both the Amendment and the Act as **unconstitutional**, holding that they violated the **independence of the judiciary**, a part of the basic structure.

The Court held that the composition of the NJAC, which included the **Law Minister** and two eminent persons, compromised judicial primacy in appointments, and restored the Collegium system.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00042', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 41, 'How many High Courts are there in India, and under which Article are they established?', 'High Courts are established under **Article 214**, which states that there shall be a High Court for each State, though Parliament can establish a common High Court for two or more states/UTs under Article 231.

As of now, India has **25 High Courts**, with some High Courts, such as the Punjab and Haryana High Court, having jurisdiction over more than one state or UT.

The **Calcutta High Court (1862)** is the oldest High Court in India, while the newest is the **Andhra Pradesh High Court (2019)**, carved out after the state''s bifurcation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00043', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 42, 'How does the Seventh Schedule divide legislative powers between the Centre and the States?', 'The **Seventh Schedule** divides legislative subjects into three lists under **Article 246**.

- The **Union List** (around 100 subjects) — defence, foreign affairs, banking, currency — on which only Parliament can legislate
- The **State List** (around 61 subjects) — police, public health, agriculture — on which, ordinarily, only State Legislatures can legislate
- The **Concurrent List** (around 52 subjects) — education, forests, marriage — on which both can legislate, with **Union law prevailing** in case of conflict

Residuary powers, over subjects not mentioned in any list, rest with **Parliament** under Article 248.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00044', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 43, 'What is the Inter-State Council, and under which Article was it established?', 'The **Inter-State Council** is a recommendatory body established under **Article 263** of the Constitution to investigate and discuss matters of common interest between the Union and the States.

It was formally constituted by a **Presidential Order in 1990**, following the recommendation of the **Sarkaria Commission** on Centre-State relations.

It is chaired by the **Prime Minister** and includes Chief Ministers of all states, Chief Ministers or Administrators of UTs, and select Union Cabinet Ministers.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00045', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 44, 'What is the role of the Finance Commission of India?', 'The **Finance Commission** is a **quasi-judicial body** established under **Article 280**, constituted by the President every **five years** or earlier.

Its primary function is to recommend the **distribution of net proceeds of taxes** between the Union and the States, and the principles governing **grants-in-aid** to states.

It also addresses measures to augment resources of Panchayats and Municipalities, based on recommendations of the State Finance Commissions; the **16th Finance Commission**, chaired by Arvind Panagariya, covers the award period **2026-31**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00046', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 45, 'What is the three-tier structure of Panchayati Raj introduced by the 73rd Amendment?', 'The **73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992** gave constitutional status to Panchayati Raj Institutions by inserting **Part IX** and the **Eleventh Schedule** (29 subjects) into the Constitution.

It established a uniform **three-tier structure**: the **Gram Panchayat** at the village level, the **Panchayat Samiti** at the intermediate or block level, and the **Zila Parishad** at the district level.

It mandated **direct elections**, reservation of seats for **SC/ST and women** (at least one-third), and the constitution of **State Election Commissions** and **State Finance Commissions**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00047', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 46, 'What did the 74th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992 provide for urban local governance?', 'The **74th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992** added **Part IX-A** and the **Twelfth Schedule** (18 subjects) to the Constitution, giving constitutional recognition to **urban local bodies**.

It provides for three types of municipalities based on the urban area''s population and character — a **Nagar Panchayat** (transitional area), a **Municipal Council** (smaller urban area), and a **Municipal Corporation** (larger urban area).

It also provided for **Wards Committees** and reservation of seats for SC/ST and women, similar to the 73rd Amendment.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00048', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 47, 'What is a Gram Sabha, and how does it differ from a Gram Panchayat?', 'A **Gram Sabha** is a body consisting of all persons registered in the **electoral rolls** of a village comprised within the area of a Panchayat at the village level, as defined under Article 243.

It is a body of the **entire adult population**, not elected representatives, and functions as a forum for direct democracy — approving budgets, selecting beneficiaries for welfare schemes, and exercising social audit.

A **Gram Panchayat**, in contrast, is the **elected executive body** at the village level, accountable to the Gram Sabha.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00049', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 48, 'What is the composition of the Election Commission of India, and who is its current head?', 'The **Election Commission of India (ECI)**, a permanent constitutional body under **Article 324**, originally had only a Chief Election Commissioner but became a multi-member body in 1989-90.

It presently consists of the **Chief Election Commissioner (CEC)** and **two Election Commissioners**, appointed by the President; **Gyanesh Kumar** is the current CEC, having taken charge in February 2025 as the 26th person to hold the post.

Appointments are now governed by the **Chief Election Commissioner and other Election Commissioners (Appointment, Conditions of Service and Term of Office) Act, 2023**, enacted after a 2023 Supreme Court directive.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00050', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 49, 'What are the main functions of the Union Public Service Commission (UPSC)?', 'The **UPSC** is a constitutional body established under **Article 315**, functioning as the central recruiting agency for **All India Services and Central Civil Services**.

Its functions, detailed under **Article 320**, include conducting examinations for appointments, advising the government on matters of recruitment, promotions, and disciplinary actions, and framing or amending recruitment rules.

The Chairman and members are appointed by the **President** and can be removed only through a process involving an inquiry by the **Supreme Court**, as laid down in Article 317.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00051', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 50, 'What are the duties and powers of the Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) of India?', 'The **CAG**, provided for under **Article 148**, is often described as the **"guardian of the public purse"** and audits all receipts and expenditure of the Union and State governments.

The CAG submits its audit reports relating to the accounts of the Union to the **President**, who causes them to be laid before Parliament; these are then examined by the **Public Accounts Committee**.

Duties and powers of the CAG are further elaborated in the **CAG''s (Duties, Powers and Conditions of Service) Act, 1971**; **K. Sanjay Murthy** is the current, 15th, CAG, in office since November 2024.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00052', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 51, 'What is the role of the Attorney General for India?', 'The **Attorney General for India**, appointed under **Article 76**, is the **highest law officer** of the country and the Indian government''s chief legal adviser.

The AG must be qualified to be appointed a judge of the Supreme Court and has the **right of audience** in any court in India and the right to take part in Parliamentary proceedings without a vote, under Article 88.

**R. Venkataramani** is the current Attorney General, re-appointed in 2025 for a further term running to **2027**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00053', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 52, 'What is the legal basis and main function of the National Human Rights Commission (NHRC)?', 'The **NHRC** is a **statutory, not constitutional, body**, established under the **Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993**.

It is mandated to inquire into complaints of **violation of human rights** by public servants, review safeguards for human rights, and promote human rights literacy.

It is a multi-member body chaired by a **retired Chief Justice of India** or a judge of the Supreme Court, and its recommendations are not legally binding but carry significant moral and persuasive authority.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00054', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 53, 'When was the Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) established, and what statute now governs it?', 'The **Central Vigilance Commission (CVC)** was established in **1964** on the recommendation of the **Santhanam Committee** on prevention of corruption.

It functioned as an executive, non-statutory body until it was given **statutory status** through the **Central Vigilance Commission Act, 2003**.

The CVC is India''s apex vigilance body, free from executive control, overseeing vigilance administration and advising central government agencies on matters relating to corruption.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00055', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 54, 'What does the Lokpal and Lokayuktas Act, 2013 provide for?', 'The **Lokpal and Lokayuktas Act, 2013** provides for the establishment of a **Lokpal** at the Centre and **Lokayuktas** in the states, to inquire into allegations of corruption against public functionaries.

The **Lokpal** is a multi-member body consisting of a **Chairperson** and up to **eight members**, of whom not more than half shall be judicial members, with at least **50% reservation** for members from SC/ST/OBC/minority/women categories.

The Act followed the **Anna Hazare-led anti-corruption movement** of 2011; the first Lokpal Chairperson, **Justice Pinaki Chandra Ghose**, was appointed in 2019.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00056', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 55, 'What are the grounds for declaring a National Emergency under Article 352?', '**Article 352** empowers the President to proclaim a **National Emergency** if satisfied that the security of India is threatened by **war, external aggression, or armed rebellion**.

The term **"armed rebellion"** replaced the earlier phrase **"internal disturbance"** through the **44th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1978**, making it harder to invoke emergency on vague grounds.

Such a proclamation must be approved by **both Houses of Parliament within one month** by a special majority, and once approved, can remain in force for **six months** at a time, renewable indefinitely with further parliamentary approval.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00057', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 56, 'Under what circumstances can President''s Rule be imposed under Article 356?', '**Article 356** allows the President to impose **President''s Rule** in a State if satisfied, on a Governor''s report or otherwise, that the government of the State **cannot be carried on in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution**.

Under President''s Rule, the State''s executive authority is exercised by the **Governor** on behalf of the President, and the State Legislative Assembly is either suspended or dissolved.

Originally, President''s Rule could last up to **three years** with periodic parliamentary approval; the **S.R. Bommai case (1994)** made the proclamation subject to **judicial review** and limited its misuse.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00058', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 57, 'What is a Financial Emergency under Article 360, and has it ever been invoked in India?', '**Article 360** empowers the President to proclaim a **Financial Emergency** if satisfied that the financial stability or credit of India, or any part of its territory, is threatened.

During a Financial Emergency, the Union can direct States to observe specified **canons of financial propriety**, and the President can direct a **reduction of salaries** of persons serving the Union or a State, including judges of the Supreme Court and High Courts.

A Financial Emergency has **never been proclaimed** in India since the Constitution came into force in 1950.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00059', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 58, 'What are the three types of constitutional amendment procedures under Article 368?', '**Article 368** provides for amendment of the Constitution through distinct procedures of varying rigidity.

- By a **simple majority** of Parliament, outside the formal procedure of Article 368 (e.g., formation of new states or alteration of boundaries)
- By a **special majority** of Parliament — a majority of total membership and two-thirds of members present and voting in each House
- By a **special majority plus ratification by at least half the State Legislatures** — required for amendments affecting federal provisions, such as election of the President or representation of states in Parliament', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00060', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 59, 'What is the purpose of the Ninth Schedule of the Constitution?', 'The **Ninth Schedule** was added by the **First Constitutional Amendment Act, 1951**, originally to protect land reform laws from judicial review by placing them beyond challenge on Fundamental Rights grounds.

Laws placed in the Ninth Schedule were traditionally immune from being struck down for violating Fundamental Rights, under **Article 31B**.

However, in the **I.R. Coelho case (2007)**, the Supreme Court held that laws placed in the Ninth Schedule **after 24 April 1973** (the date of the Kesavananda Bharati judgment) are open to judicial review if they violate the **basic structure** or Fundamental Rights.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00061', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 60, 'How many Schedules does the Indian Constitution currently have, and what do the newer ones cover?', 'The Indian Constitution currently has **twelve Schedules**, having started with eight in 1950.

Notable additions include the **Ninth Schedule** (1st Amendment, 1951, land reform laws), the **Tenth Schedule** (52nd Amendment, 1985, anti-defection), the **Eleventh Schedule** (73rd Amendment, 1992, Panchayati Raj subjects), and the **Twelfth Schedule** (74th Amendment, 1992, Municipality subjects).

The **Eighth Schedule** lists the officially recognised languages of India, currently numbering **22**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00062', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 61, 'What was the significance of Article 370, and what happened to it in 2019?', '**Article 370** granted **special autonomous status** to the former state of Jammu & Kashmir, allowing it to have its own constitution and restricting the application of central laws without state concurrence, except in defence, foreign affairs, and communications.

On **5 August 2019**, the President issued a Constitutional Order effectively abrogating the special provisions of Article 370, and Parliament passed the **Jammu and Kashmir Reorganisation Act, 2019**, bifurcating the state into **two Union Territories** — Jammu & Kashmir (with legislature) and Ladakh (without legislature).

In **December 2023**, a 5-judge Constitution Bench of the Supreme Court in *In Re: Article 370* unanimously **upheld the abrogation** as constitutionally valid.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00063', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Polity & Constitution', 0, 62, 'What is the significance of the 103rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 2019?', 'The **103rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 2019** introduced **10% reservation for Economically Weaker Sections (EWS)** among citizens not already covered by existing SC/ST/OBC reservation schemes.

It inserted **Article 15(6)** and **Article 16(6)**, enabling the State to make special provisions for the advancement of EWS in educational institutions and public employment, over and above existing reservation ceilings.

In **Janhit Abhiyan vs Union of India (2022)**, a 5-judge Constitution Bench of the Supreme Court **upheld the validity** of EWS reservation by a 3:2 majority, holding it did not violate the basic structure despite breaching the 50% reservation ceiling.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00064', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 0, 'What are the major sites of the Indus Valley Civilization located in present-day India, and what is one distinctive feature each is known for?', '**Dholavira** (Gujarat) is known for its unique **water conservation system** of reservoirs and a signboard with Indus script.

**Lothal** (Gujarat) had a famous **dockyard**, pointing to maritime trade.

**Kalibangan** (Rajasthan) revealed evidence of a **ploughed field** and fire altars.

**Rakhigarhi** (Haryana) is considered one of the **largest Harappan sites** and has yielded important ancient DNA evidence.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00065', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 1, 'What were the key urban planning features of Mohenjo-daro and Harappa?', 'Both cities show a **grid pattern** of streets intersecting at right angles, divided into a citadel (upper town) and a lower town.

Mohenjo-daro is especially known for the **Great Bath**, a large watertight tank likely used for ritual bathing, and an advanced **drainage system** with covered drains along streets.

Harappa is notable for its **granaries** and evidence of a well-organised residential area.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00066', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 2, 'How is the Rigveda significant among the four Vedas?', 'The **Rigveda** is the **oldest** of the four Vedas and one of the oldest texts in any Indo-European language, composed in **Vedic Sanskrit**.

It consists of **10 Mandalas (books)** containing hymns (suktas) addressed mainly to nature deities such as **Agni, Indra, and Varuna**.

It is the principal source for reconstructing the society and religion of the **Early Vedic period** (c. 1500–1000 BCE).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00067', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 3, 'What distinguishes the Early Vedic period from the Later Vedic period?', 'The **Early Vedic period** (c. 1500–1000 BCE) was pastoral, cattle-centred, with a tribal polity and simple sacrifices reflected in the **Rigveda**.

The **Later Vedic period** (c. 1000–600 BCE) saw a shift to **settled agriculture**, use of iron tools, emergence of **varna-based social stratification**, growth of larger kingdoms (janapadas), and elaborate rituals described in the **Yajurveda, Samaveda, Atharvaveda, and Brahmana texts**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00068', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 4, 'Who founded Jainism as a systematized philosophy, and what were his core teachings?', '**Mahavira** (Vardhamana), the **24th and last Tirthankara**, is credited with systematizing Jain philosophy in the 6th century BCE. He was born at **Kundagrama near Vaishali** and attained **Nirvana at Pavapuri**.

His teachings rest on the **Triratna (Three Jewels)**: Right Faith, Right Knowledge, and Right Conduct.

He emphasized **Ahimsa (non-violence)**, **Anekantavada** (many-sidedness of truth), and strict asceticism as paths to liberation (moksha).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00069', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 5, 'What are the Four Noble Truths and the Eightfold Path preached by Gautama Buddha?', 'The **Four Noble Truths** state that: life is full of suffering (dukkha); suffering has a cause (desire/craving); suffering can be ended; and there is a path leading to its cessation.

That path is the **Eightfold Path (Ashtangika Marga)**, comprising Right View, Right Intention, Right Speech, Right Action, Right Livelihood, Right Effort, Right Mindfulness, and Right Concentration — often grouped under wisdom, ethical conduct, and mental discipline.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00070', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 6, 'Where were the four major events in the life of Gautama Buddha — birth, enlightenment, first sermon, and death — located?', 'Buddha was born at **Lumbini** (in present-day Nepal).

He attained enlightenment under the Bodhi tree at **Bodh Gaya**.

He delivered his first sermon (Dharmachakra Pravartana) at **Sarnath**, near Varanasi.

He attained **Mahaparinirvana (death)** at **Kushinagar**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00071', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 7, 'What were the four Buddhist Councils, and who patronized each?', 'The **First Council** (c. 483 BCE) was held at **Rajagriha** under the patronage of **King Ajatashatru**, soon after Buddha''s death.

The **Second Council** (c. 383 BCE) was held at **Vaishali** under **King Kalashoka**, where the Sangha split into Sthaviravadins and Mahasanghikas.

The **Third Council** (c. 250 BCE) was held at **Pataliputra** under **Emperor Ashoka**, presided over by Moggaliputta Tissa, which compiled the Tripitaka.

The **Fourth Council** (c. 1st-2nd century CE) was held in **Kashmir** under **Kushana king Kanishka**, where the split into **Hinayana and Mahayana** schools was formalized.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00072', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 8, 'How did Chandragupta Maurya come to establish the Mauryan Empire?', '**Chandragupta Maurya**, guided by his mentor and strategist **Chanakya (Kautilya)**, overthrew the **Nanda dynasty** around 321 BCE and established the Mauryan Empire with its capital at **Pataliputra**.

He later defeated **Seleucus Nicator**, a general of Alexander, acquiring territories up to the Hindu Kush, and received **Megasthenes** as a Greek ambassador at his court — whose account *Indica* describes Mauryan administration.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00073', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 9, 'What prompted Ashoka''s policy of Dhamma, and what does it signify?', 'The bloodshed of the **Kalinga War (c. 261 BCE)** profoundly affected Ashoka, leading him to renounce further military conquest (`Bherighosha` replaced by `Dhammaghosha`) and embrace **Buddhism**.

His policy of **Dhamma** was not a religious doctrine but a code of **social ethics** — emphasizing tolerance, non-violence, respect for elders, and welfare measures — propagated through **edicts inscribed on rocks and pillars** across the empire and officials called **Dhamma Mahamatras**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00074', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 10, 'Why is the reign of Samudragupta significant, and what source describes his conquests?', '**Samudragupta**, often called the **''Napoleon of India''** by historian V.A. Smith, greatly expanded the Gupta Empire through extensive military campaigns across northern and southern India.

His achievements are recorded in the **Allahabad Prashasti (Pillar Inscription)**, composed by his court poet **Harisena**, which also portrays him as a patron of arts, being skilled in music and poetry.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00075', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 11, 'What scientific and mathematical achievements mark the Gupta period as a ''Golden Age''?', '**Aryabhata**, in his work *Aryabhatiya* (499 CE), explained the concept of **zero**, calculated the value of pi, and proposed that the earth rotates on its axis.

**Varahamihira** contributed to astronomy and astrology through the *Panchasiddhantika* and *Brihat Samhita*.

This era also saw flourishing Sanskrit literature (Kalidasa), the rock-cut **Ajanta cave paintings**, and advances in metallurgy, exemplified by the rust-resistant **Iron Pillar of Delhi**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00076', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 12, 'What was distinctive about the Sangam Age in South India?', 'The **Sangam Age** (roughly 3rd century BCE to 3rd century CE) refers to a body of classical **Tamil literature** composed at assemblies (Sangams) believed to be held at **Madurai** under the patronage of **Pandya kings**.

It provides insight into the polity, society, and economy of the three early Tamil dynasties — the **Cheras, Cholas, and Pandyas** — and records flourishing **overseas trade with Rome** through ports like Muziris and Arikamedu.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00077', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 13, 'Which dynasties constituted the Delhi Sultanate, and in what sequence did they rule?', 'The Delhi Sultanate (1206–1526) comprised five dynasties in sequence: the **Mamluk (Slave) dynasty** (1206–1290), the **Khilji dynasty** (1290–1320), the **Tughlaq dynasty** (1320–1414), the **Sayyid dynasty** (1414–1451), and the **Lodi dynasty** (1451–1526).

The Sultanate ended when **Babur** defeated **Ibrahim Lodi** at the **First Battle of Panipat (1526)**, founding the Mughal Empire.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00078', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 14, 'Who was Razia Sultan, and what was unique about her reign?', '**Razia Sultan**, daughter of **Iltutmish**, was the **only woman to rule as Sultan of Delhi** (1236–1240) in the Mamluk dynasty.

Her reign faced resistance from the Turkish nobility (the *Chalisa* or Group of Forty) partly because of her gender, and also due to her closeness to an Abyssinian noble, **Malik Yaqut**; she was eventually overthrown and killed.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00079', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 15, 'What were the major market control reforms introduced by Alauddin Khilji?', 'Alauddin Khilji introduced strict **market control reforms (Bazaar Niyantran)** to maintain a large standing army at low cost, fixing prices of essential commodities such as grain, cloth, and horses.

He established **state-controlled granaries**, maintained detailed price registers, and appointed officers like the **Shahna-i-Mandi** to supervise markets — measures historians regard as a remarkable early experiment in price control.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00080', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 16, 'What were Muhammad bin Tughlaq''s two most controversial administrative experiments?', 'He ordered the **transfer of the capital** from Delhi to **Daulatabad** in the Deccan, intending better administrative control over the empire, but the move caused great hardship and was eventually reversed.

He also introduced **token currency** — copper/bronze coins meant to have the value of silver tanka — but widespread counterfeiting forced him to withdraw the experiment, draining the treasury.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00081', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 17, 'Who founded the Vijayanagara Empire, and what led to its eventual decline?', 'The Vijayanagara Empire was founded in **1336 CE** by brothers **Harihara and Bukka** on the banks of the **Tungabhadra River**, reaching its zenith under **Krishnadevaraya** of the Tuluva dynasty.

Its power was broken at the **Battle of Talikota (1565)**, where a confederacy of Deccan Sultanates decisively defeated Vijayanagara forces, after which the capital Hampi was sacked, though the dynasty survived in reduced form for decades.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00082', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 18, 'When and by whom was the Bahmani Kingdom established?', 'The **Bahmani Kingdom** was founded in **1347 CE** by **Zafar Khan**, who took the title **Ala-ud-din Bahman Shah**, after revolting against Muhammad bin Tughlaq''s governor in the Deccan.

Its capital was first at **Gulbarga** and later **Bidar**; the kingdom eventually fragmented around 1527 into **five Deccan Sultanates** — Bijapur, Golconda, Ahmadnagar, Bidar, and Berar.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00083', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 19, 'What were the key features of Akbar''s administrative and religious policies?', 'Akbar introduced the **Mansabdari system**, ranking nobles and officials by numerical ranks (zat and sawar) to organize the military and civil administration.

His land revenue system, refined by **Raja Todar Mal**, was called the **Zabti/Dahsala system**, based on a ten-year average of crop yields and prices.

He also promoted religious tolerance through the policy of **Sulh-i-Kul** (peace with all) and founded the eclectic order **Din-i-Ilahi**, besides abolishing the **jizya tax** on non-Muslims.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00084', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 20, 'What was the historical significance of the Battle of Haldighati (1576)?', 'The Battle of Haldighati was fought between the forces of **Akbar**, led by **Raja Man Singh**, and **Maharana Pratap** of Mewar.

Although Akbar''s forces prevailed and Maharana Pratap had to retreat, Pratap was never fully subdued and continued guerrilla resistance, making him a celebrated symbol of **Rajput resistance** to Mughal expansion.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00085', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 21, 'For what is the Mughal emperor Shah Jahan primarily remembered, and what marked a turning point under Aurangzeb?', '**Shah Jahan** is remembered as a great patron of architecture, commissioning the **Taj Mahal** at Agra (built in memory of Mumtaz Mahal), the **Red Fort**, and the **Jama Masjid** in Delhi.

Under **Aurangzeb**, the empire reached its greatest territorial extent but also saw the **reimposition of jizya**, prolonged **Deccan wars**, and growing religious orthodoxy — developments historians link to the empire''s long-term decline after his death.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00086', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 22, 'What were the core teachings of the Bhakti saint-poets Kabir and Guru Nanak?', '**Kabir**, believed to be a disciple of Ramananda, preached a formless, **Nirguna** concept of God, rejecting idol worship, caste distinctions, and ritualism, blending ideas from both Hindu and Islamic traditions in his verses (dohas).

**Guru Nanak**, founder of **Sikhism**, similarly preached **monotheism**, equality of all humans regardless of caste or religion, and the importance of honest living (kirat karo) and selfless service (seva), later compiled in the **Guru Granth Sahib**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00087', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 23, 'Who was Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti, and what was the significance of the Chishti Sufi order?', '**Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti** founded the **Chishti Sufi order** in India, establishing his khanqah (hospice) at **Ajmer**, which remains a major pilgrimage site (dargah) today.

The Chishti order emphasized **love, tolerance, simplicity, and service to the poor**, and deliberately kept a distance from state power, helping Sufi ideas find broad popular appeal across religious communities in medieval India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00088', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 24, 'How did Shivaji organize the administration of the Maratha kingdom?', 'Shivaji was formally crowned **Chhatrapati** in **1674** at **Raigad**, establishing an independent Maratha kingdom.

His administration featured a council of eight ministers known as the **Ashtapradhan**, and he is especially noted for mastering **guerrilla warfare (Ganimi Kava)** tactics to counter the larger Mughal and Bijapur armies, along with an efficient revenue system based on **Chauth and Sardeshmukhi** levies.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00089', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 25, 'What was the outcome of the Third Battle of Panipat (1761), and why is it historically significant?', 'The Third Battle of Panipat (1761) was fought between the **Maratha Confederacy**, led by Sadashivrao Bhau, and **Ahmad Shah Abdali** of Afghanistan, allied with Rohilla and Awadh forces.

The Marathas suffered a **devastating defeat** with heavy losses, which significantly weakened their expansion northward and created a power vacuum that indirectly facilitated the later rise of **British dominance** in India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00090', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 26, 'When did Vasco da Gama arrive in India, and what was its significance for European trade?', '**Vasco da Gama**, a Portuguese explorer, discovered the **sea route to India** via the Cape of Good Hope, landing at **Calicut (Kozhikode)** in **1498**.

This opened **direct maritime trade** between Europe and India, bypassing Arab and Venetian middlemen, and marked the beginning of sustained European commercial and later colonial involvement in India, starting with the **Portuguese**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00091', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 27, 'What was the outcome of the Battle of Plassey (1757)?', 'The **Battle of Plassey (1757)** was fought between the **British East India Company**, led by **Robert Clive**, and **Siraj-ud-Daulah**, the Nawab of Bengal.

Through the treachery of Siraj-ud-Daulah''s commander **Mir Jafar**, the British secured a decisive victory, which gave the Company effective political control over **Bengal** and is widely regarded as the **foundation of British territorial power** in India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00092', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 28, 'What rights did the British East India Company gain from the Battle of Buxar (1764)?', 'The **Battle of Buxar (1764)** was fought by the British against the combined forces of **Mir Qasim** (Bengal), **Shuja-ud-Daula** (Awadh), and **Mughal emperor Shah Alam II**.

The decisive British victory led to the **Treaty of Allahabad (1765)**, under which the Company obtained **Diwani rights** (the right to collect revenue) over **Bengal, Bihar, and Odisha**, marking its transformation from a trading entity into a ruling power.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00093', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 29, 'What was the Permanent Settlement of 1793, and who introduced it?', 'The **Permanent Settlement** was introduced in **1793** by Governor-General **Lord Cornwallis** in Bengal, Bihar, and Odisha.

It fixed the land revenue payable by **zamindars** to the Company **permanently**, converting them into hereditary landowners, which created a powerful landed class but often led to oppressive rent extraction from the actual cultivators.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00094', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 30, 'What were the main immediate and underlying causes of the Revolt of 1857?', 'The immediate trigger was the introduction of the new **Enfield rifle cartridges**, rumoured to be greased with cow and pig fat, which offended both Hindu and Muslim sepoys.

Underlying causes included Lord Dalhousie''s **Doctrine of Lapse** (annexing princely states without a natural heir), economic exploitation of peasants and artisans, and resentment among dispossessed nobility and sepoys over pay and discriminatory treatment.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00095', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 31, 'Who were the key leaders of the Revolt of 1857 at different centres?', 'At **Delhi**, the sepoys rallied around the symbolic figurehead **Bahadur Shah Zafar**, the last Mughal emperor.

At **Kanpur**, the revolt was led by **Nana Sahib**, assisted by **Tatya Tope**; at **Jhansi**, by **Rani Lakshmibai**; and at **Lucknow**, by **Begum Hazrat Mahal**. **Mangal Pandey**, a sepoy at Barrackpore, is often credited with an early act of defiance that helped spark the uprising.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00096', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 32, 'What social reforms did Raja Ram Mohan Roy champion, and what organization did he found?', 'Raja Ram Mohan Roy founded the **Brahmo Sabha in 1828** in Calcutta (later reorganized as the **Brahmo Samaj**), which advocated **monotheism** and rejected idol worship and ritualism.

He campaigned vigorously against the practice of **Sati**, contributing significantly to **Lord William Bentinck''s Regulation XVII of 1829**, which formally abolished and criminalized the practice.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00097', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 33, 'What were the central teachings and reform agenda of the Arya Samaj?', 'The **Arya Samaj** was founded in **1875** by **Swami Dayanand Saraswati** in Bombay, with the call **''Back to the Vedas.''**

It rejected idol worship, caste rigidities, and child marriage, while promoting the **Shuddhi movement** for reconversion to Hinduism, women''s education, and a rational, Vedic-based reformed Hinduism.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00098', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 34, 'Who founded the Ramakrishna Mission, and what was its guiding philosophy?', 'The **Ramakrishna Mission** was founded in **1897** by **Swami Vivekananda**, a chief disciple of **Ramakrishna Paramahamsa**, with headquarters at **Belur Math**.

It combined **Vedanta philosophy** with practical social service — running schools, hospitals, and relief work — and Vivekananda''s famous address at the **1893 Parliament of Religions in Chicago** brought global attention to Hindu philosophy.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00099', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 35, 'When and by whom was the Indian National Congress founded, and where was its first session held?', 'The Indian National Congress was founded in **1885**, with the key role played by **Allan Octavian Hume**, a retired British civil servant.

Its **first session** was held in **Bombay in December 1885** under the presidency of **W.C. Bonnerjee**, with 72 delegates attending.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00100', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 36, 'What distinguished the Moderates from the Extremists within the early Indian National Congress?', 'The **Moderates** (such as Dadabhai Naoroji, Gopal Krishna Gokhale, and Pherozeshah Mehta), who dominated the Congress until around 1905, believed in constitutional methods — petitions, resolutions, and dialogue with the British — to seek reforms.

The **Extremists** (such as Bal Gangadhar Tilak, Bipin Chandra Pal, and Lala Lajpat Rai — the ''Lal-Bal-Pal'' trio) favoured more assertive methods including **Swadeshi, boycott, and passive resistance**, and sought **Swaraj** as a fundamental right rather than a gradual concession.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00101', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 37, 'Why did Lord Curzon partition Bengal in 1905, and what was the public reaction?', 'Lord Curzon partitioned Bengal in **1905**, officially citing administrative convenience, but it was widely seen as a deliberate attempt to **weaken Bengali nationalism** by splitting the Hindu-majority and Muslim-majority regions.

The move triggered the **Swadeshi Movement**, involving boycott of British goods, promotion of indigenous industries, and mass protests; the partition was ultimately annulled in **1911**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00102', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 38, 'What caused the Surat Split of 1907 in the Indian National Congress?', 'The **Surat Split (1907)** occurred due to deepening ideological differences between the **Moderates and Extremists** over methods of political action and the selection of the Congress president.

The Extremists, led by **Tilak**, were effectively expelled, and the Congress split into two factions, which were not reunited until the **Lucknow Session of 1916**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00103', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 39, 'What key provision did the Morley-Minto Reforms (Indian Councils Act, 1909) introduce?', 'The **Morley-Minto Reforms of 1909** expanded the number of elected members in legislative councils, but their most consequential feature was the introduction of **separate electorates for Muslims**.

This institutionalized **communal representation** in Indian politics for the first time, a development many historians view as a step toward later communal polarization.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00104', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 40, 'What were the key features and significance of the Champaran Satyagraha (1917)?', 'The **Champaran Satyagraha (1917)** in Bihar was Gandhi''s **first major satyagraha in India**, undertaken on behalf of indigo cultivators forced under the **Tinkathia system** to grow indigo on a portion of their land for British planters.

It successfully secured relief for the peasants and established Gandhi''s method of **non-violent civil resistance** as a viable political tool in the Indian freedom struggle.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00105', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 41, 'What led to the Jallianwala Bagh massacre of 1919, and what was its impact?', 'The massacre occurred on **13 April 1919** at **Jallianwala Bagh, Amritsar**, when **General Reginald Dyer** ordered troops to open fire on an unarmed crowd gathered partly to protest the repressive **Rowlatt Act**, killing hundreds.

The massacre caused widespread outrage, prompting **Rabindranath Tagore** to renounce his knighthood, and significantly radicalized Indian public opinion against British rule.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00106', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 42, 'What were the aims and the reason for calling off the Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22)?', 'Launched by Gandhi in **1920**, the **Non-Cooperation Movement** called for boycotting British titles, educational institutions, courts, and foreign goods, combined with promotion of **khadi** and **Hindu-Muslim unity** (linked with the Khilafat Movement).

Gandhi abruptly **withdrew the movement in February 1922** after the **Chauri Chaura incident**, where a violent mob killed policemen, as he believed the movement had strayed from strict non-violence.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00107', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 43, 'What was the Simon Commission, and why was it boycotted?', 'The **Simon Commission (1927)**, officially the Indian Statutory Commission, was appointed to review the working of the **Government of India Act, 1919** and suggest constitutional reforms.

It was boycotted across India with cries of **''Simon Go Back''** because it had **no Indian members**, seen as a blatant insult to Indian self-respect; protests included one in Lahore where **Lala Lajpat Rai** was fatally injured in a lathi charge.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00108', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 44, 'What was the significance of the Dandi March (Salt Satyagraha) of 1930?', 'Gandhi led the **Dandi March** from **12 March to 6 April 1930**, walking about 240 miles from Sabarmati Ashram to the coastal village of **Dandi** in Gujarat, where he broke the colonial **salt laws** by making salt from seawater.

It marked the formal launch of the **Civil Disobedience Movement**, drawing mass participation across India and significant international media attention to the independence struggle.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00109', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 45, 'What was agreed upon in the Gandhi-Irwin Pact (1931)?', 'The **Gandhi-Irwin Pact**, signed in **March 1931** between Gandhi and Viceroy **Lord Irwin**, led to the **suspension of the Civil Disobedience Movement** in exchange for the release of political prisoners and permission for Indians to make salt for personal use.

It also led to Gandhi''s participation, as the sole Congress representative, in the **Second Round Table Conference** in London later that year.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00110', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 46, 'What was the Poona Pact of 1932, and between whom was it signed?', 'The **Poona Pact** was signed in **September 1932** between **Mahatma Gandhi** and **Dr. B.R. Ambedkar**, following Gandhi''s fast against the **Communal Award**''s provision for separate electorates for the ''Depressed Classes.''

Under the pact, separate electorates were replaced with **reserved seats for Depressed Classes within the general electorate**, a compromise that significantly shaped future affirmative action policy in India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00111', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 47, 'What were the key features of the Government of India Act, 1935?', 'The Government of India Act, 1935 proposed an **All-India Federation** of British provinces and princely states (which never fully materialized) and introduced **provincial autonomy**, giving elected Indian ministries greater control over provincial subjects.

It also established a **Federal Court** and expanded the franchise, and is considered the **blueprint for much of the Constitution of independent India**, including its administrative and federal structure.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00112', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 48, 'Who were Bhagat Singh and his associates, and what was the HSRA?', '**Bhagat Singh**, along with **Chandrashekhar Azad, Sukhdev, and Rajguru**, were prominent members of the **Hindustan Socialist Republican Association (HSRA)**, a revolutionary organization aiming for complete independence and a socialist state.

Bhagat Singh and **Batukeshwar Dutt** threw a bomb in the **Central Legislative Assembly in 1929** to protest repressive bills, deliberately courting arrest; Bhagat Singh, Sukhdev, and Rajguru were later **hanged in March 1931** in the Lahore Conspiracy Case.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00113', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 49, 'What was the Cripps Mission (1942), and why did it fail?', 'The **Cripps Mission**, led by **Sir Stafford Cripps** in **March 1942**, offered Dominion Status after the war and the right for provinces to opt out of the Indian Union, in exchange for wartime cooperation.

It failed because it did **not offer immediate self-government** and deferred full independence to an undefined post-war future; Gandhi famously described it as **''a post-dated cheque on a crashing bank.''**', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00114', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 50, 'What was the Quit India Movement (1942), and what was its outcome?', 'Launched by Gandhi on **8 August 1942** with the call **''Do or Die,''** the **Quit India Movement** demanded an immediate end to British rule.

The British responded with mass arrests of top Congress leaders overnight, leading to a largely **leaderless but widespread popular uprising** involving strikes, sabotage, and parallel governments in some areas; though suppressed, it signalled that British rule had become untenable in the long run.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00115', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 51, 'What was the Indian National Army (INA), and who led it?', 'The **Indian National Army (Azad Hind Fauj)** was formed with Indian prisoners of war and expatriates to fight British rule with Japanese assistance during World War II, and was reorganized and led by **Subhas Chandra Bose** from 1943.

Bose also proclaimed a provisional **''Azad Hind'' government** in exile; though militarily unsuccessful, the subsequent **INA trials (Red Fort Trials, 1945-46)** galvanized nationwide sympathy and hastened the end of British rule.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00116', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 52, 'What was the Lahore Resolution of 1940, and what did it demand?', 'The **Lahore Resolution**, passed by the **All-India Muslim League** under **Muhammad Ali Jinnah** in **March 1940**, demanded that regions where Muslims were numerically in a majority (northwestern and eastern India) be constituted as **''independent states.''**

It is regarded as the foundational document articulating the demand that eventually led to the creation of **Pakistan**, formalizing the League''s **Two-Nation Theory**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00117', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 53, 'What was the Cabinet Mission Plan of 1946?', 'The **Cabinet Mission** (1946) proposed a three-tier federal structure with a weak centre handling only defence, foreign affairs, and communications, provinces grouped into three sections, and strong provincial autonomy, intended to keep India united while addressing Muslim League concerns.

It also proposed an **interim government** and a **Constituent Assembly** to frame India''s constitution; however, differing interpretations by the Congress and Muslim League led to its eventual breakdown and the shift toward partition.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00118', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 54, 'What was Direct Action Day (1946), and what triggered it?', '**Direct Action Day**, called by the **Muslim League** on **16 August 1946**, was intended to press the demand for Pakistan after the breakdown of the Cabinet Mission talks.

It resulted in widespread **communal violence**, most severely in Calcutta (the ''Great Calcutta Killings''), and significantly hardened positions on both sides, accelerating the political slide toward **Partition**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00119', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 55, 'What was the Mountbatten Plan, and how did it lead to Partition?', 'The **Mountbatten Plan (June 1947)**, announced by the last Viceroy **Lord Mountbatten**, proposed the partition of British India into two independent dominions, **India and Pakistan**, with princely states given the choice to accede to either.

It formed the basis of the **Indian Independence Act, 1947**, passed by the British Parliament, under which India and Pakistan became independent on **15 and 14 August 1947** respectively.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00120', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 56, 'Who was tasked with drawing the boundary between India and Pakistan at Partition, and what body did this?', 'The boundaries between India and Pakistan (in Punjab and Bengal) were determined by the **Radcliffe Line**, drawn by British barrister **Sir Cyril Radcliffe**, who chaired the **Boundary Commissions** for both provinces.

The hurried and secretive process, announced only after independence, contributed to **mass migration and communal violence**, resulting in one of the largest displacements of people in modern history.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00121', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 57, 'Who were the ''Lal-Bal-Pal'' and why are they remembered in the national movement?', '''Lal-Bal-Pal'' refers to **Lala Lajpat Rai, Bal Gangadhar Tilak, and Bipin Chandra Pal**, the triumvirate of assertive nationalist leaders associated with the **Extremist** wing of the Congress in the early 1900s.

They championed **Swaraj, Swadeshi, boycott, and national education**, mobilizing mass sentiment well beyond the limited, petition-based politics of the earlier Moderates.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00122', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 58, 'What was the significance of the Lucknow Pact of 1916?', 'The **Lucknow Pact (1916)** marked a rare moment of unity between the **Indian National Congress and the All-India Muslim League**, who jointly demanded greater self-government from the British.

It also reunited the **Moderate and Extremist factions** of the Congress, and controversially endorsed **separate electorates** for Muslims, a concession that had long-term implications for communal politics.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00123', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 59, 'What was the Swadeshi Movement, and what economic ideas did it promote?', 'The **Swadeshi Movement**, which grew out of the agitation against the **Partition of Bengal (1905)**, called for the **boycott of British/foreign goods** and the promotion of **indigenously made (swadeshi) products**.

It encouraged the growth of Indian-owned textile mills and other industries, promoted **national education** institutions, and is seen as a precursor to the mass movements later led by Gandhi.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00124', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 60, 'What was the Rowlatt Act (1919), and how did Indians respond to it?', 'The **Rowlatt Act (1919)** empowered the British government to **detain individuals without trial** and curtail civil liberties, ostensibly to combat anti-colonial ''conspiracies,'' extending wartime emergency powers into peacetime.

Gandhi condemned it as a **''black act''** and called for a nationwide **hartal (strike)**; the resulting protests, especially in Punjab, led directly to the tragic **Jallianwala Bagh massacre**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00125', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 61, 'What was the Khilafat Movement, and why did Gandhi support it?', 'The **Khilafat Movement (1919-1924)** was launched by Indian Muslims, led by the **Ali Brothers (Shaukat Ali and Muhammad Ali)**, to pressure the British to preserve the authority of the **Ottoman Caliph** after World War I.

Gandhi supported it to forge **Hindu-Muslim unity**, linking it with the **Non-Cooperation Movement**; however, the Khilafat cause lost relevance after Turkey itself abolished the Caliphate in 1924 under **Mustafa Kemal Atatürk**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00126', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian History (Ancient, Medieval & Modern)', 1, 62, 'What distinguished the aims of the 1946 Interim Government from the subsequent transfer of power?', 'The **Interim Government (1946)**, formed under the Cabinet Mission''s framework with **Jawaharlal Nehru** as Vice-President of the Executive Council, was meant to govern jointly with Congress and Muslim League participation while a Constituent Assembly framed the constitution.

Persistent disagreement and the Muslim League''s policy of obstruction within this government reflected the deepening political deadlock that ultimately culminated in the **Partition of India in 1947**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00127', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 0, 'What are the three parallel ranges of the Himalayas, from north to south?', 'The northernmost range is the **Himadri (Greater Himalayas)**, the highest and most continuous range containing peaks like **Everest** and **Kangchenjunga**.

South of it lies the **Himachal (Lesser Himalayas)**, with rugged ranges such as the **Pir Panjal** and **Dhauladhar**, known for hill stations.

The southernmost and youngest range is the **Shiwalik**, made of unconsolidated sediments, with **Duns** (valleys like Dehradun) lying between it and the Himachal range.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00128', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 1, 'Which is the highest peak located entirely within Indian territory?', '**Nanda Devi** (7,816 m), in Uttarakhand, is the highest peak lying wholly within India.

**Kangchenjunga** (8,586 m), India''s highest overall and the world''s third-highest peak, straddles the **India-Nepal border** in Sikkim, so it is not entirely within India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00129', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 2, 'How do Himalayan rivers differ from Peninsular rivers?', '**Himalayan rivers** (e.g., Ganga, Indus, Brahmaputra) are **perennial**, fed by both monsoon rain and melting snow/glaciers, and are young, long rivers that still actively erode, forming deep gorges and large meanders.

**Peninsular rivers** (e.g., Godavari, Krishna, Mahanadi) are mostly **seasonal/rain-fed**, flow over the old, stable Peninsular plateau through shallower valleys, and generally lack the extensive meandering seen in the plains.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00130', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 3, 'Where does the Indus river originate, and in which direction does it flow?', 'The **Indus** originates near **Lake Mansarovar** in Tibet, close to the **Bokhar Chu glacier**, at an elevation of about 5,164 m.

It flows through **Ladakh**, then takes a sharp bend around the **Nanga Parbat** massif before flowing southwards through **Pakistan** into the **Arabian Sea**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00131', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 4, 'What is the source of the river Ganga, and what is its source glacier called?', 'The Ganga originates as the **Bhagirathi** from the **Gangotri glacier** at **Gaumukh** in Uttarakhand.

It is joined by the **Alaknanda** at **Devprayag**, after which the combined river is called the **Ganga**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00132', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 5, 'What is distinctive about the course of the Brahmaputra river across different countries?', 'The Brahmaputra originates near the **Angsi Glacier** in Tibet, where it is known as the **Yarlung Tsangpo**.

It enters India through Arunachal Pradesh as the **Dihang (Siang)**, is joined by the **Dibang** and **Lohit** to become the **Brahmaputra** in Assam, and finally joins the Ganga in Bangladesh as the **Jamuna** before draining into the **Bay of Bengal**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00133', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 6, 'Name the major tributaries of the river Ganga on its northern (left) and southern (right) banks.', 'On the **left (northern) bank**, the main tributaries are the **Ghaghara, Gandak, Kosi**, and **Ramganga**, all originating in the Himalayas.

On the **right (southern) bank**, the main tributaries are the **Yamuna, Son, Chambal**, and **Betwa**, which drain the Peninsular region.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00134', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 7, 'Why do the Narmada and Tapi rivers flow westward unlike most Peninsular rivers?', 'The **Narmada** and **Tapi** flow through **rift valleys** formed by down-faulting between the **Vindhya** and **Satpura** ranges, rather than following the general eastward slope of the Peninsular plateau.

This geological structure directs both rivers westward into the **Arabian Sea**, unlike other major Peninsular rivers (Godavari, Krishna, Mahanadi, Kaveri) which flow east into the **Bay of Bengal**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00135', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 8, 'Differentiate between the Western Ghats and the Eastern Ghats.', 'The **Western Ghats (Sahyadri)** form a continuous, steep, and higher range running along India''s west coast, acting as a major **monsoon-blocking barrier**; they are a recognized **UNESCO World Heritage Site** and biodiversity hotspot, with the highest peak **Anamudi** (2,695 m).

The **Eastern Ghats** are discontinuous, eroded, and lower, broken by major Peninsular rivers (Godavari, Krishna, Kaveri) that cut through them to reach the Bay of Bengal.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00136', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 9, 'What is the geological origin of the Deccan Plateau''s black soil region?', 'The Deccan Plateau was formed by extensive **volcanic (basaltic lava) eruptions** at the end of the **Cretaceous period**, creating the **Deccan Traps**.

Weathering of this basalt over time produced the **black (regur) soil**, which is rich in iron, magnesium, and moisture-retention capacity, making it ideal for **cotton cultivation**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00137', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 10, 'In which part of India is the Thar Desert located, and what is its key climatic feature?', 'The **Thar Desert** lies mainly in **Rajasthan** (extending into Gujarat, Punjab, and Haryana), to the west of the **Aravalli Range**.

It is a classic example of a **hot desert** with very low and erratic rainfall, high diurnal temperature range, and sparse vegetation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00138', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 11, 'How do the Andaman & Nicobar Islands differ geologically from the Lakshadweep Islands?', 'The **Andaman and Nicobar Islands** are the **submerged peaks of a volcanic mountain range** (an extension of the Arakan Yoma range of Myanmar), located in the Bay of Bengal.

The **Lakshadweep Islands**, in the Arabian Sea, are **coral-based (atoll)** formations built on a submerged plateau, and are much smaller in total area.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00139', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 12, 'What causes the Indian monsoon, in basic terms?', 'The monsoon arises mainly from the **differential heating of land and sea**: in summer, the Indian landmass heats up faster than the surrounding ocean, creating a **low-pressure zone** over the subcontinent that draws in moisture-laden winds from the **Indian Ocean**.

The seasonal shift of the **Inter-Tropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ)** northward, and the role of the **Tibetan Plateau** in creating upper-air circulation, further strengthen this inflow, which arrives as the **southwest monsoon**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00140', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 13, 'Through how many Indian states does the Tropic of Cancer pass?', 'The **Tropic of Cancer (23°30′ N)** passes through **eight Indian states**: **Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura**, and **Mizoram**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00141', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 14, 'What is the ''retreating'' or northeast monsoon, and which region receives its main rainfall from it?', 'The **retreating (northeast) monsoon** occurs from **October to December**, as the southwest monsoon withdraws and winds reverse to blow from land to sea, picking up moisture over the **Bay of Bengal**.

This brings the bulk of annual rainfall to **Tamil Nadu** and parts of coastal Andhra Pradesh, which otherwise lie in the rain-shadow of the southwest monsoon.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00142', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 15, 'How does the El Niño phenomenon typically affect the Indian monsoon?', '**El Niño** refers to the abnormal warming of surface waters in the **central and eastern equatorial Pacific Ocean**.

It is generally associated with a **weaker southwest monsoon and below-normal rainfall** in India, since it disrupts the normal pressure gradients that drive monsoon winds, though the correlation is not always exact.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00143', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 16, 'Which soil type covers the Indo-Gangetic plains and why is it considered highly fertile?', 'The **alluvial soil** covers the Indo-Gangetic plains, deposited by rivers like the Ganga, Yamuna, and Brahmaputra.

It is rich in **potash and lime** but often deficient in nitrogen and phosphorus; being fine-grained and easily workable, it supports intensive cultivation of **rice, wheat, and sugarcane**, and is divided into older **Bangar** and newer **Khadar** types.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00144', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 17, 'What is ''regur'' soil, where is it found, and what crop is it best suited for?', '**Regur (black soil)** is derived from **Deccan Trap basalt** and is found mainly across **Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Gujarat**, and parts of Andhra Pradesh and Karnataka.

It retains moisture well due to its high clay content, making it especially suited for **cotton cultivation**, hence it is also called ''black cotton soil''.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00145', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 18, 'Where is red soil predominantly found in India and what gives it its colour?', '**Red soil** is found over large parts of **Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh, Odisha, Chhattisgarh**, and parts of Jharkhand, developed on ancient **crystalline and metamorphic rocks**.

Its colour comes from a high concentration of **iron oxide (ferric oxide)**; it is generally less fertile than alluvial or black soil and responds well to fertilizers.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00146', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 19, 'How is laterite soil formed and in which regions is it typically found?', 'Laterite soil forms through **intense leaching** under conditions of **high rainfall and high temperature**, where silica is washed away leaving behind oxides of **iron and aluminium**.

It is found in high-rainfall plateau regions like parts of **Kerala, Karnataka (Western Ghats), Odisha**, and the northeastern states, and is generally poor in fertility but suitable for crops like cashew and tea after treatment.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00147', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 20, 'What are the main methods of soil conservation practised in India?', 'Common structural methods include **contour ploughing, terracing, and building contour/check bunds** to slow water runoff on slopes.

Vegetative methods include **afforestation, shelterbelts** (as in the Thar Desert), and **strip cropping**, while crop-based practices like **crop rotation** help maintain soil fertility and reduce erosion.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00148', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 21, 'Which states form the core of the Green Revolution belt in India, and what was its primary crop focus?', 'The Green Revolution, beginning in the mid-1960s, was concentrated mainly in **Punjab, Haryana**, and **western Uttar Pradesh**.

Its focus was on **high-yielding variety (HYV) seeds** of **wheat** (and later rice), supported by assured irrigation and chemical fertilizers, which sharply boosted foodgrain output in these states.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00149', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 22, 'What climatic and soil conditions favour rice cultivation in India?', 'Rice requires **high temperature (above 25°C), high humidity, and abundant rainfall (over 100 cm)** or assured irrigation, along with **clayey, water-retentive soil**.

It is therefore concentrated in the eastern and coastal states — **West Bengal, Uttar Pradesh, Punjab (irrigated), Andhra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu**, and the deltaic regions of major rivers.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00150', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 23, 'Which states are the leading wheat-producing regions of India?', 'Wheat, a **rabi crop**, requires moderate rainfall (50–75 cm) or irrigation and cool winters with a warm, dry period during ripening.

It is concentrated mainly in **Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, Haryana, Madhya Pradesh**, and Rajasthan, which together account for the bulk of national production.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00151', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 24, 'Which states lead in sugarcane production in India, and what growing conditions does it need?', 'Sugarcane needs **hot and humid climate** with temperatures of 21–27°C and rainfall of 75–150 cm (or irrigation).

**Uttar Pradesh** is the largest producer by area and output, followed by **Maharashtra**, with other significant producers including Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, and Bihar.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00152', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 25, 'What are the three main cropping seasons in India, and give one example crop of each.', '- **Kharif** (sown with onset of monsoon, June–July; harvested Sept–Oct): e.g., **rice, cotton, maize**
- **Rabi** (sown in winter, Oct–Dec; harvested March–April): e.g., **wheat, mustard, gram**
- **Zaid** (short summer season between Rabi and Kharif): e.g., **watermelon, cucumber, moong**', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00153', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 26, 'Which Indian states are the largest producers of tea, and what conditions does the crop require?', 'Tea requires a **warm, humid climate with well-distributed rainfall** and well-drained, slightly acidic soil on hill slopes.

**Assam** is India''s largest tea-producing state, followed by **West Bengal (Darjeeling and Dooars/Terai)**; other producers include Tamil Nadu (Nilgiris) and Kerala.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00154', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 27, 'What are the main sources of irrigation in India?', 'The principal sources are **canals** (fed by rivers or reservoirs, important in the Indo-Gangetic plains and Punjab-Haryana), **wells and tube wells** (the largest source overall, especially in groundwater-rich alluvial areas), and **tanks** (important in the Peninsular plateau, especially Tamil Nadu and Andhra Pradesh).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00155', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 28, 'Which state holds the largest reserves of iron ore in India?', '**Odisha** holds the largest iron ore reserves in India, followed by **Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, and Karnataka**.

Key mining regions include the **Bonai-Keonjhar-Mayurbhanj belt** in Odisha and the **Bailadila range** in Chhattisgarh.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00156', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 29, 'Which state has the largest coal reserves in India, and what are the major coal-bearing basins?', '**Jharkhand** has the largest coal reserves in India, with major coalfields like **Jharia and Bokaro**, closely followed by **Odisha and Chhattisgarh**.

Most of India''s coal occurs in **Gondwana-age rock formations**, roughly 250 million years old, found mainly in the Damodar Valley and the Mahanadi, Godavari, and Son river valleys.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00157', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 30, 'Where are India''s major petroleum-producing regions located?', 'Offshore fields like **Bombay High** in the Arabian Sea are India''s largest producer, supplemented by onshore fields in **Gujarat (Ankleshwar)** and **Assam (Digboi, Naharkatiya)**, where India''s oldest oil well was drilled.

Newer offshore finds in the **Krishna-Godavari basin** off Andhra Pradesh also contribute to national output.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00158', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 31, 'Why does India''s hydroelectric potential remain concentrated in the Himalayan river systems?', 'Himalayan rivers are **perennial** with a steep gradient and large, continuous water flow even in the dry season, unlike seasonal Peninsular rivers.

This combination of **high, reliable discharge and steep fall** makes states like Himachal Pradesh, Uttarakhand, Jammu & Kashmir, and Arunachal Pradesh prime locations for hydroelectric projects.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00159', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 32, 'Where are India''s main uranium and monazite (thorium) deposits found?', '**Uranium** is mined mainly from the **Jaduguda mines in Jharkhand** (Singhbhum region), with newer deposits found in Andhra Pradesh (Tummalapalle) and Meghalaya.

**Monazite sands**, a source of thorium, are found mainly along the **coastal beaches of Kerala** (Chavara) and parts of Odisha and Tamil Nadu.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00160', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 33, 'Which Indian state has the highest solar power potential and installed solar capacity?', '**Rajasthan** has the highest solar power potential in India due to its vast arid land, clear skies, and high solar insolation, and also leads in installed solar capacity, with large solar parks such as **Bhadla Solar Park**.

Other leading solar states include Gujarat, Karnataka, and Tamil Nadu.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00161', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 34, 'Where are India''s tropical evergreen forests found, and what is their main characteristic?', 'Tropical evergreen forests grow in areas receiving **over 200 cm of rainfall annually**, mainly along the **Western Ghats, the northeastern states, and the Andaman & Nicobar Islands**.

They are characterised by dense, multi-layered canopies of broad-leaved trees that remain green throughout the year, since no single dry season is long enough to cause leaf shedding.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00162', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 35, 'What is India''s most widespread forest type, and where is it found?', '**Tropical deciduous (monsoon) forests** are the most widespread forest type in India, found across a large belt covering parts of the Indo-Gangetic plain''s fringes, the Peninsular plateau, and the Shiwaliks.

Trees such as **teak and sal** shed their leaves for about six to eight weeks in the dry season, and the forests are classified into moist and dry deciduous types based on rainfall.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00163', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 36, 'Where are India''s mangrove forests concentrated, and name the largest mangrove region.', 'Mangrove forests grow in **tidal, saline coastal and deltaic areas**, particularly in the **Sundarbans delta of West Bengal** (shared with Bangladesh), which is the **largest mangrove forest in the world**.

Other notable mangrove areas include the Mahanadi, Godavari, and Krishna deltas, and the Andaman & Nicobar coastline.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00164', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 37, 'According to Forest Survey of India assessments, which state typically has the largest forest cover in absolute area?', '**Madhya Pradesh** consistently has the largest forest cover in absolute area among Indian states, as reported in successive **India State of Forest Reports**.

However, in terms of **percentage of geographical area** under forest cover, northeastern states like **Mizoram** rank highest.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00165', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 38, 'What target for forest cover was set under India''s National Forest Policy, 1988?', 'The **National Forest Policy, 1988** set a target of bringing **33% of India''s total geographical area** under forest or tree cover (with a higher target of 60% for hill and mountainous regions), primarily for ecological stability rather than commercial exploitation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00166', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 39, 'What were India''s key demographic indicators as per the 2011 Census?', 'India''s population in 2011 stood at approximately **121.08 crore**, making it the world''s second most populous country at the time.

The **sex ratio** was **943 females per 1,000 males**, and the **literacy rate** was **74.04%**, with Kerala recording the highest literacy among states.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00167', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 40, 'Which Indian state/UT had the highest and lowest population density as per the 2011 Census?', '**Bihar** recorded the highest population density among states at **1,102 persons per sq km**, while among Union Territories, **Delhi** had an extremely high density.

At the other end, **Arunachal Pradesh** had the lowest population density among states, reflecting its mountainous terrain and low urbanisation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00168', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 41, 'What is meant by India''s ''demographic dividend''?', 'The **demographic dividend** refers to the economic growth potential arising when the proportion of the **working-age population (15–64 years)** is larger than the dependent population (children and elderly).

India is projected to have one of the youngest populations globally for the next few decades, but realising this dividend depends on adequate **employment generation, skilling, and health/education investment**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00169', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 42, 'What are the seven continents and five oceans of the world, in descending order of area?', '- Continents (largest to smallest): **Asia, Africa, North America, South America, Antarctica, Europe, Australia**
- Oceans (largest to smallest): **Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern (Antarctic), Arctic**', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00170', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 43, 'Which river is considered the longest in the world, and which carries the greatest volume of water?', 'The **Nile** (about 6,650 km) is conventionally regarded as the world''s longest river, flowing through northeastern Africa into the Mediterranean Sea, though some recent studies argue the **Amazon** is comparably long or longer depending on measurement method.

The **Amazon**, in South America, unquestionably carries the **largest volume (discharge) of water** of any river in the world.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00171', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 44, 'Which is the world''s highest mountain peak, and where is it located?', '**Mount Everest** (8,848.86 m, per the 2020 China-Nepal joint survey) is the world''s highest peak, located in the **Mahalangur Himal** section of the Himalayas on the **Nepal-China (Tibet) border**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00172', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 45, 'Which is the largest hot desert in the world, and which is the largest desert overall?', 'The **Sahara Desert**, spanning much of North Africa, is the world''s **largest hot desert**.

However, by the broader climatological definition of a desert (a region of very low precipitation), the **Antarctic Desert** is actually the **largest desert in the world overall**, followed by the Arctic Desert.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00173', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 46, 'What is the ''Ring of Fire'', and why is it significant?', 'The **Ring of Fire** is a horseshoe-shaped belt around the **Pacific Ocean**, stretching from South America through North America, across to East Asia and down to New Zealand.

It is significant because roughly **75% of the world''s active and dormant volcanoes** and a very high share of global earthquakes occur along it, due to the presence of numerous **tectonic plate boundaries (subduction zones)**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00174', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 47, 'Where is the Great Barrier Reef located, and what is it composed of?', 'The **Great Barrier Reef** lies off the northeastern coast of **Australia**, in the Coral Sea, and is the **world''s largest coral reef system**.

It is built up of **coral polyps (calcium carbonate skeletons)** and is visible even from outer space, though it faces serious threats from coral bleaching linked to rising sea temperatures.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00175', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 48, 'In which countries does the Amazon rainforest mainly lie?', 'The **Amazon rainforest**, the world''s largest tropical rainforest, lies predominantly in **Brazil**, with significant portions also in **Peru, Colombia**, and smaller parts in Ecuador, Bolivia, Venezuela, Guyana, Suriname, and French Guiana.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00176', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 49, 'What are the key characteristics of an equatorial climate?', 'Equatorial climate, found roughly between **5° N and 5° S latitude** (e.g., the Amazon and Congo basins, and Indonesia), is marked by **uniformly high temperatures throughout the year (around 27°C)** and **heavy rainfall in all months**, with no distinct dry season.

This supports dense, multi-layered tropical rainforest vegetation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00177', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 50, 'Where is the Mediterranean type of climate found, and what is its seasonal rainfall pattern?', 'The **Mediterranean climate** is found around the Mediterranean Sea basin and in similar mid-latitude west-coast locations like **California, central Chile, South Africa''s Cape region, and southwestern Australia**.

It is characterised by **hot, dry summers and mild, wet winters**, the reverse of the monsoon rainfall pattern.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00178', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 51, 'What distinguishes a tundra climate, and where is it typically found?', 'The **tundra climate** occurs in high-latitude regions near the Arctic Circle (e.g., northern Canada, Alaska, Siberia, northern Scandinavia).

It features **very short, cool summers and long, severely cold winters**, with the ground remaining frozen as **permafrost** for most of the year, supporting only low vegetation like mosses, lichens, and small shrubs.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00179', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 52, 'Which two seas does the Suez Canal connect, and why is it strategically important?', 'The **Suez Canal**, located in Egypt, connects the **Mediterranean Sea** with the **Red Sea**.

It is strategically vital as it allows ships travelling between Europe and Asia to avoid the much longer route around the **Cape of Good Hope**, making it one of the world''s busiest shipping lanes.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00180', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 53, 'Which two oceans does the Panama Canal connect?', 'The **Panama Canal**, located in Central America, connects the **Atlantic Ocean** and the **Pacific Ocean**, cutting across the **Isthmus of Panama** and drastically shortening the sea route between the east and west coasts of the Americas.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00181', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 54, 'Which two water bodies does the Strait of Malacca connect, and between which countries does it lie?', 'The **Strait of Malacca** connects the **Andaman Sea (Indian Ocean)** with the **South China Sea (Pacific Ocean)**.

It lies between the **Malay Peninsula (Malaysia)** and the island of **Sumatra (Indonesia)**, and is one of the world''s most important shipping routes for energy and trade moving between the Indian Ocean and East Asia.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00182', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 55, 'What does the Palk Strait separate, and what water body lies south of it connecting the same two landmasses?', 'The **Palk Strait** lies between **India (Tamil Nadu)** and **Sri Lanka**, connecting the Palk Bay with the Bay of Bengal.

Further south, the **Gulf of Mannar** (with the Adam''s Bridge/Rama Setu chain of shoals in between) connects the same two countries'' coastlines toward the Indian Ocean.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00183', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 56, 'What does the Ten Degree Channel separate?', 'The **Ten Degree Channel** separates the **Andaman Islands** (to the north) from the **Nicobar Islands** (to the south), named for its location along the 10° N latitude line.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00184', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 57, 'Which countries border the Strait of Hormuz, and why is it globally significant?', 'The **Strait of Hormuz** lies between **Iran** (north) and the **United Arab Emirates/Oman** (Musandam Peninsula, south), connecting the **Persian Gulf** to the **Gulf of Oman** and the Arabian Sea.

It is one of the world''s most strategically important **oil transit chokepoints**, as a large share of global seaborne crude oil exports passes through it.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00185', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 58, 'What does the Bosphorus Strait separate, and which two seas does it connect?', 'The **Bosphorus Strait** runs through **Istanbul, Turkey**, separating the **European and Asian parts of Turkey** (and of the Eurasian continent).

It connects the **Black Sea** to the **Sea of Marmara**, which in turn connects to the Mediterranean via the Dardanelles.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00186', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 59, 'Which two landmasses does the Strait of Gibraltar separate, and which water bodies does it connect?', 'The **Strait of Gibraltar** separates **Spain (Europe)** from **Morocco (Africa)**.

It connects the **Atlantic Ocean** with the **Mediterranean Sea** and is only about 13 km wide at its narrowest point.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00187', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 60, 'Where is the Atacama Desert located, and what is distinctive about it?', 'The **Atacama Desert** lies along the Pacific coast of **Chile**, in South America, between the Andes and the Pacific Ocean.

It is considered one of the **driest places on Earth**, with some weather stations having never recorded measurable rainfall, due to the cold **Humboldt (Peru) ocean current** and a rain-shadow effect from the Andes.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00188', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Geography (Indian & World)', 2, 61, 'What is the difference between the Konkan coast and the Coromandel coast of India?', 'The **Konkan coast** lies along the **western coast** of India (Maharashtra-Goa-Karnataka stretch), characterised by a narrow coastal plain, estuaries, and the steep Western Ghats rising close to the shore.

The **Coromandel coast** lies along the **southeastern coast** (Tamil Nadu-Andhra Pradesh), broader and marked by large river deltas like those of the Krishna, Godavari, and Kaveri.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00189', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 0, 'What economic model did India''s First Five-Year Plan (1951–56) adopt, and what was its priority sector?', 'India''s First Five-Year Plan (1951–56) was based largely on the **Harrod-Domar growth model**, which linked the rate of economic growth to the levels of saving and investment.

The plan gave primary importance to **agriculture**, including irrigation and power projects, since the economy was recovering from Partition and food shortages.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00190', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 1, 'When was the Planning Commission established and when was it dissolved?', 'The **Planning Commission** was set up in **1950** by a Cabinet Resolution (an extra-constitutional, non-statutory body) to formulate India''s Five-Year Plans.

It was dissolved in **2014** and replaced by **NITI Aayog**, which began functioning from **1 January 2015**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00191', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 2, 'What does NITI Aayog stand for, and how does its role differ from that of the Planning Commission?', 'NITI Aayog stands for the **National Institution for Transforming India**.

Unlike the Planning Commission, which allocated plan funds to states and prepared centralized Five-Year Plans, NITI Aayog functions as a **think tank** that provides policy advice and fosters **cooperative and competitive federalism**, without the power to allocate funds to ministries or states.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00192', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 3, 'What is a "Rolling Plan," and which government introduced it in India?', 'A **Rolling Plan** is a planning approach in which a new plan is formulated every year, taking into account the achievements and shortfalls of the previous year, rather than fixing a rigid plan period in advance.

It was introduced in India by the **Janata Party government in 1978**, replacing the Fifth Five-Year Plan, and was later discontinued when the Sixth Five-Year Plan (1980–85) was reinstated by the Congress government.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00193', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 4, 'What was the "Bombay Plan" of 1944?', 'The **Bombay Plan** (1944) was a blueprint for India''s post-independence economic development, drafted by a group of leading Indian industrialists including **J.R.D. Tata and G.D. Birla**.

It advocated a significant role for **state intervention and planning** alongside private enterprise, and influenced the mixed-economy approach adopted after independence.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00194', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 5, 'Who is the ex-officio Chairperson of NITI Aayog?', 'The **Prime Minister of India** serves as the ex-officio Chairperson of NITI Aayog.

The governing council of NITI Aayog comprises all **state Chief Ministers and Lieutenant Governors of Union Territories**, reflecting its cooperative-federalism design.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00195', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 6, 'Differentiate between GDP and GNP.', '**Gross Domestic Product (GDP)** measures the total market value of all final goods and services produced **within the geographical boundaries of a country** in a given year, regardless of who owns the factors of production.

**Gross National Product (GNP)** equals GDP plus **net factor income from abroad** (income earned by residents abroad minus income earned by non-residents within the country).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00196', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 7, 'What is Net Domestic Product (NDP), and how is it derived from GDP?', '**Net Domestic Product (NDP)** is obtained by subtracting **depreciation (consumption of fixed capital)** from GDP.

It reflects the actual addition to the wealth of the nation during a year, since depreciation merely replaces worn-out capital rather than adding new value.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00197', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 8, 'What is the difference between NNP at market price and National Income (NNP at factor cost)?', '**NNP at market price** is Net National Product valued at the prices actually paid by consumers, which include indirect taxes and exclude subsidies.

**National Income (NNP at factor cost)** adjusts this by **subtracting net indirect taxes** (indirect taxes minus subsidies), giving the income actually accruing to factors of production such as wages, rent, interest, and profit.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00198', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 9, 'What is the current base year used for India''s GDP estimation, and which organisation releases these estimates?', 'India''s national income estimates currently use **2011–12** as the base year for GDP calculation.

These estimates are released by the **National Statistical Office (NSO)**, under the **Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MoSPI)**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00199', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 10, 'What is the "GDP deflator," and how does it differ from CPI?', 'The **GDP deflator** is the ratio of nominal GDP to real GDP, used to measure the overall price level change across **all goods and services produced in the economy**, not just a fixed basket.

Unlike the **Consumer Price Index (CPI)**, which tracks prices of a fixed basket of goods and services consumed by households, the GDP deflator automatically adjusts its basket every year to reflect current production patterns.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00200', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 11, 'Under which constitutional provision is the Union Budget presented, and what is its formal name?', 'The Union Budget is presented under **Article 112** of the Constitution, where it is formally called the **"Annual Financial Statement"** — a statement of the estimated receipts and expenditure of the Government of India for a financial year.

It must be laid before **both Houses of Parliament**, and the Lok Sabha alone has the power to vote on the Demands for Grants.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00201', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 12, 'Define fiscal deficit and explain what it indicates.', '**Fiscal deficit** is the difference between the government''s **total expenditure** and its **total receipts excluding borrowings** in a financial year.

It indicates the total borrowing requirement of the government, reflecting the extent to which the government must borrow to finance its expenditure.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00202', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 13, 'What is a revenue deficit, and how is it different from a fiscal deficit?', 'A **revenue deficit** occurs when **revenue expenditure exceeds revenue receipts**, indicating that the government is unable to meet its routine running expenses from its current income.

While revenue deficit relates only to the revenue account, **fiscal deficit** covers the overall gap including capital expenditure, making fiscal deficit a broader measure of the government''s total borrowing need.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00203', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 14, 'What is "primary deficit"?', '**Primary deficit** is the fiscal deficit minus **interest payments** on previous borrowings.

It shows the government''s current borrowing requirement **excluding the burden of past debt**, helping assess the sustainability of ongoing fiscal policy.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00204', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 15, 'When was the FRBM Act enacted, and what was its primary objective?', 'The **Fiscal Responsibility and Budget Management (FRBM) Act** was enacted in **2003** and came into force in **2004**.

Its primary objective was to ensure **inter-generational equity in fiscal management** by mandating fiscal discipline, reducing fiscal and revenue deficits, and improving transparency in government finances, with deficit targets subsequently revised through amendments including in 2018.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00205', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 16, 'What are the three types of funds operated by the Government of India under the Constitution?', '- **Consolidated Fund of India** (Article 266) — holds all government revenues, loans raised, and repayments; no money can be withdrawn without parliamentary authorization.
- **Contingency Fund of India** (Article 267) — a fund at the disposal of the President to meet unforeseen expenditure, pending parliamentary approval.
- **Public Account of India** (Article 266) — holds money like provident funds and small savings, where the government acts as a banker.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00206', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 17, 'When was the Goods and Services Tax (GST) launched in India, and under which constitutional amendment?', '**GST** was launched on **1 July 2017**, through the **101st Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016**.

It subsumed a host of indirect taxes like excise duty, service tax, and VAT into a unified **"one nation, one tax"** regime.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00207', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 18, 'What is the composition of the GST Council, and who chairs it?', 'The **GST Council**, established under **Article 279A**, is chaired by the **Union Finance Minister**, with the Union Minister of State for Finance and the Finance Ministers of all states as members.

It recommends rates, exemptions, and administrative matters related to GST, with decisions historically taken by consensus, though the Act also prescribes a weighted voting mechanism.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00208', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 19, 'Differentiate between CGST, SGST, and IGST.', '**CGST (Central GST)** and **SGST (State GST)** are levied simultaneously on **intra-state supplies** of goods and services, collected by the Centre and the respective state respectively.

**IGST (Integrated GST)** is levied on **inter-state supplies** and imports, collected by the Centre and then apportioned between the Centre and the destination state.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00209', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 20, 'Give examples distinguishing direct taxes from indirect taxes.', '**Direct taxes** are levied directly on the income or wealth of a person and cannot be shifted to another party — examples include **Income Tax** and **Corporate Tax**.

**Indirect taxes** are levied on goods and services and can be shifted from the seller to the buyer — examples include **GST** and **Customs Duty**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00210', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 21, 'Which body administers direct taxes in India, and under which Act is income tax levied?', 'Direct taxes in India are administered by the **Central Board of Direct Taxes (CBDT)**, a statutory authority functioning under the **Department of Revenue, Ministry of Finance**.

Income tax is levied under the **Income Tax Act, 1961**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00211', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 22, 'What is "Corporation Tax," and who collects it?', '**Corporation Tax** is a direct tax levied on the **net income or profits of companies**, both domestic and foreign, operating in India.

It is collected by the **Central Government** through the **Central Board of Direct Taxes (CBDT)**, and ranks among the largest sources of direct tax revenue.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00212', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 23, 'What is Customs Duty, and which authority administers it in India?', '**Customs Duty** is an indirect tax levied on the **import and export of goods** across India''s borders, governed primarily by the **Customs Act, 1962**.

It is administered by the **Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs (CBIC)**, and serves both as a revenue source and as a tool for protecting domestic industry.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00213', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 24, 'When was the Reserve Bank of India established, and when was it nationalised?', 'The **Reserve Bank of India (RBI)** was established on **1 April 1935** under the **RBI Act, 1934**, originally as a privately owned institution.

It was **nationalised on 1 January 1949**, making it fully government-owned, and it functions as India''s central bank.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00214', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 25, 'What are the key functions of the RBI?', '- **Issuer of currency** — sole authority to issue currency notes (except one-rupee notes/coins, issued by the Government of India).
- **Banker to the government** — manages the banking needs of the Union and state governments.
- **Banker''s bank and lender of last resort** — regulates and supports commercial banks, especially during liquidity crises.
- **Regulator of monetary policy and foreign exchange** — manages inflation, money supply, and forex reserves.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00215', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 26, 'What is the Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR)?', '**Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR)** is the minimum percentage of a bank''s **net demand and time liabilities (NDTL)** that it must maintain as **cash reserves with the RBI**, in liquid cash form (not earning interest).

Raising the CRR reduces the lendable funds available with banks, thereby tightening liquidity in the economy.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00216', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 27, 'What is the Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR)?', '**Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR)** is the minimum percentage of a bank''s net demand and time liabilities that must be maintained in the form of **liquid assets** such as cash, gold, or approved government securities.

Unlike CRR, SLR funds are held by the bank itself (not with the RBI) and can earn returns, while also helping the government raise funds through mandated investment in government securities.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00217', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 28, 'Define "repo rate" and "reverse repo rate."', 'The **repo rate** is the rate at which the RBI lends short-term funds to commercial banks against government securities; raising it makes borrowing costlier and helps control inflation.

The **reverse repo rate** is the rate at which the RBI borrows funds from commercial banks, absorbing excess liquidity from the banking system.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00218', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 29, 'What is the composition of the Monetary Policy Committee (MPC), and when was it constituted?', 'The **Monetary Policy Committee (MPC)** was constituted following the **2016 amendment to the RBI Act, 1934**, which established a statutory inflation-targeting framework.

It comprises **six members** — the **RBI Governor** (Chairperson), two other RBI officials, and **three external members** appointed by the Central Government — mandated to set the policy repo rate to keep CPI inflation at a target (**4%, with a tolerance band of +/-2%**) set by the Government in consultation with the RBI.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00219', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 30, 'When was NABARD established, and what is its mandate?', '**NABARD (National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development)** was established on **12 July 1982**, based on the recommendations of the **B. Sivaraman Committee**.

It serves as the apex development bank for **agriculture and rural development**, providing refinance to banks and cooperative institutions and overseeing rural credit planning.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00220', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 31, 'What is "Open Market Operations (OMO)" as a monetary policy tool?', '**Open Market Operations (OMO)** refer to the **RBI''s buying and selling of government securities** in the open market to regulate liquidity in the banking system.

When the RBI sells securities, it absorbs liquidity from the system; when it buys securities, it injects liquidity, thereby influencing money supply and interest rates.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00221', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 32, 'What is the Wholesale Price Index (WPI), and who releases it?', 'The **Wholesale Price Index (WPI)** measures the average change in prices of goods **at the wholesale/producer level**, before they reach retail consumers, and does not include services.

It is released by the **Office of the Economic Adviser, Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT)**, with the base year recently revised from **2011–12 to 2022–23**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00222', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 33, 'What is the Consumer Price Index (CPI), and why is it significant for monetary policy?', 'The **Consumer Price Index (CPI)** measures the average change in retail prices paid by **end consumers** for a fixed basket of goods and services.

It is significant because the RBI''s **Monetary Policy Committee uses CPI (Combined) inflation**, not WPI, as its formal inflation-targeting benchmark; CPI''s base year has also undergone periodic revision by MoSPI.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00223', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 34, 'Distinguish between demand-pull and cost-push inflation.', '**Demand-pull inflation** occurs when aggregate demand in the economy **exceeds aggregate supply**, pulling prices upward — often linked to excess money supply or rising incomes.

**Cost-push inflation** occurs when the **cost of production rises** (e.g., due to higher input or wage costs), forcing producers to raise prices even without a corresponding rise in demand.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00224', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 35, 'What is "stagflation"?', '**Stagflation** is an unusual economic condition characterized by the simultaneous occurrence of **stagnant economic growth, high unemployment, and high inflation**.

It challenges conventional economic theory, since inflation and unemployment are typically expected to move in opposite directions (as per the Phillips Curve).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00225', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 36, 'What is "deflation," and why is it generally considered harmful?', '**Deflation** refers to a sustained **decline in the general price level** of goods and services in an economy, i.e., negative inflation.

It is considered harmful because falling prices can discourage current spending and investment (as consumers delay purchases expecting further price falls), potentially triggering a recessionary spiral.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00226', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 37, 'Which two committees are most associated with defining India''s poverty line in recent decades?', 'The **Tendulkar Committee (2009)** redefined the poverty line based on Mixed Reference Period consumption, moving away from the earlier calorie-based norm and incorporating expenditure on health and education.

The **Rangarajan Committee (2014)** subsequently proposed a revised poverty line, suggesting separate rural and urban consumption expenditure thresholds, though its recommendations were not formally adopted as the official poverty line.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00227', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 38, 'What is "disguised unemployment"?', '**Disguised unemployment** occurs when more people are engaged in an activity (typically agriculture) than are actually needed, such that removing some workers would **not reduce total output**.

It is common in the Indian agricultural sector, where family labour is often underutilized but not formally counted as unemployed.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00228', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 39, 'Differentiate between seasonal and structural unemployment.', '**Seasonal unemployment** arises when workers (e.g., in agriculture) are without work during certain months of the year due to the **seasonal nature of economic activity**.

**Structural unemployment** arises from a **mismatch between workers'' skills and the requirements of available jobs**, often due to technological change or shifts in industry structure.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00229', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 40, 'What is the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS)?', 'The **Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS)**, launched by the **National Statistical Office (NSO)** in **2017**, is India''s primary survey for measuring employment and unemployment indicators on a regular basis.

It replaced the earlier quinquennial employment-unemployment surveys of the **NSSO**, providing annual rural and quarterly urban estimates of labour force indicators.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00230', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 41, 'What do the terms "Usual Status," "Weekly Status," and "Daily Status" refer to in unemployment measurement?', 'These are different **reference periods** used by Indian labour surveys to estimate unemployment.

**Usual Status** considers a person''s activity over the **preceding 365 days**, **Current Weekly Status** considers activity during the **preceding 7 days**, and **Current Daily Status** measures activity on each day of the preceding week, offering progressively more granular pictures of underemployment.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00231', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 42, 'What is Minimum Support Price (MSP), and which body recommends it?', '**Minimum Support Price (MSP)** is the price at which the government guarantees to purchase specified agricultural crops from farmers, acting as a **price floor** to protect them from distress sales during bumper harvests.

It is recommended by the **Commission for Agricultural Costs and Prices (CACP)** and approved by the **Cabinet Committee on Economic Affairs (CCEA)**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00232', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 43, 'What is the Public Distribution System (PDS), and which Act expanded its legal entitlement basis?', 'The **Public Distribution System (PDS)** is a government-run system for distributing subsidised food grains (mainly rice and wheat) and other essentials to the poor through a network of **Fair Price Shops**.

It was given a statutory, rights-based foundation through the **National Food Security Act (NFSA), 2013**, which entitles eligible households to subsidised food grains.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00233', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 44, 'What was the "Green Revolution," and who is considered its chief architect in India?', 'The **Green Revolution** refers to the significant increase in foodgrain production, especially wheat and rice, achieved from the **mid-1960s** through high-yielding variety (HYV) seeds, irrigation, and fertilizers.

**M.S. Swaminathan** is widely regarded as the chief architect of the Green Revolution in India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00234', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 45, 'What were the two major categories of land reform measures undertaken after independence?', '- **Abolition of intermediaries** — ending the zamindari and similar landlord systems to establish a direct relationship between the state and cultivators.
- **Land ceiling and tenancy reforms** — fixing an upper limit on land holdings and regulating tenancy terms to protect tenant cultivators and redistribute surplus land.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00235', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 46, 'What is the APMC Act, and why has it been a subject of reform debate?', 'The **Agricultural Produce Market Committee (APMC) Act** is state legislation requiring farmers to sell their produce through regulated wholesale markets (mandis), intended to protect farmers from exploitation by intermediaries.

It has been a subject of reform debate because APMCs are often criticized for creating **monopolistic market yards and cartelization**, prompting central efforts (such as the now-repealed 2020 farm laws) to allow farmers greater freedom to sell outside mandis.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00236', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 47, 'What is e-NAM?', '**e-NAM (National Agriculture Market)**, launched in **2016**, is a **pan-India electronic trading portal** that networks existing APMC mandis to create a unified national market for agricultural commodities.

It aims to enable better price discovery and reduce information asymmetry for farmers by allowing online trading across integrated mandis.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00237', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 48, 'What was the significance of the Industrial Policy Resolution, 1956?', 'The **Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956** classified industries into three categories (exclusively state-run, state-dominant with private participation, and private-sector-open), establishing the **public sector''s dominant role** in India''s industrial development.

It is often referred to as the **"Economic Constitution of India"** for shaping industrial strategy for decades under the mixed-economy model.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00238', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 49, 'What were the "LPG reforms" of 1991?', 'The **LPG reforms** refer to the economic reforms of **1991** — **Liberalization, Privatization, and Globalization** — undertaken in response to a severe balance of payments crisis.

They dismantled the **License-Permit Raj**, reduced import tariffs, opened sectors to private and foreign investment, and integrated India more closely with the global economy.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00239', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 50, 'What is "disinvestment," and which body currently oversees it?', '**Disinvestment** refers to the sale or liquidation of government equity/stake in **Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs)**, undertaken to raise revenue and improve efficiency.

Disinvestment policy is currently handled by the **Department of Investment and Public Asset Management (DIPAM)** under the Ministry of Finance.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00240', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 51, 'How are Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) classified in India?', 'MSMEs in India are classified under the **MSME Development Act** based on **investment in plant and machinery/equipment and annual turnover**, with separate thresholds for micro, small, and medium categories, revised in **2020** to use a composite criterion combining both investment and turnover.

This revised composite classification replaced the earlier system that classified manufacturing and service enterprises separately and only by investment.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00241', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 52, 'What is the Balance of Payments (BoP), and what are its two main components?', 'The **Balance of Payments (BoP)** is a systematic record of all economic transactions between residents of a country and the rest of the world during a given period.

Its two main components are the **Current Account** (trade in goods/services, income, and transfers) and the **Capital Account** (capital transfers and changes in financial assets/liabilities such as investments and loans).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00242', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 53, 'Differentiate between FDI and FPI.', '**Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)** involves a long-term stake and **controlling interest** in a foreign enterprise, typically accompanied by management involvement and technology transfer.

**Foreign Portfolio Investment (FPI)** involves investment in financial assets like **stocks and bonds** without seeking managerial control, and is generally more short-term and volatile in nature.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00243', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 54, 'What constitutes India''s foreign exchange reserves?', 'India''s **foreign exchange reserves**, managed by the RBI, comprise four components: **Foreign Currency Assets (FCA)**, **Gold reserves**, **Special Drawing Rights (SDRs)**, and the **Reserve Tranche Position (RTP)** with the IMF.

Foreign Currency Assets form the largest component, held mainly in major reserve currencies like the US dollar.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00244', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 55, 'What is meant by "current account convertibility" of the rupee, and has India achieved it?', '**Current account convertibility** means a currency can be freely converted into foreign currency for **trade-related transactions** (imports, exports, remittances) without government restriction.

India achieved **full current account convertibility in 1994**, following recommendations of committees in the post-1991 reform era, though **capital account convertibility remains only partial**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00245', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 56, 'What are Special Drawing Rights (SDRs)?', '**Special Drawing Rights (SDRs)** are an international reserve asset created by the **International Monetary Fund (IMF)** in **1969** to supplement member countries'' official reserves.

The value of the SDR is based on a basket of major international currencies, and SDRs can be exchanged among member countries for freely usable currencies.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00246', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 57, 'What is a "trade deficit," and how is it different from a current account deficit?', 'A **trade deficit** occurs when the value of a country''s **merchandise imports exceeds its exports** of goods.

A **current account deficit (CAD)** is a broader measure that includes trade in goods and services plus net income and transfers; a country can have a trade deficit while a surplus in services (like India''s IT exports) partly offsets it in the current account.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00247', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 58, 'When was SEBI established, and when did it get statutory powers?', 'The **Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI)** was initially set up in **1988** as a non-statutory body.

It was given **statutory powers in 1992** through the **SEBI Act, 1992**, becoming the primary regulator of India''s securities markets.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00248', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 59, 'What are the main functions of SEBI?', '- **Protecting investor interests** in the securities markets.
- **Regulating** the business of stock exchanges and other securities markets.
- **Registering and regulating intermediaries** such as brokers, merchant bankers, and mutual funds.
- **Promoting and monitoring** self-regulatory organizations and preventing fraudulent or unfair trade practices.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00249', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 60, 'Name India''s two major stock exchanges and note a key fact about each.', 'The **Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE)**, established in **1875**, is **Asia''s oldest stock exchange**.

The **National Stock Exchange (NSE)**, established in **1992**, introduced **fully automated electronic/screen-based trading** to India and is now the country''s largest exchange by trading volume.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00250', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 61, 'Under which regulations are mutual funds governed in India, and who regulates them?', 'Mutual funds in India are regulated by the **Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI)** under the **SEBI (Mutual Funds) Regulations, 1996**.

The industry''s self-regulatory body, the **Association of Mutual Funds in India (AMFI)**, works alongside SEBI to promote investor awareness and healthy market practices.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00251', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Indian Economy', 3, 62, 'What is the role of Credit Rating Agencies (CRAs), and name two operating in India.', '**Credit Rating Agencies** assess the **creditworthiness of borrowers** — including companies and debt instruments — assigning ratings that help investors gauge the risk of default.

Prominent CRAs registered with SEBI and operating in India include **CRISIL** and **ICRA**, among others such as CARE and India Ratings.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00252', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 0, 'What is a trophic level in an ecosystem?', 'A **trophic level** is the position an organism occupies in a food chain based on its feeding relationship, starting with **producers** at the first level, followed by **primary consumers** (herbivores), **secondary consumers** (carnivores/omnivores), and **tertiary consumers** (top predators).

Energy flows unidirectionally through these levels, while matter cycles through decomposers back to producers.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00253', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 1, 'What is the "ten percent law" of energy transfer in a food chain?', 'The **ten percent law**, proposed by **Raymond Lindeman**, states that only about **10%** of the energy available at one trophic level is transferred to the next, with the remaining **90%** lost as heat through respiration and metabolic activities.

This explains why food chains are rarely longer than **four to five trophic levels** and why the biomass pyramid typically narrows upward.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00254', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 2, 'Who are the "producers" in an ecosystem?', '**Producers**, or **autotrophs**, are organisms that synthesize their own food from inorganic substances, mainly through **photosynthesis** (green plants, algae, cyanobacteria) or **chemosynthesis** (certain bacteria).

They form the base of every food chain and are the only point at which solar or chemical energy enters the biological system.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00255', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 3, 'What is a biome, and name the major biomes found in India?', 'A **biome** is a large-scale ecological community of plants and animals shaped by regional **climate, soil, and rainfall patterns** over a geographic area.

India spans several biomes, including **tropical rainforests** (Western Ghats, Northeast), **tropical deciduous forests**, **thorn/scrub forests** (Rajasthan, Deccan), **montane/alpine biomes** (Himalaya), **mangrove ecosystems** (Sundarbans), and **desert biomes** (Thar).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00256', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 4, 'What is an ecotone, and what is meant by the "edge effect"?', 'An **ecotone** is a transitional zone between two distinct ecosystems or biological communities, such as the boundary between a forest and a grassland.

The **edge effect** refers to the tendency of ecotones to have **greater species density and diversity** than either adjoining community, because they contain species from both habitats plus organisms unique to the transition zone itself.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00257', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 5, 'What is a keystone species? Give an example.', 'A **keystone species** is one whose impact on its ecosystem is **disproportionately large relative to its population size**, such that its removal would drastically alter or collapse the ecosystem''s structure.

The **sea otter** (which controls sea urchin populations to protect kelp forests) and the **tiger** (as an apex predator regulating herbivore populations in Indian forests) are classic examples.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00258', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 6, 'What are biodiversity hotspots, and who defined the concept?', 'A **biodiversity hotspot** is a biogeographic region with a significant reservoir of **endemic species** that is simultaneously experiencing **exceptional habitat loss**.

The concept was introduced by British ecologist **Norman Myers in 1988**; a region qualifies if it has at least **1,500 endemic vascular plant species** and has lost **70% or more** of its original habitat.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00259', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 7, 'Which biodiversity hotspots are found wholly or partly in India?', 'India contains parts of **four global biodiversity hotspots**:

- **Himalaya** (Eastern Himalayan region)
- **Indo-Burma** (Northeast India)
- **Western Ghats and Sri Lanka**
- **Sundaland** (Nicobar Islands)', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00260', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 8, 'What is in-situ conservation? Give examples of methods used in India.', '**In-situ conservation** protects species **within their natural habitat**, allowing them to evolve under natural selection pressures.

In India this is implemented through **National Parks, Wildlife Sanctuaries, Biosphere Reserves, and Sacred Groves**, which safeguard entire ecosystems rather than isolated species.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00261', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 9, 'What is ex-situ conservation? Give examples.', '**Ex-situ conservation** involves protecting species **outside their natural habitat**, typically used for critically endangered species or genetic material preservation.

Examples include **zoological parks, botanical gardens, seed banks, gene banks, cryopreservation facilities, and captive breeding programmes**, such as the National Bureau of Plant Genetic Resources'' seed bank in New Delhi.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00262', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 10, 'Under which law was the National Biodiversity Authority established, and where is it based?', 'The **National Biodiversity Authority (NBA)** was established in **2003** under the **Biological Diversity Act, 2002**, to regulate access to Indian biological resources and associated traditional knowledge.

It is headquartered in **Chennai** and works alongside State Biodiversity Boards and local Biodiversity Management Committees.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00263', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 11, 'What is an endemic species?', 'An **endemic species** is one found naturally **only in a specific geographic region** and nowhere else in the world, often due to geographic isolation or unique environmental conditions.

The **Nilgiri Tahr** (confined to the Western Ghats) and the **lion-tailed macaque** are examples of species endemic to India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00264', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 12, 'Why are the Western Ghats considered ecologically significant?', 'The **Western Ghats**, a mountain range running along India''s western coast, is one of the world''s **eight "hottest hotspots" of biological diversity** and a **UNESCO World Heritage Site**.

It harbours exceptionally high levels of **endemism** in flora, amphibians, and fish, and influences the **monsoon pattern** over peninsular India; the **Gadgil** and **Kasturirangan Committees** both examined its ecologically sensitive zones.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00265', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 13, 'What is the legal difference between a National Park and a Wildlife Sanctuary under the Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972?', 'A **National Park** offers a higher degree of protection: **no human activity (including grazing or private rights) is permitted** without specific central government approval, and its boundaries can only be altered by a legislature resolution.

A **Wildlife Sanctuary** allows **some regulated human activity** such as grazing and collection of forest produce, and certain rights can continue if not harmful to wildlife, making its protection regime comparatively more flexible.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00266', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 14, 'What are the three zones of a Biosphere Reserve?', 'A Biosphere Reserve is structured into three concentric zones:

- **Core zone** — strictly protected, undisturbed natural ecosystem with no human activity
- **Buffer zone** — surrounds the core, permits limited research, education, and eco-friendly activity
- **Transition zone** — the outermost area where sustainable human settlement, agriculture, and resource use are allowed', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00267', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 15, 'How many Biosphere Reserves has India notified, and how many are part of the UNESCO World Network?', 'India has notified **18 Biosphere Reserves**, of which **13 are included in UNESCO''s World Network of Biosphere Reserves (WNBR)**.

The **Cold Desert Biosphere Reserve in Himachal Pradesh** was among the more recent additions to the UNESCO network.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00268', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 16, 'Which was India''s first Biosphere Reserve, and when was it notified?', 'The **Nilgiri Biosphere Reserve**, spanning parts of Tamil Nadu, Kerala, and Karnataka in the Western Ghats, was India''s **first Biosphere Reserve**, notified in **1986**.

It was later added to UNESCO''s World Network of Biosphere Reserves.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00269', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 17, 'In which year was Project Tiger launched, and how many reserves did it begin with?', '**Project Tiger** was launched in **1973** at **Jim Corbett National Park**, initially covering **nine tiger reserves** across India.

It was one of the earliest and most prominent species-specific conservation initiatives in the world.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00270', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 18, 'Approximately how many Tiger Reserves does India have today?', 'India''s network of Tiger Reserves has expanded to **nearly 58** (as of 2025), reflecting continuous additions since Project Tiger''s launch in 1973.

These reserves follow a **core-buffer strategy**, where the core area is kept inviolate for tiger breeding and the buffer permits regulated multiple use.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00271', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 19, 'What is the National Tiger Conservation Authority (NTCA), and under which law was it constituted?', 'The **National Tiger Conservation Authority (NTCA)** is a statutory body constituted in **2006** under the **Wildlife (Protection) Amendment Act, 2006**, to provide statutory authority to Project Tiger.

It oversees tiger reserve management, approves state tiger conservation plans, and conducts the **All India Tiger Estimation** every four years.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00272', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 20, 'Which Indian state has the highest tiger population?', '**Madhya Pradesh** holds the **highest tiger population** among Indian states according to recent tiger census figures, earning it the informal title of "Tiger State of India."

Karnataka and Uttarakhand also host large tiger populations.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00273', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 21, 'When and where was the Ramsar Convention adopted, and when did India join it?', 'The **Ramsar Convention on Wetlands** was adopted in **1971** in the Iranian city of **Ramsar**, making it one of the oldest modern intergovernmental environmental agreements.

India became a **signatory in 1982**, committing to designate and conserve Wetlands of International Importance.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00274', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 22, 'Approximately how many Ramsar sites does India have?', 'India''s count of **Ramsar sites (Wetlands of International Importance)** has grown steadily and crossed **85 sites by 2024**, with further additions continuing thereafter.

**Tamil Nadu** has consistently had the highest number of Ramsar sites among Indian states.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00275', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 23, 'Which wetlands were among the first Ramsar sites designated in India?', 'India''s **first Ramsar sites**, designated in **1981**, included **Chilika Lake (Odisha)** — the largest brackish water lagoon in India — and **Keoladeo National Park (Bharatpur, Rajasthan)**, renowned for migratory waterfowl.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00276', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 24, 'What makes the Sundarbans ecologically unique?', 'The **Sundarbans**, spread across India and Bangladesh at the Ganga-Brahmaputra delta, is the **world''s largest contiguous mangrove forest**.

It is simultaneously a **Tiger Reserve, Biosphere Reserve, Ramsar site, and UNESCO World Heritage Site**, and is the only mangrove habitat where tigers are known to swim between islands and prey in water.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00277', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 25, 'Kaziranga National Park is famous for which species?', '**Kaziranga National Park** in Assam is world-renowned for hosting the largest population of the **one-horned (Indian) rhinoceros**, a species once pushed to the brink of extinction by poaching.

It is a **UNESCO World Heritage Site** and also a **Tiger Reserve**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00278', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 26, 'Gir National Park and Wildlife Sanctuary is the only natural habitat of which species?', '**Gir National Park**, in Gujarat''s Saurashtra region, is the **only natural habitat of the Asiatic lion** in the wild.

Its isolated lion population makes it a key site for genetic vulnerability concerns, prompting proposals to establish a second home for the species elsewhere, such as Kuno in Madhya Pradesh.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00279', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 27, 'Which was the first national park established in India?', '**Jim Corbett National Park** in Uttarakhand, originally named **Hailey National Park**, was established in **1936**, making it **India''s first national park**.

It was later renamed after the hunter-naturalist **Jim Corbett** and became the site where Project Tiger was launched in 1973.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00280', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 28, 'When was Project Elephant launched, and what is its objective?', '**Project Elephant** was launched by the Government of India in **1992** to protect elephants, their habitats, and migratory corridors.

Its objectives include mitigating **human-elephant conflict**, ensuring the welfare of captive elephants, and preventing poaching for ivory.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00281', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 29, 'What is Project Lion, announced in 2020?', '**Project Lion**, announced in **2020**, aims to conserve the **Asiatic lion** population of the Gir region through habitat improvement, disease management, and veterinary care.

It also supports efforts for a **second viable population site** for the Asiatic lion, addressing risks from epidemics or disasters affecting the single Gir population.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00282', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 30, 'What caused the catastrophic decline of vulture populations in India in the 1990s?', 'Indian vulture populations crashed by over **95%** since the 1990s primarily due to **diclofenac**, a veterinary anti-inflammatory drug given to cattle that proved **fatally toxic to vultures** feeding on carcasses, causing kidney failure.

India banned veterinary use of diclofenac in **2006** and has since run vulture breeding and conservation programmes.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00283', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 31, 'List the IUCN Red List categories in order of extinction risk.', 'The IUCN Red List classifies species using the following categories, broadly in increasing order of threat:

- **Least Concern (LC)**
- **Near Threatened (NT)**
- **Vulnerable (VU)**
- **Endangered (EN)**
- **Critically Endangered (CR)**
- **Extinct in the Wild (EW)**
- **Extinct (EX)**

A separate category, **Data Deficient (DD)**, applies when insufficient information exists to assess risk.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00284', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 32, 'Name a critically endangered grassland bird species native to India.', 'The **Great Indian Bustard**, found mainly in Rajasthan and Gujarat''s grasslands, is classified as **Critically Endangered** by the IUCN.

Its population has collapsed due to habitat loss and collisions with **overhead power transmission lines**, prompting Supreme Court directions for undergrounding power cables in its habitat.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00285', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 33, 'When was Project Snow Leopard launched?', '**Project Snow Leopard** was launched in **2009** to conserve the snow leopard and its high-altitude Himalayan ecosystem across states like Jammu & Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh, Uttarakhand, Sikkim, and Arunachal Pradesh.

It adopts a landscape-level, participatory approach involving local communities.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00286', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 34, 'What is the Indian Rhino Vision 2020 initiative?', '**Indian Rhino Vision 2020** was a collaborative conservation programme aimed at increasing Assam''s wild rhino population and distributing it across **seven protected areas** to reduce the risk of a single catastrophic event wiping out the species.

It involved translocation of rhinos to parks like **Manas National Park** to re-establish populations.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00287', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 35, 'Which three crocodilian species are covered under India''s crocodile conservation project launched in 1975?', 'India''s **Crocodile Conservation Project**, launched in **1975** with UNDP/FAO assistance, covers three species:

- **Gharial** (fish-eating, narrow-snouted crocodilian)
- **Mugger crocodile** (marsh crocodile)
- **Saltwater crocodile**

It successfully used captive breeding and release to rebuild wild populations.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00288', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 36, 'When was the National Action Plan on Climate Change (NAPCC) launched, and how many missions does it comprise?', 'India''s **National Action Plan on Climate Change (NAPCC)** was launched in **2008**, outlining a strategy to address climate change through **eight national missions**, including the National Solar Mission, National Water Mission, and National Mission for a Green India.

It forms the domestic policy backbone supporting India''s international climate commitments.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00289', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 37, 'What is the UNFCCC, and when was it adopted?', 'The **United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC)** is an international environmental treaty adopted at the **Rio Earth Summit in 1992**, entering into force in **1994**.

It established the principle of **"common but differentiated responsibilities"** and created the annual **Conference of Parties (COP)** as its governing body.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00290', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 38, 'What is the Kyoto Protocol, and what principle underlies its emission targets?', 'The **Kyoto Protocol**, adopted in **1997** and entering into force in **2005**, operationalized the UNFCCC by setting **legally binding emission reduction targets** for developed (Annex I) countries only.

It was rooted in the principle that industrialized nations bore greater historical responsibility for greenhouse gas emissions, exempting developing countries like India and China from binding targets.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00291', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 39, 'What is the Paris Agreement, and what temperature goal does it set?', 'The **Paris Agreement**, adopted at **COP21 in 2015**, is a legally binding international treaty aiming to limit global temperature rise to **well below 2°C above pre-industrial levels**, while pursuing efforts to limit it to **1.5°C**.

Unlike Kyoto, it requires **all parties**, both developed and developing, to submit **Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs)**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00292', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 40, 'What is a COP in the context of international climate negotiations?', '**COP (Conference of Parties)** is the supreme decision-making body of the UNFCCC, comprising all signatory countries that meet **annually** to review progress and negotiate further climate action.

Landmark COPs include **COP3 (Kyoto, 1997)**, **COP21 (Paris, 2015)**, and **COP26 (Glasgow, 2021)**, where India announced its Panchamrit commitments.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00293', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 41, 'What are India''s key updated NDC targets for 2030, submitted in 2022?', 'India''s **updated Nationally Determined Contributions (2022)** commit to reducing the **emissions intensity of GDP by 45%** from 2005 levels by 2030, and achieving about **50% cumulative electric power installed capacity from non-fossil fuel sources** by 2030.

These targets strengthened India''s earlier 2015 NDC commitments of 33-35% emissions intensity reduction and 40% non-fossil capacity.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00294', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 42, 'What is "Panchamrit," and where was it announced?', '**Panchamrit** refers to the **five-point climate commitment** announced by India''s Prime Minister at **COP26 in Glasgow (2021)**, which included reaching **500 GW of non-fossil energy capacity**, meeting **50% of energy requirements from renewables**, reducing **projected carbon emissions by 1 billion tonnes** by 2030, cutting the **carbon intensity of the economy by 45%**, and achieving **net-zero emissions by 2070**.

Some of these quantified figures were not all formally codified into India''s submitted NDC document.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00295', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 43, 'By which year has India pledged to achieve net-zero emissions?', 'India has pledged to achieve **net-zero carbon emissions by 2070**, announced at **COP26 in Glasgow (2021)** as part of its Panchamrit commitments.

This makes India''s net-zero target year later than many developed nations, reflecting its developmental priorities and historically low per-capita emissions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00296', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 44, 'What is the Montreal Protocol concerned with?', 'The **Montreal Protocol**, signed in **1987**, is an international treaty designed to protect the **stratospheric ozone layer** by phasing out the production and consumption of **ozone-depleting substances**, chiefly **chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs)**.

It is widely regarded as the **most successful international environmental agreement**, having led to measurable recovery of the ozone layer.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00297', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 45, 'What is the Kigali Amendment to the Montreal Protocol?', 'The **Kigali Amendment**, adopted in **2016**, expanded the Montreal Protocol''s scope to phase down **hydrofluorocarbons (HFCs)** — powerful greenhouse gases used as refrigerants that do not deplete ozone but contribute significantly to **global warming**.

India ratified the amendment and committed to an HFC phase-down schedule starting from 2032.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00298', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 46, 'What is the Green Climate Fund?', 'The **Green Climate Fund (GCF)**, established under the UNFCCC framework in **2010**, is the world''s largest dedicated fund helping developing countries undertake **mitigation and adaptation** actions to limit or respond to climate change.

Developed countries pledged to mobilize **$100 billion annually** by 2020 to support such climate finance, a commitment that has seen mixed fulfilment.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00299', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 47, 'In which year was the Environment (Protection) Act enacted in India, and in what context?', 'The **Environment (Protection) Act** was enacted in **1986**, in direct response to the **Bhopal Gas Tragedy of 1984**, to provide an umbrella legislation for environmental protection in India.

It empowers the central government to take measures for protecting and improving environmental quality and to set standards for pollutants.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00300', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 48, 'What does the Water (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1974 provide for?', 'The **Water Act, 1974** was India''s first major pollution-control legislation, enacted to prevent and control **water pollution** and to maintain or restore the wholesomeness of water bodies.

It led to the creation of the **Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB)** and State Pollution Control Boards to implement its provisions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00301', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 49, 'What does the Air (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981 provide for?', 'The **Air Act, 1981** was enacted to prevent, control, and abate **air pollution** in India, following global momentum from the 1972 Stockholm Conference.

It empowers the Central and State Pollution Control Boards to declare **air pollution control areas** and set emission standards for industries and vehicles.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00302', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 50, 'When was the National Green Tribunal established, and what is its function?', 'The **National Green Tribunal (NGT)** was established in **2010** under the **National Green Tribunal Act, 2010**, as a specialized judicial body for the **speedy disposal of environmental disputes**.

It handles cases involving substantial questions relating to environmental protection, forest conservation, and natural resources, and can award compensation for environmental damage.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00303', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 51, 'When was the Central Pollution Control Board established?', 'The **Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB)** was established in **1974** under the Water (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, with its functions later expanded by the Air Act, 1981.

It sets national standards for air and water quality and coordinates the activities of State Pollution Control Boards.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00304', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 52, 'What does the Biological Diversity Act, 2002 provide for?', 'The **Biological Diversity Act, 2002** was enacted to give effect to India''s commitments under the **Convention on Biological Diversity (1992)**, regulating access to biological resources and associated traditional knowledge to ensure **fair and equitable benefit-sharing**.

It established a three-tier structure: the **National Biodiversity Authority**, **State Biodiversity Boards**, and local **Biodiversity Management Committees**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00305', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 53, 'What are the Schedules under the Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972?', 'The **Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972** classifies species into **Schedules** that determine their level of legal protection, with **Schedule I** species (such as the tiger and snow leopard) receiving the **highest protection** and absolute prohibition on hunting.

Lower schedules provide progressively lesser degrees of protection, while a schedule also separately lists specified plants and vermin species.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00306', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 54, 'What is CITES, and when did it come into force?', '**CITES (the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora)** is an international agreement that entered into force in **1975**, drafted following a 1963 IUCN resolution and signed in **1973**.

It regulates and monitors international trade in specimens of wild animals and plants to ensure it does not threaten their survival, classifying species into **Appendices I, II, and III** based on the degree of protection needed.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00307', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 55, 'What are the three objectives of the Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD), 1992?', 'The **Convention on Biological Diversity**, adopted at the **1992 Rio Earth Summit**, has three core objectives:

- **Conservation** of biological diversity
- **Sustainable use** of its components
- **Fair and equitable sharing of benefits** arising from the use of genetic resources', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00308', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 56, 'What does the Basel Convention regulate?', 'The **Basel Convention**, adopted in **1989**, regulates the **transboundary movement of hazardous wastes** and their disposal, aiming to prevent developed countries from exporting toxic waste to developing nations without consent.

India is a party to the convention and has domestic rules governing hazardous waste management aligned with it.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00309', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 57, 'What is the Stockholm Convention on Persistent Organic Pollutants?', 'The **Stockholm Convention**, adopted in **2001**, is a global treaty to protect human health and the environment from **Persistent Organic Pollutants (POPs)** — chemicals like DDT and PCBs that resist degradation and accumulate in living tissue.

It requires parties to eliminate or restrict the production and use of listed POPs.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00310', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 58, 'What is the World Heritage Convention, and who administers it?', 'The **Convention Concerning the Protection of the World Cultural and Natural Heritage**, adopted by **UNESCO in 1972**, establishes a framework for identifying and conserving sites of **outstanding universal value**, both cultural and natural.

It is administered by the **UNESCO World Heritage Committee**, which maintains the World Heritage List that includes sites like the Western Ghats and Sundarbans from India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00311', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 59, 'What is the Nagoya Protocol?', 'The **Nagoya Protocol**, adopted in **2010** as a supplementary agreement to the CBD, provides a legal framework for the **fair and equitable sharing of benefits** arising from the utilization of genetic resources, including appropriate access and transfer of relevant technologies.

It entered into force in **2014**, and India has aligned its Biological Diversity Act framework with its provisions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00312', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 60, 'What is eutrophication?', '**Eutrophication** is the excessive enrichment of a water body with nutrients, typically **nitrogen and phosphorus** from agricultural runoff, sewage, or detergents, leading to explosive growth of algae (**algal blooms**).

The subsequent decomposition of this biomass depletes dissolved oxygen, creating **hypoxic "dead zones"** that harm fish and other aquatic life.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00313', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Environment & Ecology', 4, 61, 'What is the Montreux Record under the Ramsar Convention?', 'The **Montreux Record** is a register of Ramsar sites where **ecological character has changed, is changing, or is likely to change** due to human interference, pollution, or other developments, maintained as part of the Ramsar Convention''s monitoring framework.

India''s **Keoladeo National Park** and **Loktak Lake** have both been placed on this record at various times due to ecological degradation, though Keoladeo was later removed after remedial measures.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00314', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 0, 'When was the Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) established, and who is regarded as its founder?', 'ISRO was established on **15 August 1969**, replacing the earlier Indian National Committee for Space Research (INCOSPAR).

It is headquartered in **Bengaluru** and functions under the **Department of Space**. **Dr. Vikram Sarabhai** is regarded as the father of the Indian space programme and founded INCOSPAR in 1962.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00315', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 1, 'Where is the Satish Dhawan Space Centre located, and why is this site significant?', 'The Satish Dhawan Space Centre is located at **Sriharikota**, on a barrier island in **Andhra Pradesh**.

It is ISRO''s primary launch site because its location near the equator and on the east coast allows rockets to gain extra velocity from the Earth''s rotation and to drop spent stages safely over the sea.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00316', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 2, 'What is the significance of the Vikram Sarabhai Space Centre (VSSC)?', 'VSSC, located in **Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala**, is ISRO''s lead centre for developing **launch vehicle technology**, including the PSLV and GSLV programmes.

It was established in **1963**, originally as the Thumba Equatorial Rocket Launching Station (TERLS).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00317', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 3, 'What major discovery did Chandrayaan-1 make, and when was it launched?', 'Chandrayaan-1 was launched on **22 October 2008** aboard a PSLV rocket, making India the fourth entity to reach the Moon.

Its Moon Impact Probe and the NASA-supplied Moon Mineralogy Mapper instrument provided the data that confirmed the **presence of water molecules on the lunar surface**, a landmark global finding announced in 2009.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00318', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 4, 'What happened during the Chandrayaan-2 mission, and what was its key shortfall?', 'Chandrayaan-2, launched in **July 2019** on a GSLV Mk III rocket, successfully placed an **orbiter** in lunar orbit that continues to function and send data.

However, its **Vikram lander** lost communication and crash-landed during the final descent phase in September 2019, meaning the soft-landing objective was not achieved.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00319', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 5, 'When did Chandrayaan-3 achieve its historic soft landing, and what is the landing site named?', 'Chandrayaan-3''s **Vikram lander** touched down near the Moon''s south polar region on **23 August 2023**, making India the **first country to land near the lunar south pole** and the fourth to achieve a soft lunar landing.

The landing site was subsequently named **''Shiv Shakti Point''**, and 23 August is now observed as **National Space Day**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00320', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 6, 'What were the lander and rover of Chandrayaan-3 named, and what did the rover carry?', 'The lander was named **Vikram** (after Dr. Vikram Sarabhai) and the rover was named **Pragyan**.

Pragyan carried instruments including the **Alpha Particle X-ray Spectrometer (APXS)** and the **Laser-Induced Breakdown Spectroscope (LIBS)**, used to determine the elemental composition of the lunar surface near the south pole.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00321', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 7, 'What was distinctive about India''s Mars Orbiter Mission (Mangalyaan)?', 'The Mars Orbiter Mission was launched on **5 November 2013** and entered Mars orbit on **24 September 2014**.

It made India the **first country to reach Mars orbit in its very first attempt**, and it was developed at a remarkably low cost, often cited as cheaper than the Hollywood film *Gravity*.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00322', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 8, 'What is Aditya-L1, and when was it launched?', 'Aditya-L1 is India''s **first dedicated solar observation mission**, launched by ISRO on **2 September 2023** aboard a PSLV rocket.

It was placed into a **halo orbit around the Sun-Earth Lagrange Point 1 (L1)**, which it reached on **6 January 2024**, allowing continuous, uninterrupted observation of the Sun.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00323', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 9, 'What is a Lagrange Point, and why is L1 chosen for solar observation missions?', 'A **Lagrange Point** is a location in space where the gravitational pull of two large bodies (such as the Sun and Earth) balances the centripetal force felt by a smaller object, allowing it to remain in a stable position relative to both.

The **L1 point lies about 1.5 million km from Earth** towards the Sun, and a spacecraft there gets an unobstructed, continuous view of the Sun without being eclipsed by the Earth or Moon.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00324', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 10, 'What is the principal scientific payload aboard Aditya-L1, and what does it study?', 'The principal payload is the **Visible Emission Line Coronagraph (VELC)**, designed and built by the **Indian Institute of Astrophysics, Bengaluru**.

It blocks out the Sun''s bright disc to observe the faint **solar corona**, studying phenomena like coronal mass ejections and space weather that can affect satellites and power grids on Earth.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00325', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 11, 'What is the objective of the Gaganyaan mission?', 'Gaganyaan is India''s **Human Spaceflight Programme**, aiming to send Indian astronauts (**''Gaganyatris''**) into **low Earth orbit** (around 400 km) aboard an Indian-made spacecraft and bring them back safely.

It will make India only the **fourth country** to achieve independent human spaceflight capability, after the USA, Russia, and China.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00326', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 12, 'What was tested during the Gaganyaan TV-D1 mission, and what humanoid is associated with the programme?', '**TV-D1 (Test Vehicle Abort Mission-1)**, conducted in **October 2023**, successfully demonstrated the **Crew Escape System**, which can pull the crew module away from the rocket in case of an emergency during launch.

An uncrewed precursor flight is planned to carry **''Vyommitra''**, a female-form humanoid robot, to test life-support and other systems before a crewed flight.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00327', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 13, 'What distinguishes the PSLV from the GSLV in ISRO''s launch vehicle fleet?', 'The **Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle (PSLV)** is ISRO''s workhorse rocket, primarily used to place satellites into **polar and sun-synchronous orbits**, and has also launched India''s major interplanetary missions (Chandrayaan-1, Mangalyaan).

The **Geosynchronous Satellite Launch Vehicle (GSLV)** is designed to place heavier payloads into **geostationary transfer orbit**, and its success depended on India indigenously developing a **cryogenic upper-stage engine**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00328', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 14, 'What is LVM3 (GSLV Mk III), and which major missions has it launched?', '**LVM3**, earlier called **GSLV Mk III**, is ISRO''s heaviest-lift launch vehicle, capable of carrying about four tonnes to geostationary transfer orbit.

It launched **Chandrayaan-2 and Chandrayaan-3**, and has also carried commercial payloads including batches of **OneWeb satellites**, demonstrating India''s growing commercial launch capability.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00329', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 15, 'What is the Small Satellite Launch Vehicle (SSLV), and why was it developed?', 'The **SSLV** is a smaller, low-cost launch vehicle developed by ISRO to cater to the growing market for launching **small and micro-satellites** into low Earth orbit on short notice.

It is designed for **quick turnaround and assembly**, requiring far fewer personnel and days to integrate compared to the PSLV or GSLV.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00330', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 16, 'What is NISAR, and when was it launched?', '**NISAR (NASA-ISRO Synthetic Aperture Radar)** is a joint Earth-observation satellite launched on **30 July 2025** from Sriharikota aboard a **GSLV-F16** rocket.

It carries an **L-band radar from NASA** and an **S-band radar from ISRO**, and will track minute changes in Earth''s land and ice surfaces, with applications in disaster response and climate monitoring.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00331', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 17, 'What is NavIC, and what is its significance?', '**NavIC (Navigation with Indian Constellation)**, earlier known as IRNSS, is India''s own **regional satellite navigation system**, providing accurate positioning services over India and a region extending about 1,500 km beyond its borders.

It reduces India''s dependence on foreign systems like the US **GPS** for strategic and civilian navigation needs.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00332', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 18, 'What is the role of the INSAT satellite system?', '**INSAT (Indian National Satellite System)** is a series of multipurpose geostationary satellites used for **telecommunications, television broadcasting, meteorological observation, and disaster warning**.

It is one of the largest domestic satellite communication systems in the Asia-Pacific region.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00333', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 19, 'What is the function of NewSpace India Limited (NSIL)?', '**NSIL**, incorporated in **2019**, is the **commercial arm of ISRO** under the Department of Space, responsible for the commercial exploitation of space technologies developed by ISRO.

It handles the transfer of ISRO-developed technologies to industry and the production and marketing of space-based products and services.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00334', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 20, 'What is IN-SPACe, and why was it created?', '**IN-SPACe (Indian National Space Promotion and Authorisation Centre)** is an autonomous, single-window nodal agency set up in **2020** under the Department of Space.

It authorises and promotes **private sector participation** in space activities, allowing private companies to use ISRO''s facilities and undertake independent space activities.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00335', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 21, 'When was the DRDO established, and where is it headquartered?', 'The **Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO)** was formed in **1958** by merging the Technical Development Establishment and the Directorate of Technical Development and Production with the Defence Science Organisation.

It is headquartered in **New Delhi** and functions under the **Ministry of Defence**, running a network of laboratories across the country.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00336', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 22, 'What was ''Mission Divyastra'', and why was it significant?', 'Mission Divyastra, conducted on **11 March 2024**, was India''s **first flight test of the Agni-V missile fitted with MIRV (Multiple Independently Targetable Re-entry Vehicle) technology**.

MIRV capability allows a single missile to carry and deploy **multiple warheads at different targets**, significantly strengthening India''s nuclear deterrence and placing it among a small group of nations with this capability.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00337', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 23, 'What is the range classification and strategic purpose of the Agni-V missile?', 'Agni-V is a **long-range, nuclear-capable ballistic missile** with a range of over **5,000 km**, placing it in the category of an intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM).

It is primarily intended to provide India **credible deterrence against targets across Asia**, including all of China.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00338', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 24, 'What is Agni Prime, and how does it differ from earlier Agni missiles?', '**Agni Prime (Agni-P)** is a new-generation, canisterised ballistic missile with a range of about **1,000 to 2,000 km**, designed to replace older Agni-I, II, and III missiles.

It is significantly **lighter and more accurate**, uses composite materials, and can be launched from both rail and road mobile launchers, improving survivability.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00339', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 25, 'What is BrahMos, and what makes it distinctive among cruise missiles?', '**BrahMos** is a **supersonic cruise missile**, jointly developed by India''s DRDO and Russia''s NPO Mashinostroyeniya (the name derives from the rivers Brahmaputra and Moskva).

It is considered one of the fastest cruise missiles in the world, operating at nearly **Mach 2.8-3**, and can be launched from land, sea, air, and submarine platforms.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00340', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 26, 'What is the Akash missile system used for?', '**Akash** is an indigenously developed **short-range surface-to-air missile (SAM)** system designed to defend against aerial targets such as fighter aircraft, cruise missiles, and drones.

It is deployed by both the **Indian Army and Indian Air Force** and has an effective range of about 25-30 km.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00341', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 27, 'What is India''s declared nuclear doctrine?', 'India''s nuclear doctrine, formally adopted in 2003, is built around the principle of **''No First Use'' (NFU)** of nuclear weapons.

It commits India to **''credible minimum deterrence''**, meaning nuclear weapons will only be used in **retaliation** to a nuclear attack on Indian territory or Indian forces anywhere, with the retaliatory strike intended to cause unacceptable damage.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00342', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 28, 'What was Pokhran-II, and when did it take place?', 'Pokhran-II refers to the series of **five nuclear tests conducted by India in May 1998** at the Pokhran test range in Rajasthan, under the code name **Operation Shakti**.

These tests confirmed India''s capability in fission and thermonuclear devices and led to India formally declaring itself a nuclear weapons state.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00343', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 29, 'What is the Nuclear Command Authority (NCA)?', 'The **Nuclear Command Authority** is India''s apex body responsible for operational and administrative control of nuclear weapons, including authorising their use.

It comprises a **Political Council**, chaired by the **Prime Minister**, which is the sole body authorised to order a nuclear strike, and an **Executive Council**, chaired by the **National Security Advisor**, which provides advice and executes directives.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00344', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 30, 'What is the significance of INS Arihant?', '**INS Arihant** is India''s first indigenously built **nuclear-powered ballistic missile submarine (SSBN)**, commissioned in **2016**.

Its commissioning gave India a credible **sea-based second-strike capability**, completing India''s **nuclear triad** of delivery through land, air, and sea.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00345', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 31, 'What is India''s three-stage nuclear power programme?', 'The three-stage nuclear power programme was conceived by **Dr. Homi J. Bhabha** to make optimal use of India''s limited uranium but abundant **thorium** reserves.

It proceeds from Pressurised Heavy Water Reactors using natural uranium, to Fast Breeder Reactors using plutonium, and finally to reactors using the **uranium-233/thorium cycle** in the third stage.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00346', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 32, 'What is the role of the Nuclear Power Corporation of India Limited (NPCIL)?', '**NPCIL**, a public sector enterprise under the **Department of Atomic Energy**, is responsible for **designing, constructing, and operating India''s nuclear power plants**.

It also undertakes activities related to the entire nuclear fuel cycle for power generation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00347', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 33, 'What is significant about the Kudankulam Nuclear Power Plant?', 'The **Kudankulam Nuclear Power Plant** in Tamil Nadu is India''s **largest nuclear power station**, built with technical and financial cooperation from **Russia**.

Its first unit became operational in 2013-14, and it uses **VVER-1000 pressurised water reactors**, with further units under various stages of construction.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00348', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 34, 'Which was India''s first nuclear power station?', 'The **Tarapur Atomic Power Station**, located in Maharashtra, was India''s **first nuclear power plant**, with its first units commissioned in **1969** using Boiling Water Reactor technology supplied by the United States under the ''Atoms for Peace'' programme.

It remains one of the oldest continuously operating nuclear plants in the country.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00349', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 35, 'What is the role of the Bhabha Atomic Research Centre (BARC)?', '**BARC**, headquartered in Mumbai and founded in **1954** (renamed in 1967 after Homi Bhabha''s death), is India''s **premier nuclear research facility**.

It conducts multidisciplinary research in **nuclear reactor technology, nuclear fuel, radiation applications in medicine and agriculture**, and supports India''s nuclear power and weapons programmes.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00350', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 36, 'What is the function of the Atomic Energy Regulatory Board (AERB)?', '**AERB** was constituted in **1983** under the Atomic Energy Act to carry out **regulatory and safety functions** envisaged in the Act.

It lays down **safety standards and enforces rules and regulations** for ensuring safety in nuclear and radiation facilities in India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00351', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 37, 'Which is the only genetically modified (GM) crop currently permitted for commercial cultivation in India, and when was it approved?', '**Bt cotton** is the only GM crop approved for commercial cultivation in India, first approved in **2002**.

It is genetically engineered with genes from the soil bacterium *Bacillus thuringiensis* to produce a toxin that provides resistance against the **bollworm pest**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00352', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 38, 'What is DMH-11, and what controversy surrounds it?', '**DMH-11 (Dhara Mustard Hybrid-11)** is a genetically modified mustard variety developed by Delhi University scientists, engineered for higher yields through better hybridisation.

Its **environmental release was approved in 2022** by the Genetic Engineering Appraisal Committee, but it has faced legal challenges and opposition from environmental groups concerned about its ecological impact, and it is not yet approved for commercial cultivation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00353', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 39, 'What is the role of the Genetic Engineering Appraisal Committee (GEAC)?', '**GEAC**, functioning under the **Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change**, is the apex regulatory body responsible for the **appraisal and approval of genetically modified organisms (GMOs)** and products in India, including their environmental release.

No GM crop can be commercially released or field-tested in India without GEAC clearance.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00354', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 40, 'What is CRISPR-Cas9, and why is it significant?', '**CRISPR-Cas9** is a **gene-editing technology** that allows scientists to precisely cut and modify specific sequences of DNA within an organism''s genome.

It has revolutionised genetics research and holds promise for treating genetic diseases, improving crop traits, and developing disease-resistant plant varieties, and its discoverers were awarded the **Nobel Prize in Chemistry in 2020**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00355', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 41, 'What is the difference between totipotent and pluripotent stem cells?', '**Totipotent stem cells** (found in early embryos) have the ability to differentiate into **any cell type, including extra-embryonic tissues**, and can develop into a complete organism.

**Pluripotent stem cells** can differentiate into almost all cell types of the body but **cannot form extra-embryonic tissues** like the placenta, making them central to regenerative medicine research.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00356', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 42, 'What is ''Golden Rice'', and why was it developed?', '**Golden Rice** is a genetically engineered variety of rice modified to **biosynthesise beta-carotene**, a precursor of vitamin A, in the edible parts of the grain.

It was developed to help address **vitamin A deficiency**, a major public health problem in parts of Asia and Africa where rice is a dietary staple.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00357', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 43, 'What is the National Mission on Quantum Technologies and Applications?', 'Approved with an outlay of over **₹6,000 crore**, this mission aims to develop India''s capabilities in **quantum computing, quantum communication, quantum cryptography, and quantum sensing**.

It seeks to create a field of quantum-ready scientists and position India among leading nations in this emerging technology, under the **Department of Science and Technology**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00358', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 44, 'What is PARAM, and what is the National Supercomputing Mission?', '**PARAM** refers to a series of **supercomputers developed indigenously** by the Centre for Development of Advanced Computing (C-DAC), beginning with PARAM 8000 in 1991.

The **National Supercomputing Mission**, jointly steered by the Department of Science and Technology and MeitY, aims to establish a network of **high-performance computing facilities** across academic and research institutions in India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00359', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 45, 'What basic principle underlies blockchain technology?', 'A **blockchain** is a **distributed, decentralised digital ledger** that records transactions across many computers in a way that makes them very difficult to alter retroactively.

Each ''block'' of data is cryptographically linked to the previous one, forming a **chain**, and because the ledger is shared and verified across a network rather than controlled by a single authority, it does not require a trusted central intermediary.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00360', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 46, 'What is the role of the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR)?', '**ICMR**, functioning under the **Department of Health Research, Ministry of Health and Family Welfare**, is one of the oldest and largest medical research bodies in the world.

It formulates, coordinates, and promotes **biomedical research** in India, covering communicable and non-communicable diseases, nutrition, and reproductive health.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00361', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 47, 'Who developed Covaxin, and what type of vaccine is it?', '**Covaxin** was developed indigenously by **Bharat Biotech** in collaboration with the **ICMR-National Institute of Virology (NIV), Pune**, which isolated the virus strain used.

It is a **whole-virion inactivated vaccine**, meaning it uses a killed form of the SARS-CoV-2 virus to trigger an immune response.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00362', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 48, 'What is ''herd immunity'' in the context of vaccination?', '**Herd immunity** occurs when a sufficiently large proportion of a population becomes immune to an infectious disease, either through vaccination or prior infection, making its spread from person to person unlikely.

This indirectly protects individuals who are not themselves immune, such as newborns or those with weakened immune systems, by reducing the overall presence of the pathogen in the community.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00363', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 49, 'What is antimicrobial resistance (AMR), and why is it a public health concern?', '**Antimicrobial resistance** occurs when bacteria, viruses, fungi, and parasites change over time and **no longer respond to medicines**, such as antibiotics, making infections harder or impossible to treat.

It is driven largely by the **overuse and misuse of antibiotics** in humans, animals, and agriculture, and the World Health Organization has identified it as one of the top global public health threats.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00364', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 50, 'Which organism acts as the vector for malaria, and what causes the disease?', 'Malaria is caused by parasites of the genus **Plasmodium** and is transmitted to humans through the bite of an infected **female Anopheles mosquito**.

Among the human-infecting species, ***Plasmodium falciparum*** causes the most severe and potentially fatal form of the disease.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00365', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 51, 'What does the pH scale measure, and what do its values indicate?', 'The **pH scale** measures the **concentration of hydrogen ions** in a solution, indicating how acidic or basic (alkaline) it is, on a scale typically ranging from 0 to 14.

A value of **7 is neutral** (like pure water), values **below 7 indicate acidity**, and values **above 7 indicate alkalinity**, with each whole number representing a tenfold change in hydrogen ion concentration.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00366', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 52, 'What is nanotechnology, and what scale does it operate at?', '**Nanotechnology** involves the manipulation of matter at an extremely small scale, generally between **1 and 100 nanometres**, where materials often exhibit unique physical, chemical, and biological properties not seen at larger scales.

Its applications range from targeted drug delivery and water purification to stronger, lighter construction materials and more efficient solar cells.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00367', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 53, 'What does LASER stand for, and what is a key property that makes it useful?', '**LASER** stands for **''Light Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation''**.

Its key property is that it produces light that is **coherent, monochromatic, and highly directional**, allowing it to be focused into an extremely narrow, intense beam, which is why it is used in applications ranging from surgery and industrial cutting to fibre-optic communication.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00368', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 54, 'What is the significance of the reusable launch vehicle technology being developed by ISRO, such as ''Pushpak''?', 'ISRO''s **Reusable Launch Vehicle (RLV) technology demonstrator**, nicknamed **''Pushpak''**, is a winged vehicle designed to test technologies for a **fully reusable space launch system**.

Its successful autonomous landing experiments (RLV-LEX) aim to drastically **reduce the cost of access to space** by allowing rocket components to be recovered and reused, similar in goal to reusable rockets developed elsewhere in the world.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00369', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 55, 'What is the Physical Research Laboratory (PRL), and where is it located?', 'The **Physical Research Laboratory**, located in **Ahmedabad, Gujarat**, was founded by **Dr. Vikram Sarabhai in 1947** and is often called the ''cradle of space science'' in India.

It conducts research in space and atmospheric sciences, astronomy and astrophysics, and planetary and earth sciences, and played a key role in developing payloads for India''s planetary missions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00370', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 56, 'What is the function of the National Remote Sensing Centre (NRSC)?', '**NRSC**, located in **Hyderabad** and functioning under ISRO, is responsible for **remote sensing satellite data acquisition, processing, and dissemination**.

Its data supports applications such as agricultural crop forecasting, disaster management, and natural resource mapping across India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00371', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 57, 'What is Mission Shakti, demonstrated by India in 2019?', '**Mission Shakti**, carried out on **27 March 2019**, was India''s first successful test of an **Anti-Satellite (A-SAT) missile**, in which DRDO used a ballistic missile defence interceptor to destroy a live Indian satellite in low Earth orbit.

The test made India the **fourth country** (after the US, Russia, and China) to demonstrate this capability.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00372', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 58, 'What is ''Shukrayaan'', and what is its intended purpose?', '**Shukrayaan** is a proposed ISRO mission to **Venus**, intended to study the planet''s atmosphere, surface, and subsurface using an orbiter.

It reflects India''s ambition to extend its planetary exploration capability beyond the Moon and Mars to other planets in the solar system.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00373', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 59, 'What distinguishes a ''sun-synchronous orbit'', commonly used for India''s remote sensing satellites?', 'A **sun-synchronous orbit** is a near-polar orbit arranged so that the satellite passes over any given point on Earth''s surface at the **same local solar time** on every pass.

This consistent lighting condition makes such orbits ideal for **Earth observation and remote sensing satellites**, as it allows comparable imagery to be captured across different days and seasons.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00374', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 60, 'What was significant about India''s indigenous light combat aircraft Tejas, from a science and technology standpoint?', '**Tejas** is an indigenously designed and developed **single-engine, multi-role light combat aircraft**, built by Hindustan Aeronautics Limited (HAL) with DRDO''s Aeronautical Development Agency overseeing its design.

Its development demonstrated India''s growing capability in **advanced aerospace engineering**, including fly-by-wire flight control systems and composite airframe materials, reducing historic dependence on imported fighter aircraft designs.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00375', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Science & Technology', 5, 61, 'What is the purpose of India''s Deep Ocean Mission?', 'The **Deep Ocean Mission**, approved in **2021** under the Ministry of Earth Sciences, aims to explore the deep ocean for **resources such as polymetallic nodules**, develop technologies for deep-sea mining and submersibles, and study ocean biodiversity and climate change impacts.

It includes the development of ''Matsya 6000'', a manned submersible designed to carry humans to a depth of **6,000 metres**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00376', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 0, 'How many classical dance forms are officially recognized by the Sangeet Natak Akademi, and what are they?', 'The **Sangeet Natak Akademi** recognizes **eight classical dance forms** of India: **Bharatanatyam** (Tamil Nadu), **Kathak** (North India), **Kathakali** (Kerala), **Kuchipudi** (Andhra Pradesh), **Odissi** (Odisha), **Manipuri** (Manipur), **Mohiniyattam** (Kerala), and **Sattriya** (Assam).

The Union **Ministry of Culture** separately treats **Chhau**, a tribal martial dance of Odisha, West Bengal, and Jharkhand, as a **ninth classical dance**, though the Akademi''s own list remains at eight.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00377', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 1, 'What is the origin and classical basis of Bharatanatyam?', '**Bharatanatyam** originated in the **Tamil Nadu** temples as a solo dance performed by *devadasis*, historically known as **Sadir**, and is considered one of the oldest classical dance forms, rooted in the **Natya Shastra** of Bharata Muni.

It was revived and codified in its modern form in the early 20th century, notably through the efforts of the **Tanjore Quartet**, and emphasizes precise geometric postures, *adavus* (basic steps), and expressive *abhinaya*.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00378', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 2, 'What distinguishes Kathak from other classical dance forms, and what are its major gharanas?', '**Kathak**, meaning ''storyteller,'' developed in **North India** as a narrative dance form performed by *kathakas* in temples, and was later refined under **Mughal court patronage**, giving it a distinctive blend of Hindu devotional themes and Persian-influenced court aesthetics.

Its major gharanas (schools) are the **Jaipur gharana** (known for vigorous footwork and technical virtuosity), the **Lucknow gharana** (known for graceful expression, or *abhinaya*), and the **Banaras gharana**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00379', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 3, 'What are the key features of Kathakali, and from which state does it originate?', '**Kathakali** originates in **Kerala** and is a dance-drama form distinguished by **elaborate costumes, large headdresses, and intricate facial makeup** that follow a strict color code to represent different character types (such as *pacha* for noble heroes and *kathi* for villains).

Its themes are drawn mainly from the **Ramayana, Mahabharata, and Puranas**, and the performance combines stylized hand gestures (*mudras*), facial expressions, and percussion accompaniment, traditionally lasting through the night.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00380', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 4, 'What are the two traditional streams from which Odissi dance evolved?', '**Odissi**, from **Odisha**, traces its evolution to two parallel traditions: the **Mahari** tradition, performed by temple dancers dedicated to Lord Jagannath at the **Jagannath Temple, Puri**, and the **Gotipua** tradition, in which young boys dressed as girls performed devotional dances.

Its hallmark is the **tribhanga** posture, a three-bend stance of the body, along with sculpturesque poses drawn from temple carvings.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00381', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 5, 'Who is credited with founding Kuchipudi, and what state is it associated with?', '**Kuchipudi** originates from a village of the same name in **Andhra Pradesh** and is traditionally credited to the 17th-century Vaishnava saint-poet **Siddhendra Yogi**, who organized it as a dance-drama performed by Brahmin men.

Unlike purely solo classical forms, Kuchipudi retained strong dance-drama (*natya*) elements, often enacting stories such as the *Bhama Kalapam*, and later developed solo repertoire as well.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00382', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 6, 'What devotional tradition shaped Manipuri dance, and what is its most famous repertoire?', '**Manipuri dance**, from **Manipur**, is deeply shaped by **Vaishnavism**, particularly the worship of Radha-Krishna, after the tradition was popularized in the region in the 18th century.

Its most celebrated repertoire is the **Ras Lila**, depicting the divine love of Radha and Krishna, marked by gentle, flowing movements, minimal percussive footwork, and elaborate traditional costumes including the cylindrical skirt called the *kumil*.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00383', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 7, 'What does the name Mohiniyattam mean, and where does it originate?', '**Mohiniyattam** translates to ''dance of the enchantress,'' referring to **Mohini**, the enchanting female form taken by Lord Vishnu, and it originates from **Kerala**.

It is a solo, predominantly feminine dance style marked by swaying, graceful movements, gentle footwork, and lyrical *abhinaya*, and is often considered a companion form to the more vigorous, male-dominated Kathakali of the same region.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00384', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 8, 'Who founded Sattriya dance, and where is it traditionally performed?', '**Sattriya** was founded by the 15th-16th century Vaishnavite saint-reformer **Srimanta Sankaradeva** in **Assam** as part of the **Neo-Vaishnavite movement**, originally performed inside monastery-cum-temple institutions called **sattras**.

It was formally recognized as a classical dance form by the Sangeet Natak Akademi in the year **2000**, making it the most recent addition to the official list of eight.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00385', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 9, 'What are the two principal systems of Indian classical music?', 'Indian classical music is broadly divided into two systems: **Hindustani classical music**, practiced mainly in **North India** and historically shaped by Persian and Central Asian influences following the Delhi Sultanate and Mughal periods, and **Carnatic classical music**, practiced mainly in **South India** and more directly rooted in ancient Sanskrit musicological treatises.

Both systems share foundational concepts of **raga** (melodic framework) and **tala** (rhythmic cycle) but differ in their compositional styles, terminology, and performance conventions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00386', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 10, 'What is a gharana in Hindustani classical music, and which is considered the oldest?', 'A **gharana** is a system of social organization in Hindustani classical music that links musicians through lineage, discipleship, or a shared stylistic and technical approach to performance, often centered on a particular family or court.

The **Gwalior gharana** is widely regarded as the **oldest** of the vocal gharanas, serving as the foundation from which several later gharanas, such as **Agra, Jaipur-Atrauli, Kirana, and Patiala**, developed.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00387', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 11, 'Who constitute the ''Carnatic Music Trinity''?', 'The **Carnatic Music Trinity** refers to three celebrated 18th-19th century composers from the **Thanjavur region** of Tamil Nadu: **Tyagaraja**, **Muthuswami Dikshitar**, and **Syama Sastri**.

Their compositions, mostly devotional in nature and composed largely in **Telugu and Sanskrit**, form the core repertoire of present-day Carnatic concerts.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00388', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 12, 'What do the terms ''raga'' and ''tala'' mean in Indian classical music?', 'A **raga** is a melodic framework of specific ascending and descending note patterns that evokes a particular mood or emotion, serving as the basis for improvisation in both Hindustani and Carnatic music.

A **tala** is the rhythmic cycle or time measure that structures a composition, defined by a fixed number of beats grouped into sections, such as the common **teentaal** (16 beats) in Hindustani music.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00389', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 13, 'What is Dhrupad, and why is it significant in Hindustani music history?', '**Dhrupad** is considered the **oldest surviving form of Hindustani classical vocal music**, characterized by a solemn, austere style with slow elaboration of the raga (*alap*) without the ornamentation found in later styles like *khayal*.

It flourished under the patronage of the **Mughal court**, especially under **Akbar**, whose court musician **Tansen** was a renowned Dhrupad exponent, and today it is closely associated with the **Dagar family** tradition.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00390', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 14, 'Name the major stringed instruments associated with Indian classical music and their typical traditions.', '- **Sitar** — a plucked string instrument central to Hindustani music, popularized globally by **Ravi Shankar**
- **Sarod** — a fretless stringed instrument known for its deep, resonant tone, associated with musicians like **Amjad Ali Khan**
- **Veena** — one of the most ancient Indian instruments, closely associated with Carnatic music and with the goddess **Saraswati**
- **Santoor** — a trapezoid-shaped hammered string instrument, traditionally from **Kashmir**, popularized in classical music by **Shivkumar Sharma**', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00391', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 15, 'Which instrument was Ustad Bismillah Khan renowned for, and what honour did he receive?', '**Ustad Bismillah Khan** was renowned for playing the **shehnai**, a wind instrument traditionally associated with auspicious occasions, and he is credited with elevating it to a respected classical concert instrument.

He was awarded the **Bharat Ratna**, India''s highest civilian honour, in **2001**, becoming one of the few classical musicians to receive it.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00392', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 16, 'What is the Tabla, and with whom is its invention traditionally associated?', 'The **tabla** is a pair of hand-played percussion drums central to Hindustani classical music, consisting of the smaller **dayan** (treble drum) and the larger **bayan** (bass drum).

Its invention is traditionally, though not conclusively, attributed to the 13th-century poet-musician **Amir Khusrau**, associated with the Delhi Sultanate court.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00393', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 17, 'What are the distinguishing features of the Nagara style of temple architecture?', 'The **Nagara style** developed in **North India** from roughly the 5th century CE onward and is typically characterized by a curvilinear tower called the **shikhara**, built without the elaborate boundary walls and ornamental gateways (*gopurams*) typical of South Indian temples.

Its sub-styles are classified based on shikhara shape, such as the **Latina** (simple curvilinear), **Phamsana** (broader, shorter), and **Valabhi** (rectangular, barrel-vaulted roof) types.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00394', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 18, 'What are the distinguishing features of the Dravida style of temple architecture?', 'The **Dravida style**, found predominantly in **South India**, is marked by a pyramidal tower called the **vimana** above the sanctum, as opposed to the curvilinear shikhara of the north, and typically includes a towering ornamental gateway called the **gopuram**.

Dravida temples are usually enclosed within rectangular **boundary walls (prakara)** and often feature large temple tanks, as seen in temples built under the **Pallava, Chola, Pandya, and Vijayanagara** dynasties.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00395', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 19, 'What is the Vesara style of temple architecture, and which dynasties promoted it?', 'The **Vesara style** is a **hybrid architectural form** combining elements of both the Nagara (northern) and Dravida (southern) styles, developed mainly in the **Deccan region**.

It was notably promoted by the **Chalukyas of Badami/later Chalukyas** and further refined by the **Hoysalas**, whose temples at **Belur, Halebidu, and Somnathpur** are prime examples, featuring intricate star-shaped platforms and detailed soapstone carving.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00396', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 20, 'What is unique about the Ellora Caves'' Kailasa temple?', 'The **Kailasa (Kailasanatha) temple** at the **Ellora Caves** in Maharashtra, built under the **Rashtrakuta** ruler **Krishna I** in the 8th century CE, is the **largest monolithic rock-cut structure in the world**, carved entirely from a single rock face from the top downward.

Ellora itself is unique for containing **Buddhist, Hindu, and Jain** rock-cut monuments side by side, reflecting the religious pluralism of the period.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00397', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 21, 'What distinguishes the Ajanta Caves, and what are they most famous for?', 'The **Ajanta Caves** in **Maharashtra** are a complex of **Buddhist rock-cut monuments**, comprising *chaityas* (prayer halls) and *viharas* (monasteries), excavated over roughly two main phases spanning the **2nd century BCE to the 6th century CE**.

They are most famous for their **mural paintings**, depicting the Jataka tales and scenes from the Buddha''s life, considered among the finest surviving examples of ancient Indian painting.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00398', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 22, 'What are the monolithic Rathas of Mahabalipuram, and under which dynasty were they built?', 'The **Rathas (chariots) of Mahabalipuram**, in Tamil Nadu, are a group of **monolithic rock-cut temples**, each carved from a single piece of granite in the shape of a temple chariot, built under the **Pallava** dynasty, notably during the reign of **Narasimhavarman I**, in the 7th century CE.

They are popularly known as the **Pancha Rathas** (five chariots), each named after characters from the Mahabharata, and form part of the Group of Monuments at Mahabalipuram, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00399', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 23, 'What is Indo-Islamic architecture, and what are its characteristic features?', '**Indo-Islamic architecture** refers to the architectural style that emerged from the synthesis of Islamic building traditions, introduced from the **Delhi Sultanate** period onward, with indigenous Indian construction techniques and decorative elements.

Its characteristic features include the **true arch and dome**, use of **minarets**, geometric and calligraphic ornamentation, and extensive use of **red sandstone and marble**, as seen in structures ranging from the **Qutub Minar** to the **Taj Mahal**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00400', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 24, 'Who began construction of the Qutub Minar, and who completed it?', 'Construction of the **Qutub Minar** in Delhi was begun by **Qutb-ud-din Aibak**, founder of the **Delhi Sultanate** (Slave/Mamluk dynasty), around **1199 CE**, to commemorate the start of Muslim rule in Delhi.

It was completed by his successor **Iltutmish**, and later repaired by **Firoz Shah Tughlaq** after damage from lightning, making it a structure with contributions across several reigns.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00401', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 25, 'Under whose patronage was the Taj Mahal built, and what is it made of?', 'The **Taj Mahal** at **Agra** was commissioned by the Mughal emperor **Shah Jahan** in memory of his wife **Mumtaz Mahal**, with construction beginning around **1632 CE** and completed roughly two decades later.

It is constructed primarily of **white marble**, inlaid with semi-precious stones in a technique known as *pietra dura*, and is recognized as a UNESCO World Heritage Site and one of the New Seven Wonders of the World.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00402', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 26, 'What are Charminar and Gol Gumbaz, and where are they located?', '**Charminar**, built in **1591** by **Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah** of the **Qutb Shahi dynasty**, is a monument with four grand arches and minarets located in **Hyderabad**, Telangana.

**Gol Gumbaz**, located in **Bijapur, Karnataka**, is the mausoleum of **Muhammad Adil Shah** of the **Adil Shahi dynasty**, and is notable for having one of the **largest unsupported domes in the world**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00403', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 27, 'What is Indo-Saracenic architecture, and when did it develop?', '**Indo-Saracenic architecture** is a revivalist architectural style that developed during the period of **British colonial rule** in the late 19th century, blending **Indo-Islamic and Indian temple architectural elements** with Gothic and Neo-Classical European styles.

Prominent examples include the **Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus (formerly Victoria Terminus)** in Mumbai and the **Gateway of India**, both reflecting this East-West architectural fusion.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00404', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 28, 'What are the major schools of Rajput (Rajasthani) painting?', '**Rajput painting** flourished in the royal courts of Rajasthan from the 16th to 19th centuries, with distinct regional schools including the **Mewar school** (bold colors, devotional themes), the **Bundi-Kota school** (hunting scenes, lush landscapes), the **Marwar school**, and the **Kishangarh school**, the last famous for its iconic *Bani Thani* portrait.

Common themes across these schools include scenes from the **Ramayana, Mahabharata, Bhagavata Purana**, and courtly life, often rendered in vivid natural pigments.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00405', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 29, 'What characterizes Mughal painting, and under which emperors did it flourish most?', '**Mughal painting** developed as a court art blending **Persian miniature traditions** with indigenous Indian styles, emphasizing naturalistic portraiture, detailed court scenes, and historical narratives.

It reached its peak under **Akbar**, who established an imperial atelier staffed by Persian and Indian artists, and continued to flourish under **Jahangir**, known for his interest in naturalistic studies of flora and fauna, and **Shah Jahan**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00406', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 30, 'What distinguishes Pahari painting, and name its two major schools.', '**Pahari painting** developed in the hill states of the Himalayan foothills (present-day Himachal Pradesh and Jammu region) from the 17th to 19th centuries, noted for its lyrical, romantic depiction of themes such as **Radha-Krishna legends** and the **Nayika-bheda** classification of heroines.

Its two major schools are the **Basohli school**, known for bold colors and intense expression, and the later **Kangra school**, known for softer, more delicate and naturalistic renderings.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00407', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 31, 'What is Madhubani painting, and where does it originate?', '**Madhubani painting**, also called **Mithila painting**, originates from the **Mithila region of Bihar**, traditionally created by women on freshly plastered mud walls and floors of homes during festivals and special occasions, using natural dyes and pigments.

It is characterized by **geometric patterns, bold lines, and vivid colors**, often depicting religious motifs, nature, and scenes from mythology, and it holds a **Geographical Indication (GI) tag**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00408', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 32, 'What is Warli painting, and what is distinctive about its visual style?', '**Warli painting** is a tribal art form practiced by the **Warli tribe** of **Maharashtra** (primarily in the Thane and Palghar districts), traditionally painted in white pigment made from rice paste on a mud-washed red or brown background.

Its visual style is distinctive for using only **basic geometric shapes** — circles, triangles, and squares — to depict scenes of daily life, agriculture, and festivals, without the use of human or animal figures in realistic detail.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00409', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 33, 'What is Tanjore (Thanjavur) painting known for?', '**Tanjore painting**, originating in **Thanjavur, Tamil Nadu**, under the patronage of the **Nayaka and Maratha rulers** of Thanjavur, is a classical South Indian painting style known for its **rich colors, compact composition**, and characteristic use of **gold foil (gold leaf) relief work** and embedded semi-precious stones.

Its subjects are predominantly devotional, most often depicting Hindu deities such as Krishna in ornate, glittering settings.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00410', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 34, 'What is Pattachitra, and which regions is it associated with?', '**Pattachitra** is a traditional cloth-based scroll painting associated chiefly with **Odisha** and parts of **West Bengal**, the name deriving from the Sanskrit words *patta* (cloth) and *chitra* (picture).

It is characterized by intricate detailing, mythological narratives (especially relating to **Lord Jagannath**), and natural pigments, and the style is closely linked to the traditional art found around the **Puri Jagannath Temple**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00411', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 35, 'What was the Bengal School of Art, and who is considered its founder?', 'The **Bengal School of Art** was an influential **nationalist art movement** in early 20th-century India that sought to counter the dominance of Western academic art styles by reviving indigenous and Mughal/Rajput artistic traditions.

It is primarily associated with **Abanindranath Tagore**, who, along with artists like **Nandalal Bose**, promoted a distinctly Indian aesthetic that became closely linked with the broader **Swadeshi movement**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00412', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 36, 'As of 2025, approximately how many UNESCO World Heritage Sites does India have, and how are they categorized?', 'As of **2025**, India has **44 UNESCO World Heritage Sites**, comprising **36 cultural sites**, **7 natural sites**, and **1 mixed site**, making India one of the countries with the highest number of such sites globally.

The most recent addition, inscribed in **July 2025**, is the **Maratha Military Landscapes**, a serial site comprising a dozen forts built or fortified under the **Maratha empire**, mostly in Maharashtra.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00413', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 37, 'What were the Charaideo Moidams, and why was their 2024 inscription significant?', 'The **Charaideo Moidams** are a cluster of over ninety earthen royal **burial mounds** built by the **Tai-Ahom dynasty** in **Assam** over roughly six centuries, often described as the ''pyramids of Assam.''

Their inscription as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in **July 2024** was significant as they became the **first cultural heritage site from Northeast India** to receive this designation.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00414', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 38, 'What are the Khajuraho temples famous for, and under which dynasty were they built?', 'The **Khajuraho Group of Monuments** in Madhya Pradesh were built mainly between the 10th and 12th centuries CE under the **Chandela dynasty**, and are inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.

They are internationally renowned for their **intricate erotic and sensuous sculptures**, alongside a far larger body of sculptures depicting deities, daily life, and mythology, all rendered in the **Nagara architectural style**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00415', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 39, 'What was Hampi, and which dynasty''s capital did it serve as?', '**Hampi**, in present-day Karnataka, was the capital of the **Vijayanagara Empire**, flourishing especially under rulers such as **Krishnadevaraya** in the 16th century, before being sacked following the **Battle of Talikota (1565)**.

The ruins, inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, include the **Virupaksha temple**, the iconic **stone chariot** at the Vittala temple complex, and extensive royal and sacred structures.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00416', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 40, 'What is unique about the Sundarbans as a UNESCO World Heritage Site?', 'The **Sundarbans**, spanning the delta region of **West Bengal** at the mouth of the Ganga-Brahmaputra river system, is the **largest mangrove forest in the world** and was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage (natural) Site in **1987**.

It is globally significant as a critical habitat for the **Royal Bengal Tiger**, alongside numerous other threatened species, within a complex and highly dynamic estuarine ecosystem.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00417', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 41, 'Why was the Western Ghats inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and when?', 'The **Western Ghats**, a mountain range running along India''s western coast through states from Gujarat to Kerala, were inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage (natural) Site in **2012** due to their exceptional **biodiversity** and status as one of the world''s **eight ''hottest'' biodiversity hotspots**.

The serial site comprises numerous protected areas across multiple states, recognized for extraordinarily high levels of **endemic flora and fauna**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00418', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 42, 'What is Dholavira, and why is it archaeologically significant?', '**Dholavira**, located in the Rann of Kutch in **Gujarat**, is one of the largest and best-preserved urban settlements of the **Indus Valley (Harappan) Civilization**, inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in **2021**.

It is archaeologically significant for its sophisticated **water conservation and reservoir systems**, its distinctive three-part urban layout, and a stone inscription believed to be an early form of signage.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00419', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 43, 'What are the Vedas, and which is considered the oldest?', 'The **Vedas** are the oldest sacred texts of Hinduism and among the oldest religious literature in the world, comprising four texts: the **Rigveda, Samaveda, Yajurveda, and Atharvaveda**.

The **Rigveda** is considered the **oldest** of the four, consisting primarily of hymns (*suktas*) dedicated to various deities, and is a key source for reconstructing the society and beliefs of the early **Vedic period**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00420', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 44, 'What is Sangam literature, and in which language was it composed?', '**Sangam literature** refers to a body of ancient **Tamil** poetic and literary works, traditionally believed to have been composed over several centuries in assemblies (*sangams*) held in and around **Madurai**, roughly spanning the **3rd century BCE to 3rd century CE**.

It is considered among the earliest known **secular literature** of India, covering themes of love, war, governance, and ethics, distinct from the largely religious focus of Sanskrit texts of the period.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00421', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 45, 'What is the Jnanpith Award, and what does it recognize?', 'The **Jnanpith Award** is India''s **highest literary honour**, instituted in **1965** by the Bharatiya Jnanpith organisation, awarded annually to an Indian writer for their **outstanding contribution to literature**, across any of the languages listed in the **Eighth Schedule of the Constitution** (plus English).

It was first awarded to the Malayalam writer **G. Sankara Kurup** in 1965.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00422', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 46, 'Who authored the Ramayana and the Mahabharata?', 'The **Ramayana** is traditionally attributed to the sage **Valmiki**, who composed it in Sanskrit, while the **Mahabharata**, the longer of the two great Indian epics, is traditionally attributed to the sage **Vyasa (Krishna Dwaipayana Vyasa)**.

Both epics, composed and compiled over long periods, contain the **embedded philosophical texts** central to Hindu thought — notably the **Bhagavad Gita**, which forms part of the Mahabharata.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00423', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 47, 'What was the Bhakti movement, and how did it influence regional literature?', 'The **Bhakti movement** was a devotional religious movement that swept across India roughly from the 7th to the 17th centuries, emphasizing a **personal, emotional devotion to a chosen deity** over elaborate ritual, and largely rejecting caste distinctions in matters of faith.

It profoundly shaped **regional-language literature**, producing towering figures such as **Kabir and Tulsidas** (Hindi), **Mirabai** (Rajasthani/Hindi), **Chaitanya Mahaprabhu** (Bengal), and **Andal and the Alvars** (Tamil).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00424', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 48, 'Who were the ''Navaratnas'' of Akbar''s court?', 'The **Navaratnas** (''nine jewels'') were nine especially distinguished courtiers in the court of the Mughal emperor **Akbar**, celebrated for their accomplishments in administration, military affairs, music, and literature.

They included **Abul Fazl** (chronicler and author of the *Akbarnama*), **Faizi** (poet), **Raja Birbal**, **Raja Man Singh**, **Tansen** (musician), and **Raja Todar Mal** (revenue administrator), among others.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00425', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 49, 'What is the significance of Tulsidas''s Ramcharitmanas?', 'The **Ramcharitmanas**, composed by the 16th-century poet-saint **Tulsidas** in **Awadhi** (a dialect of Hindi), retells the story of the Ramayana with a strong devotional (Bhakti) orientation centered on **Lord Rama**.

It became one of the most influential and widely recited religious texts in North India, playing a major role in popularizing the Rama-centered Bhakti tradition among the masses in the vernacular, rather than in Sanskrit.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00426', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 50, 'What is the Kumbh Mela, and what UNESCO recognition has it received?', 'The **Kumbh Mela** is a mass Hindu pilgrimage and fair held at four river-bank sites in rotation — **Prayagraj, Haridwar, Ujjain, and Nashik** — associated with the legend of the *samudra manthan* (churning of the cosmic ocean) during which drops of the nectar of immortality fell at these locations.

It was inscribed by UNESCO on the **Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity in 2017**, recognized as the **largest peaceful gathering of pilgrims** in the world.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00427', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 51, 'What is the Hornbill Festival, and where is it held?', 'The **Hornbill Festival** is an annual cultural festival held in **Kisama, Nagaland**, typically in **early December**, showcasing the diverse traditions, music, dances, crafts, and cuisines of Nagaland''s various tribes.

It is named after the **hornbill bird**, which holds a significant place in the folklore and traditional attire of several Naga tribes, and is promoted as a major platform for tribal cultural tourism.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00428', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 52, 'What is the Pushkar Fair known for, and where is it held?', 'The **Pushkar Fair**, held annually in the town of **Pushkar, Rajasthan**, is one of the world''s largest **camel and livestock fairs**, combining trade in cattle and camels with religious pilgrimage to the town''s **Brahma temple**, one of the few temples dedicated to that deity in India.

The fair also features cultural competitions, folk performances, and has become a significant draw for international tourism.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00429', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 53, 'What is the Khajuraho Dance Festival?', 'The **Khajuraho Dance Festival** is an annual week-long festival held at **Khajuraho, Madhya Pradesh**, set against the backdrop of the **Khajuraho temples**, showcasing performances across India''s classical dance forms by renowned artists.

It is organized by the state tourism department to promote both classical dance traditions and the heritage significance of the Khajuraho monuments.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00430', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 54, 'What is the Rann Utsav, and in which state is it celebrated?', 'The **Rann Utsav** is an annual cultural festival held on the vast white salt desert of the **Great Rann of Kutch** in **Gujarat**, typically spanning several months across the winter season.

It showcases the region''s **folk music, dance (such as Garba), handicrafts, and cuisine**, and has become a significant tourism initiative promoting the unique desert landscape of Kutch.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00431', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 55, 'What is a Geographical Indication (GI) tag, and which body grants it in India?', 'A **Geographical Indication (GI) tag** identifies a product as originating from a specific geographical region, where a given quality, reputation, or characteristic is essentially attributable to that origin, protecting it against unauthorized use elsewhere.

In India, GI tags are granted under the **Geographical Indications of Goods (Registration and Protection) Act, 1999**, administered by the **Geographical Indications Registry**, located in **Chennai**, under the Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00432', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 56, 'What is Pashmina, and which region is it traditionally associated with?', '**Pashmina** is a fine, soft variety of cashmere wool obtained from the undercoat of the **Changthangi (Pashmina) goat**, reared primarily in the high-altitude regions of **Ladakh**, and traditionally woven into shawls in the **Kashmir Valley**.

**Kashmir Pashmina** holds a Geographical Indication tag, recognizing the distinctive hand-spinning and weaving techniques used in its production.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00433', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 57, 'What is Chikankari, and where did this embroidery tradition develop?', '**Chikankari** is a delicate and intricate form of **white-thread embroidery** on fabric, traditionally developed and most closely associated with **Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh**, believed to have been popularized under Mughal patronage.

It involves techniques such as *shadow work* and a variety of fine stitches, and it holds a Geographical Indication tag as ''Lucknow Chikan Craft.''', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00434', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 58, 'What is Bidriware, and which region is it associated with?', '**Bidriware** is a distinctive metal handicraft technique originating in **Bidar, Karnataka**, involving the inlay of **silver designs onto a blackened alloy of zinc and copper**, producing items such as vases, bowls, and decorative pieces.

It developed under the patronage of the **Bahmani Sultanate** and later the Barid Shahi rulers, and today carries a Geographical Indication tag.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00435', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 59, 'What is Phulkari, and which region is it traditionally from?', '**Phulkari**, meaning ''flower work,'' is a traditional embroidery craft from the **Punjab region**, characterized by vibrant floral and geometric patterns darned onto coarse cotton fabric (*khaddar*) using colorful silk thread.

Historically practiced by women as a domestic craft for dowries and special occasions, it today holds a Geographical Indication tag associated with Punjab.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00436', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 60, 'What was the significance of the Progressive Artists'' Group in modern Indian art?', 'The **Progressive Artists'' Group**, founded in **Bombay in 1947**, the same year as Indian independence, sought to break away from the nationalist, revivalist aesthetic of the Bengal School and embrace **modernist, international styles** of painting.

Its founding members included **F. N. Souza, M. F. Husain, S. H. Raza, K. H. Ara**, and others, and the group is considered pivotal in shaping the trajectory of **modern Indian art** in the post-independence era.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00437', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 61, 'What is the Jantar Mantar in Jaipur, and who built it?', 'The **Jantar Mantar** at **Jaipur**, Rajasthan, is an astronomical observatory consisting of large masonry instruments built by **Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II** in the early **18th century**, one of five such observatories he constructed across North India.

It is designed to make naked-eye astronomical observations, including measuring time, tracking celestial bodies, and predicting eclipses, and is inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00438', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Art & Culture', 6, 62, 'What is the architectural and cultural significance of Santiniketan?', '**Santiniketan**, in West Bengal, was founded as an educational and cultural retreat by **Rabindranath Tagore**, who later established **Visva-Bharati University** there in **1921**, envisioning a space that integrated nature, art, and learning in the spirit of ancient Indian ashram traditions.

It was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in **2023**, recognized for its distinctive architectural and educational philosophy blending Indian, Japanese, and Western artistic influences.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00439', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 0, 'What is the objective of the PM-KISAN scheme and when was it launched?', '**PM-KISAN (Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi)** is a central sector scheme launched in **February 2019** by the **Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare**.

It provides income support of **₹6,000 per year** (in three equal installments of ₹2,000) directly to the bank accounts of landholding farmer families, transferred through **Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT)**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00440', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 1, 'What is Ayushman Bharat PM-JAY and what health cover does it provide?', '**Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (PM-JAY)** was launched in **September 2018** and is the world''s largest government-funded health assurance scheme.

It provides a health cover of **₹5 lakh per family per year** for secondary and tertiary hospitalisation to the bottom **40% of the population** (about 10.74 crore poor and vulnerable families), identified via the SECC database. It is implemented by the **National Health Authority**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00441', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 2, 'How was Ayushman Bharat expanded for senior citizens in 2024?', 'In **September 2024**, the government approved extending **PM-JAY cover of ₹5 lakh per year** to **all senior citizens aged 70 and above**, irrespective of income, issued through a distinct **Ayushman Vay Vandana Card**.

For families already enrolled in PM-JAY, this is an **additional, ring-fenced top-up** specifically for the senior member rather than a shared family pool.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00442', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 3, 'What are the two pillars of Ayushman Bharat?', 'Ayushman Bharat rests on two components.

- **Health and Wellness Centres (HWCs)**: upgrading sub-centres and primary health centres to deliver comprehensive primary healthcare, including screening for non-communicable diseases.
- **Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (PM-JAY)**: a health insurance scheme providing secondary and tertiary care hospitalisation cover.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00443', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 4, 'What is the objective of Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY)?', '**PMJDY**, launched in **August 2014** by the **Department of Financial Services, Ministry of Finance**, is a **financial inclusion** programme aimed at ensuring access to basic banking (a zero-balance savings account), remittance, credit, insurance, and pension facilities for every unbanked household.

Accounts come with a **RuPay debit card** and accident insurance cover, forming part of the **JAM trinity** (Jan Dhan–Aadhaar–Mobile).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00444', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 5, 'What is the Swachh Bharat Mission and what are its components?', 'The **Swachh Bharat Mission (SBM)** was launched on **2 October 2014** by the **Ministry of Jal Shakti** (rural) and **Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs** (urban), with the objective of achieving an **Open Defecation Free (ODF)** India and improving solid and liquid waste management.

It has two sub-missions: **SBM-Gramin** for rural areas and **SBM-Urban** for towns and cities. India was declared ODF on **2 October 2019**, the 150th birth anniversary of Mahatma Gandhi.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00445', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 6, 'What is Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY) and what are its two verticals?', '**PMAY**, launched in **2015** by the **Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs**, aims to provide **"Housing for All"** by offering pucca houses with basic amenities to eligible urban and rural households.

It has two components: **PMAY-Urban (PMAY-U)** for city dwellers and **PMAY-Gramin (PMAY-G)** for rural households, both using credit-linked subsidy and direct assistance models.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00446', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 7, 'What is the Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana?', '**Ujjwala Yojana**, launched in **May 2016** by the **Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas**, aims to provide **free LPG connections** to women from Below Poverty Line (BPL) households to replace polluting cooking fuels like firewood and reduce indoor air pollution.

**Ujjwala 2.0**, launched in 2021, extended free connections with an additional free refill and hotplate, targeting migrant families without a permanent address proof.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00447', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 8, 'What is Skill India / PMKVY and which ministry runs it?', '**Skill India Mission**, launched in **2015**, is implemented through flagship schemes like the **Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY)** under the **Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship (MSDE)**.

Its objective is to provide industry-relevant **skill training and certification** to youth, recognising prior learning and improving employability, in line with the National Skill Development Mission.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00448', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 9, 'What is the Digital India programme and what are its key pillars?', '**Digital India**, launched in **July 2015** by the **Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY)**, aims to transform India into a digitally empowered society and knowledge economy.

Its vision areas include **digital infrastructure as a utility**, **governance and services on demand**, and **digital empowerment of citizens**, covering initiatives like BharatNet, e-governance, and Digital Locker.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00449', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 10, 'What is the Make in India initiative?', '**Make in India**, launched in **September 2014** by the **Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT)**, aims to transform India into a **global manufacturing hub** by facilitating investment, fostering innovation, building world-class infrastructure, and easing doing business.

It originally identified **25 focus sectors** spanning manufacturing and services.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00450', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 11, 'What is the Atal Pension Yojana and who is eligible?', '**Atal Pension Yojana (APY)**, launched in **May 2015**, is a government-backed pension scheme administered by the **Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA)**, aimed primarily at workers in the **unorganised sector**.

Subscribers aged **18 to 40 years** contribute until age 60 to receive a guaranteed minimum monthly pension of **₹1,000 to ₹5,000**, with the government co-contributing for eligible early subscribers.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00451', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 12, 'What is the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY)?', '**PMFBY**, launched in **2016** by the **Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare**, is a crop insurance scheme providing financial support to farmers in case of crop failure due to natural calamities, pests, or diseases.

Farmers pay a **uniform low premium** (1.5% for Rabi, 2% for Kharif food/oilseed crops, 5% for commercial/horticultural crops), with the government bearing the balance premium.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00452', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 13, 'What employment guarantee does MGNREGA provide?', 'The **Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act**, originally enacted as **NREGA in 2005** and renamed MGNREGA in 2009, guarantees **100 days of wage employment per financial year** to every rural household whose adult members volunteer for unskilled manual work.

It is a **legal right**-based, demand-driven scheme administered by the **Ministry of Rural Development**, with wages linked to the Consumer Price Index.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00453', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 14, 'What does the National Food Security Act (NFSA), 2013 provide?', 'The **National Food Security Act, 2013** gives a **legal entitlement** to subsidised foodgrains through the Public Distribution System, covering up to **75% of the rural population** and **50% of the urban population**.

Eligible households receive foodgrains (rice, wheat, coarse grains) at highly subsidised prices under **Priority Households** and **Antyodaya Anna Yojana** categories, and the Act also addresses maternity entitlements and nutritional support for children.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00454', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 15, 'What is the Beti Bachao Beti Padhao scheme?', '**Beti Bachao Beti Padhao**, launched on **22 January 2015** at Panipat, Haryana, is a joint initiative of the **Ministry of Women and Child Development, Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, and Ministry of Education**.

Its objective is to address the declining **Child Sex Ratio** and promote the survival, protection, and education of the girl child through awareness and multi-sectoral action.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00455', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 16, 'What is the Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana?', '**Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana**, launched in **2015** under the Beti Bachao Beti Padhao umbrella, is a small savings scheme for the welfare of girl children.

Parents or guardians can open an account for a girl child **below 10 years**, with the account maturing after **21 years**, offering a government-set interest rate higher than regular small savings schemes, primarily to fund education and marriage expenses.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00456', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 17, 'What is the Jal Jeevan Mission and its target?', '**Jal Jeevan Mission**, launched on **15 August 2019** by the **Ministry of Jal Shakti**, aims to provide **safe and adequate drinking water through individual household tap connections (FHTC)** to every rural household in India.

It follows a decentralised, demand-driven approach with community participation in planning, implementation, and maintenance of local water infrastructure.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00457', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 18, 'What is the Atmanirbhar Bharat Abhiyan?', '**Atmanirbhar Bharat Abhiyan** (**Self-Reliant India Mission**) was announced in **May 2020** in response to the economic disruption caused by the COVID-19 pandemic.

It is built on five pillars — **economy, infrastructure, system, vibrant demography, and demand** — and emphasises reducing import dependence, boosting domestic manufacturing, and reforms across sectors including a large economic stimulus package.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00458', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 19, 'What are Production Linked Incentive (PLI) schemes?', '**PLI schemes**, introduced from **2020** as part of Atmanirbhar Bharat, offer **financial incentives to manufacturers based on incremental sales** of goods produced domestically, to boost domestic manufacturing and attract investment.

PLI schemes have been approved across **14 key sectors**, including mobile manufacturing and electronics, pharmaceuticals, textiles, automobiles and auto components, and solar PV modules.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00459', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 20, 'What is Startup India and when was it launched?', '**Startup India**, launched in **January 2016** by the **DPIIT**, aims to build a strong ecosystem for innovation and entrepreneurship, encouraging investment in the startup sector and generating employment.

Benefits for recognised startups include **tax exemptions**, self-certification under labour and environment laws, a simplified winding-up process, and access to the **Fund of Funds for Startups**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00460', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 21, 'What is the Stand Up India scheme?', '**Stand Up India**, launched in **April 2016**, facilitates bank loans between **₹10 lakh and ₹1 crore** to at least one **Scheduled Caste/Scheduled Tribe borrower** and at least one **woman borrower** per bank branch for setting up a greenfield enterprise.

It is aimed at promoting entrepreneurship among underrepresented groups in manufacturing, trading, or services.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00461', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 22, 'What is the Pradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana (PMMY)?', '**PMMY**, launched in **April 2015**, provides collateral-free loans up to **₹20 lakh** (revised from ₹10 lakh) to non-corporate, non-farm small and micro enterprises through the **Micro Units Development and Refinance Agency (MUDRA)**.

Loans are categorised under three brackets: **Shishu** (up to ₹50,000), **Kishor** (₹50,000 to ₹5 lakh), and **Tarun** (₹5 lakh to ₹10 lakh), with a higher **Tarun Plus** category added later.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00462', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 23, 'What is the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 and when was it approved?', '**NEP 2020** was approved by the Union Cabinet in **July 2020**, replacing the National Policy on Education of 1986, and is the first education policy of the 21st century.

Key features include a new **5+3+3+4 pedagogical structure** replacing the 10+2 system, emphasis on **foundational literacy and numeracy**, multiple entry-exit options in higher education, and a target of raising **public investment in education to 6% of GDP**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00463', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 24, 'What is PM POSHAN and how does it relate to the Mid-Day Meal Scheme?', '**PM POSHAN (PM Poshan Shakti Nirman)** is the **rebranded Mid-Day Meal Scheme** (originally launched in 1995), renamed in **2021** by the **Ministry of Education**.

It provides one hot cooked meal to children in government and government-aided schools from **Class 1 to Class 8**, aiming to improve nutritional levels and enhance school enrolment, retention, and attendance.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00464', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 25, 'What is the role of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI)?', 'The **RBI**, established on **1 April 1935** under the RBI Act, 1934 and nationalised in **1949**, is India''s central bank.

Its core functions include issuing currency, acting as **banker to the government and to banks**, regulating the money supply and credit through monetary policy, managing foreign exchange reserves under FEMA, and maintaining financial stability through banking regulation and supervision.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00465', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 26, 'What is the Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) and its mandate?', 'The **Monetary Policy Committee**, constituted under the **RBI Act, 1934** (amended in 2016), is a six-member body chaired by the **RBI Governor** responsible for fixing the **benchmark policy (repo) rate** to maintain price stability while keeping growth in mind.

It operates under a flexible **inflation-targeting framework**, currently mandated to keep **CPI inflation at 4%, with a tolerance band of +/- 2%**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00466', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 27, 'What is SEBI and when did it get statutory powers?', 'The **Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI)** was established in **1988** as a non-statutory body and given **statutory powers in 1992** under the **SEBI Act, 1992**.

It regulates the securities market in India, protects investor interests, and promotes the development of the capital market, overseeing stock exchanges, intermediaries, and listed companies.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00467', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 28, 'What is the headquarters and primary function of the International Monetary Fund (IMF)?', 'The **IMF**, headquartered in **Washington, D.C.**, was established in **1944** at the Bretton Woods Conference and began operations in 1945.

Its primary functions include promoting **international monetary cooperation**, exchange rate stability, and providing financial assistance (via quota-based resources) to member countries facing balance of payments difficulties.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00468', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 29, 'What is the World Trade Organization (WTO) and where is it headquartered?', 'The **WTO**, headquartered in **Geneva, Switzerland**, was established on **1 January 1995**, succeeding the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT).

It is the only global international organisation dealing with the **rules of trade between nations**, administering trade agreements, handling trade disputes, and monitoring national trade policies of its member countries.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00469', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 30, 'What is the headquarters and mandate of the World Health Organization (WHO)?', 'The **WHO**, headquartered in **Geneva, Switzerland**, was founded in **1948** as a specialised agency of the **United Nations**.

Its mandate is to direct and coordinate international health within the UN system, including disease surveillance, setting health norms and standards, and providing technical support to countries, such as during the COVID-19 pandemic response.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00470', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 31, 'What is the United Nations Security Council (UNSC) and its permanent members?', 'The **UNSC** is the principal organ of the UN responsible for maintaining **international peace and security**, with the power to impose sanctions and authorise the use of force.

It has **15 members**: **5 permanent members with veto power** — the **United States, United Kingdom, France, Russia, and China** — and **10 non-permanent members** elected for two-year terms by the UN General Assembly.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00471', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 32, 'What is G20 and when did India hold its presidency?', 'The **G20 (Group of Twenty)** is the premier forum for international economic cooperation, comprising 19 countries, the European Union, and the African Union, representing major advanced and emerging economies.

India held the **G20 Presidency from 1 December 2022 to 30 November 2023**, hosting the **leaders'' summit on 9–10 September 2023 in New Delhi** under the theme **"Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam — One Earth, One Family, One Future."**', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00472', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 33, 'What is the International Solar Alliance (ISA)?', 'The **International Solar Alliance**, launched jointly by **India and France at COP21 in Paris (2015)**, is a treaty-based international organisation to promote solar energy deployment among sun-rich countries.

Its headquarters is located in **Gurugram, Haryana**, within the campus of the **National Institute of Solar Energy**, and its framework agreement entered into force in **December 2017**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00473', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 34, 'What is the New Development Bank (NDB) and who established it?', 'The **New Development Bank**, established by the **BRICS nations (Brazil, Russia, India, China, South Africa)** at the 2014 Fortaleza Summit, began operations in **2015** and is headquartered in **Shanghai, China**.

It was created to mobilise resources for **infrastructure and sustainable development projects** in BRICS and other emerging economies, as an alternative to the World Bank and IMF.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00474', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 35, 'What is India''s Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC) target under the Paris Agreement?', 'India updated its **NDC** under the **Paris Agreement (2015)** to target reducing the **emissions intensity of GDP by 45% by 2030** (from 2005 levels) and achieving about **50% cumulative electric power installed capacity from non-fossil fuel sources by 2030**.

At **COP26 (Glasgow, 2021)**, India also announced a long-term goal of achieving **net-zero emissions by 2070**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00475', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 36, 'What is NITI Aayog and when was it formed?', '**NITI Aayog (National Institution for Transforming India)** was established on **1 January 2015** by a Cabinet resolution, replacing the 65-year-old **Planning Commission**.

Unlike the Planning Commission, NITI Aayog acts as a **policy think tank** following a bottom-up, cooperative federalism approach, and it does **not allocate plan funds** to states or prepare Five-Year Plans.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00476', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 37, 'What is the Finance Commission and its constitutional basis?', 'The **Finance Commission** is a constitutional body established under **Article 280** of the Constitution, constituted by the President every **five years** (or earlier if needed).

Its primary function is to recommend the **distribution of net tax proceeds between the Union and the States**, and among the states themselves, along with principles governing grants-in-aid to states.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00477', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 38, 'What is the Smart Cities Mission?', 'The **Smart Cities Mission**, launched in **June 2015** by the **Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs**, aims to develop **100 cities** with core infrastructure, clean and sustainable environment, and a decent quality of life through the application of smart solutions.

It is implemented through **Special Purpose Vehicles (SPVs)** set up for each selected city, focusing on area-based development and pan-city smart solutions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00478', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 39, 'What is AMRUT and its objective?', '**AMRUT (Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation)**, launched in **2015** by the **Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs**, focuses on providing basic urban infrastructure such as **water supply, sewerage, and green spaces** in identified cities.

**AMRUT 2.0**, launched in 2021, aims to make cities **"water secure"** and achieve universal coverage of water supply.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00479', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 40, 'What is the FAME India Scheme?', '**FAME India (Faster Adoption and Manufacturing of Hybrid and Electric Vehicles)**, launched in **2015** under the **National Electric Mobility Mission**, promotes the adoption of electric and hybrid vehicles through demand incentives and charging infrastructure support.

**FAME-II**, launched in 2019, focused incentives primarily on **electric buses, three-wheelers, and four-wheelers** used for public and commercial transport.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00480', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 41, 'What is Khelo India and its objective?', '**Khelo India**, launched in **2018** by the **Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports**, aims to promote a **sports culture at the grassroots level** across the country by reviving sports structures and identifying young talent.

It includes the annual **Khelo India Youth Games** and a scholarship scheme supporting talented athletes with financial assistance.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00481', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 42, 'What is the Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana - National Rural Livelihood Mission (DAY-NRLM)?', '**NRLM**, launched in **2011** by the **Ministry of Rural Development** (restructuring the earlier Swarnajayanti Gram Swarozgar Yojana) and renamed **DAY-NRLM in 2015**, aims to **reduce rural poverty** by organising poor households into **Self-Help Groups (SHGs)** and enabling access to financial services and sustainable livelihoods.

It is implemented with support from the **World Bank** and emphasises women''s **self-help group federations**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00482', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 43, 'What is e-NAM (National Agriculture Market)?', '**e-NAM**, launched in **April 2016** by the **Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare**, is a pan-India electronic trading portal that networks existing **Agricultural Produce Market Committee (APMC) mandis** to create a unified national market for agricultural commodities.

It aims to enable farmers to get **better price discovery** through online trading and reduce information asymmetry between buyers and sellers.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00483', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 44, 'What is the Soil Health Card Scheme?', 'The **Soil Health Card Scheme**, launched in **2015** by the **Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare**, provides farmers with information on the **nutrient status of their soil** along with recommendations on appropriate dosage of nutrients to improve soil health and fertility.

Cards are issued once every **two years**, enabling judicious use of fertilisers and reducing input costs.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00484', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 45, 'What is the Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY)?', '**PMKSY**, launched in **2015** by convergence of various irrigation-related schemes, aims to ensure **"Har Khet Ko Pani"** (water to every field) and improve water use efficiency through micro-irrigation under its **"Per Drop More Crop"** component.

It also covers watershed development and completion of ongoing major and medium irrigation projects.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00485', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 46, 'What is PM SVANidhi?', '**PM SVANidhi (PM Street Vendor''s AtmaNirbhar Nidhi)**, launched in **June 2020** by the **Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs**, provides collateral-free **working capital loans** to street vendors affected by the COVID-19 pandemic.

Vendors can initially avail a loan of up to **₹10,000**, with subsequent higher loan eligibility on timely repayment, along with an interest subsidy and cashback incentives for digital transactions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00486', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 47, 'What is the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM)?', '**ABDM**, launched nationwide in **September 2021** by the **Ministry of Health and Family Welfare** (after a pilot in 2020), aims to develop the backbone for an **integrated digital health infrastructure**.

It provides every citizen a unique **Ayushman Bharat Health Account (ABHA) number** to link and access their digital health records, along with registries for healthcare professionals and facilities.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00487', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 48, 'What is the Unified Payments Interface (UPI) and which body operates it?', '**UPI**, launched in **2016**, is a real-time payment system developed by the **National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI)** that enables instant inter-bank transactions through a mobile platform using a single application and virtual payment address.

NPCI is an umbrella organisation promoted by the **RBI and Indian Banks'' Association** for operating retail payment and settlement systems in India.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00488', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 49, 'What is the Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) scheme?', '**Direct Benefit Transfer**, launched in **January 2013** and significantly expanded after 2014, aims to transfer government subsidies and benefits **directly into beneficiaries'' bank accounts**, reducing leakages, delays, and duplication in welfare delivery.

It relies on the **JAM trinity (Jan Dhan accounts, Aadhaar, Mobile numbers)** and is used for schemes like LPG subsidy (PAHAL), scholarships, and pensions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00489', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 50, 'What is the GST Council and its constitutional basis?', 'The **GST Council**, established under **Article 279-A** of the Constitution (inserted by the 101st Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016), is a joint forum of the Centre and States chaired by the **Union Finance Minister**.

It makes recommendations on GST rates, exemptions, model laws, and administrative matters, with states having **two-thirds voting weight** and the Centre **one-third** in its decisions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00490', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 51, 'What is the Pradhan Mantri Vaya Vandana Yojana (PMVVY)?', '**PMVVY**, launched in **2017** and administered through the **Life Insurance Corporation (LIC)**, is a pension scheme exclusively for **senior citizens aged 60 and above**, guaranteeing a fixed rate of return on a lump-sum investment for a fixed tenure.

It aims to protect elderly persons against a future fall in interest rates, providing a regular pension payable monthly, quarterly, half-yearly, or annually.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00491', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 52, 'What is the Deendayal Upadhyaya Gram Jyoti Yojana (DDUGJY)?', '**DDUGJY**, launched in **2015** by the **Ministry of Power**, aims to provide continuous **electricity supply to rural areas** through feeder separation, strengthening sub-transmission infrastructure, and rural electrification.

It subsumed the earlier Rajiv Gandhi Grameen Vidyutikaran Yojana for last-mile rural electrification connectivity.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00492', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 53, 'What is the Saubhagya Scheme?', '**Saubhagya (Pradhan Mantri Sahaj Bijli Har Ghar Yojana)**, launched in **2017** by the **Ministry of Power**, aimed to achieve **universal household electrification** by providing free electricity connections to all remaining un-electrified households in rural and urban areas.

The government declared the completion of household electrification under the scheme''s target in **March 2019**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00493', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 54, 'What is the Integrated Child Development Services (ICDS) scheme?', '**ICDS**, launched in **1975**, is one of the world''s largest programmes for early childhood development, implemented through **Anganwadi Centres** under the **Ministry of Women and Child Development**.

It provides a package of services — supplementary nutrition, immunisation, health check-ups, referral services, pre-school non-formal education, and nutrition/health education — targeting children below 6 years, pregnant women, and lactating mothers.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00494', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 55, 'What is the National Clean Air Programme (NCAP)?', '**NCAP**, launched in **January 2019** by the **Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change**, is a national-level strategy to tackle air pollution with targets to reduce **particulate matter (PM2.5 and PM10) concentrations**.

It originally targeted a **20-30% reduction in PM concentration by 2024** (base year 2017) across identified non-attainment cities, later revised to a 40% reduction target by 2025-26.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00495', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 56, 'What is the Fit India Movement?', 'The **Fit India Movement**, launched on **29 August 2019** (National Sports Day) by the **Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports**, is a nationwide campaign to encourage citizens to incorporate **physical activity and sports** into their daily lives.

It seeks to address lifestyle-related health issues and promote fitness as an integral part of everyday living across age groups.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00496', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 57, 'What is the objective and funding pattern of PM Gati Shakti?', '**PM Gati Shakti National Master Plan**, launched in **October 2021**, is a digital platform integrating infrastructure planning across **16 ministries** (including Railways and Roadways) to ensure coordinated, multi-modal connectivity for projects.

Its objective is to reduce logistics costs, cut project implementation delays caused by lack of coordination, and support integrated planning for **economic zones** like textile and industrial clusters.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00497', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 58, 'What is the One Nation One Ration Card scheme?', '**One Nation One Ration Card (ONORC)**, rolled out nationally from **2019-2020** by the **Department of Food and Public Distribution**, allows beneficiaries under the **National Food Security Act** to access their entitled subsidised foodgrains from **any Fair Price Shop in the country**, regardless of which state issued their ration card.

It particularly benefits **migrant workers** by ensuring food security portability across state lines.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00498', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 59, 'What is Mission Indradhanush?', '**Mission Indradhanush**, launched in **December 2014** by the **Ministry of Health and Family Welfare**, aims to achieve **full immunisation coverage** for all children under 2 years and pregnant women against **vaccine-preventable diseases**.

Its intensified version, **Intensified Mission Indradhanush (IMI)**, was launched in 2017 to accelerate progress in districts and blocks with low immunisation coverage.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00499', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 60, 'What is the Pradhan Mantri Garib Kalyan Anna Yojana (PMGKAY)?', '**PMGKAY**, launched in **March/April 2020** in response to the COVID-19 pandemic, provided **free additional foodgrains** (5 kg per person per month) to NFSA beneficiaries, over and above their regular entitlement under the Public Distribution System.

The scheme was extended multiple times and was subsequently merged/integrated with the regular NFSA foodgrain supply from January 2023 as a unified free-foodgrain scheme.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('upsc_gs-q00500', 'upsc-gs-bank', 'Government Schemes & Current Affairs', 7, 61, 'What is the mandate of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Board of India (IBBI)?', 'The **IBBI**, established in **2016** under the **Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC), 2016**, is the regulator overseeing insolvency proceedings and entities like **Insolvency Professionals, Insolvency Professional Agencies, and Information Utilities** in India.

It was created to implement a **time-bound resolution process** for corporate insolvency, consolidating earlier fragmented laws dealing with debt recovery and winding up of companies.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

